window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD && window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD("0120", [{"word":"water cycle","ipa_uk":"/ˈwɔːtə ˌsaɪkl/","ipa_us":"/ˈwɔːtər ˌsaɪkl/","definition_zh":"水循环；水在海洋、大气与陆地之间蒸发、凝结、降水、径流并回归的往复过程","definition_en":"the continuous circulation of water between ocean, atmosphere and land through evaporation, condensation, precipitation and runoff","core_image":"一滴水从海面被太阳抬上天空，凝成云，落回山脊，顺河归海，再被抬起，画出一个闭合的圈","scene":"地理课的玻璃箱里，灯照着水面，水汽升到顶盖凝成细珠，随后一滴滴落回箱底。In the classroom tank, the water cycle repeats as vapour rises, condenses on the lid and falls back.","sceneCN":"这里 water cycle 指「水在海洋、大气与陆地之间往复的完整回路」（第 1 个义项：以蒸发、凝结、降水与径流为环节的闭环过程）；句意为课堂演示箱中水汽上升、在顶盖凝结、又落回原处，这一回路反复出现。可辨识物件：玻璃箱、台灯、水面、顶盖雾珠、下落水滴。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"水循环；水文循环（不可数，指自然界水的往复过程）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"global water cycle","zh":"全球水循环"},{"phrase":"water cycle diagram","zh":"水循环示意图"},{"phrase":"accelerated water cycle","zh":"加快的水循环"},{"phrase":"water cycle model","zh":"水循环模型"},{"phrase":"disrupt the water cycle","zh":"扰乱水循环"}],"forms":[{"label":"通常形式（不可数，指过程）","form":"water cycle"},{"label":"复数（指多个回路或多次循环）","form":"water cycles"},{"label":"同义术语（学术）","form":"hydrological cycle"},{"label":"相关形容词","form":"hydrological"},{"label":"相关名词（学科）","form":"hydrology"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"hydrological","pos":"adj.","zh":"水文的；水循环的"},{"word":"hydrology","pos":"n.","zh":"水文学；水文科学"},{"word":"hydrologic","pos":"adj.","zh":"水文的（美式拼写常见）"},{"word":"water-cycle","pos":"adj.","zh":"水循环的（作定语，如 water-cycle model）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Evaporation lifts water","titleCN":"蒸发：水离开水面升入空中","definition":"the step in which surface water changes into vapour and rises into the air","definitionCN":"表层水变成水汽并升入空中的环节","example":"Sunlight on the lake drives evaporation, the first step of the cycle.","exampleCN":"阳光照在湖面上促成蒸发，这是循环的第一步。","why":"The loop has to start somewhere, and it starts at the boundary between liquid and air, where heat gives molecules enough energy to escape the surface.","whyCN":"这个回路总要有一个起点，而起点就在水与大气的交界处：热量给了水分子足够的能量，让它们脱离水面。"},{"no":"02","title":"Condensation builds cloud","titleCN":"凝结：水汽在冷空气中聚成云","definition":"the step in which rising vapour cools and turns into tiny droplets that form clouds","definitionCN":"上升的水汽遇冷变成微小水滴并聚成云的环节","example":"The vapour cools as it rises, and condensation turns it into cloud.","exampleCN":"水汽上升时冷却，凝结作用把它变成云。","why":"What goes up must cool: air expands with height, loses heat, and can no longer hold the same amount of vapour, so the excess returns to droplets.","whyCN":"上升的东西必然变冷：空气随高度膨胀、失热，再也容纳不下同样多的水汽，多出的部分就重新变回小水滴。"},{"no":"03","title":"Precipitation returns water","titleCN":"降水：云中的水重新落回地面","definition":"the step in which droplets grow heavy enough to fall as rain, snow or hail","definitionCN":"水滴增大到足够重时以雨、雪或冰雹落回地面的环节","example":"Precipitation over the mountains feeds every stream below.","exampleCN":"山上的降水补给山下的每一条溪流。","why":"A cloud is only a temporary holding place; once droplets merge and grow, gravity takes over and the water leaves the air.","whyCN":"云只是暂时的存放处；一旦水滴合并变大，重力接管，水就离开大气落下来。"},{"no":"04","title":"Runoff and rivers","titleCN":"径流：水沿地表汇入河流","definition":"the step in which water flows over the land surface into streams and rivers and back toward the sea","definitionCN":"水沿陆地表层流入溪流、河流并归海的环节","example":"Runoff carries the storm water down to the river within hours.","exampleCN":"径流在几小时内就把暴雨的水送到河里。","why":"Falling water seeks the lowest path. The land slopes, so the same water that fell on the ridge is delivered to the sea by gravity, not by pumps.","whyCN":"落下的水会寻找最低处。地面有坡度，于是落在山脊上的水靠重力而非水泵被送到海里。"},{"no":"05","title":"Infiltration into the ground","titleCN":"下渗：水渗入土壤与岩层","definition":"the step in which part of the water sinks into soil and rock instead of running off","definitionCN":"部分水不流走而渗入土壤与岩石的环节","example":"Sandy soil allows deep infiltration, so less water reaches the stream.","exampleCN":"沙质土壤下渗很深，因此到达溪流的水更少。","why":"The loop has two return roads: the surface road and the underground road. Infiltration is where the water chooses the second one.","whyCN":"这个回路有两条归路：地表之路与地下之路。下渗就是水选择第二条路的地方。"},{"no":"06","title":"A balanced budget","titleCN":"水量平衡：收入与支出相抵","definition":"the accounting view in which precipitation equals evaporation, runoff and storage change combined","definitionCN":"把降水与蒸发、径流和蓄量变化相加后相抵的核算视角","example":"Over a year, the basin's water cycle must balance its inputs and outputs.","exampleCN":"一年之内，流域的水循环必须让输入与输出相抵。","why":"Because the loop is closed, nothing can be added or lost overall; every drop that arrives must be accounted for somewhere.","whyCN":"因为回路是闭合的，总体上既不能增加也不能丢失；每一滴到来的水都必须在某处被记账。"},{"no":"07","title":"The textbook diagram","titleCN":"教材模型：带箭头的示意图","definition":"the simplified teaching model with labelled arrows showing each transfer","definitionCN":"用带标注的箭头显示每一段转移的简化教学模型","example":"The exam asked students to label the water cycle from memory.","exampleCN":"考试要求学生凭记忆给水循环图标注。","why":"A real cycle is invisible and planetary in scale, so teaching replaces it with a small set of arrows that can be drawn on one page.","whyCN":"真实的水循环看不见，而且有行星尺度，所以教学用一个能画在一页纸上的箭头集合来代替它。"},{"no":"08","title":"Abstract: any repeated circulation","titleCN":"比喻：任何反复的流转","definition":"any resource or influence that keeps returning through the same set of stages","definitionCN":"任何沿同一组环节不断返回的资源或影响","example":"Fashion runs on its own water cycle of revival and decay.","exampleCN":"时尚有它自己的一套兴衰流转。","why":"Once a closed loop of stages is named after water, the name can be lent to money, ideas or styles that also come back around.","whyCN":"一旦一套闭合的环节以水命名，这个名字就可以借给同样会绕回来的金钱、观念或风格。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Water is a native Old English word; cycle came from Greek through Latin. The compound is an English scientific description, not a borrowed phrase. Dates are approximate.","cn":"water 是古英语本族词；cycle 经拉丁语来自希腊语。这个复合词是英语的科学描述，不是借来的短语。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"OLD ENGLISH WÆTER","en":"Old English wæter 'water' continues Proto-Germanic *watōr, and Greek hydōr 'water' is a cognate from the same Indo-European root.","cn":"古英语 wæter「水」延续原始日耳曼语 *watōr，希腊语 hydōr「水」同出这一印欧词根。"},{"era":"GREEK KYKLOS","en":"Greek kyklos meant circle, wheel or turning; Latin borrowed it as cyclus, and English took the Latin form in the fourteenth century with the sense of a recurring round.","cn":"希腊语 kyklos 指圆圈、车轮或转动；拉丁语借作 cyclus，英语在十四世纪引入这一拉丁形式，义为反复的一轮。"},{"era":"TWO WORDS JOINED","en":"Natural philosophers of the seventeenth and eighteenth centuries described water as circulating between sea, air and land, and the two-word label followed from that description.","cn":"十七、十八世纪的自然哲学家用「循环」描述水在海、气、陆之间的往复，这个双词名称就由此而来。"},{"era":"HYDROLOGIC CYCLE","en":"The technical synonyms hydrologic cycle and hydrological cycle were built later from Greek hydōr plus logos, and both remain standard in hydrology.","cn":"技术同义词 hydrologic cycle 与 hydrological cycle 后来由希腊语 hydōr 加 logos 构成，两者至今都是水文学的标准说法。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first attestation and root shape): no dictionary fixes the first written use of the exact phrase water cycle; the Indo-European root is a reconstruction usually written *wed-, and the competing form *wod- is another reconstruction, not a proven variant.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代与词根形态）：没有辞书能确定 water cycle 这一确切短语的首次书面使用；其印欧词根属重构形式，通常写作 *wed-，另有 *wod- 一说，同样只是重构，并非已证实的变体。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group holds phrases that name neighbouring parts of the same system; the second group holds terms that are close in meaning but are not the whole loop.","cn":"第一组是命名同一系统中相邻环节的短语；第二组是意思相近但并不等于整个回路的术语。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"hydrological cycle","ipa":"/haɪˈdrɒl.ə.dʒɪ.kəl ˈsaɪkl/","tag":"technical synonym","definition":"The same loop named from the science of hydrology rather than from the substance water.","definitionCN":"同一个回路，只是从水文学科而不是从水本身命名。"},{"word":"water budget","ipa":"/ˈwɔːtə ˌbʌdʒɪt/","tag":"the accounting side","definition":"The balance sheet of inputs and outputs within the cycle, not the cycle itself.","definitionCN":"循环内部的收支账，而不是循环本身。"},{"word":"watershed","ipa":"/ˈwɔːtəʃed/","tag":"the container","definition":"The area that collects the water; the cycle is the movement inside it.","definitionCN":"收集水的区域；循环是在这个区域内发生的运动。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"circulation","ipa":"/ˌsɜː.kjəˈleɪ.ʃən/","tag":"the general shape","definition":"Any repeated going-round; the water cycle is one instance of circulation in nature.","definitionCN":"任何反复绕行；水循环是自然界中循环的一个实例。"},{"word":"water flow","ipa":"/ˈwɔːtə fləʊ/","tag":"one-way motion","definition":"Movement of water in one direction only, without the return that makes a cycle.","definitionCN":"水只朝一个方向流动，没有构成循环的回程。"},{"word":"evaporation","ipa":"/ɪˌvæp.əˈreɪ.ʃən/","tag":"one stage","definition":"Only the lifting stage; the cycle requires condensation, precipitation and return as well.","definitionCN":"只是上升那一段；循环还需要凝结、降水与回归。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: the two real roots, the four named stages and the diagram students actually draw.","cn":"正常联想：两个真实词根、四个有名字的阶段，以及学生真正会画的那张图。"},"normal":[{"en":"cycle is from Greek kyklos, a wheel: a wheel returns to the point where it started.","cn":"cycle 出自希腊语 kyklos「车轮」：轮子转一圈会回到起点。"},{"en":"The four textbook labels are evaporation, condensation, precipitation and runoff, in that order.","cn":"教材上的四个标签依次是蒸发、凝结、降水、径流。"},{"en":"hydrological adds Greek hydōr, water, to logos, study: hydrology is the study of water's behaviour.","cn":"hydrological 是希腊语 hydōr「水」加 logos「研究」：水文学就是研究水的行为。"},{"en":"The loop has two return roads: over the land and under it.","cn":"这个回路有两条归路：一条在地面之上，一条在地面之下。"},{"en":"The accounting rule is simple: what falls must equal what leaves plus what is stored.","cn":"记账规则很简单：落下的量等于离开的量加上储存的量。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Abstractly, the cycle is a closed path with no ends: every exit is also an entrance.","cn":"抽象地看，这个循环是一条没有端点的闭合路径：每个出口同时也是一个入口。"},{"en":"It is also an energy story: sunlight lifts, gravity returns. Two forces drive one loop.","cn":"它也是一个能量故事：太阳负责抬起，重力负责送回。两种力驱动同一个回路。"},{"en":"Any system that must keep its accounts balanced and reuse the same material can be drawn with this loop.","cn":"任何必须保持收支平衡并重复使用同一材料的系统，都可以用这个回路来画。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Deforestation can change the local water cycle and reduce rainfall.","cn":"砍伐森林会改变局地水循环并减少降雨。"},{"en":"The water cycle has no beginning and no end, so the arrows in the diagram can start anywhere.","cn":"水循环没有起点也没有终点，所以示意图的箭头从哪一段开始画都可以。"},{"en":"Warmer air speeds up the water cycle, making both floods and droughts more likely.","cn":"更暖的空气加快水循环，使洪水和干旱都更容易发生。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「水（water）+ 圆圈（cycle）」——水在天上地下绕圈走，一圈接一圈 → 水循环","word":"water cycle"},"root":"古英语 wæter「水」+ 希腊语 kyklos「圆圈、转动」（经拉丁语 cyclus 进入英语）。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one loop: water leaves the surface, becomes cloud, falls, and returns by two roads, then the loop itself is counted, drawn and borrowed as a metaphor.","cn":"八个义项沿同一个回路展开：水离开水面、变成云、落下来、沿两条路返回，随后这个回路本身被核算、被画成图，并被借作比喻。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: ocean → vapour → cloud → rain → land → ocean, a closed wheel of water.","cn":"核心意象：海洋 → 水汽 → 云 → 雨 → 陆地 → 海洋，一个闭合的水之轮。"},"chain":["SURFACE WATER","VAPOUR","CLOUD","FALLING WATER","LAND ROUTE","RETURN TO OCEAN"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S2","en":"LIFTING AND COOLING: heat takes water up, cold air turns it back into droplets.","cn":"抬升与冷却：热量把水送上去，冷空气把它变回水滴。"},{"senses":"S3","en":"THE DROP: what the air can no longer hold comes down as weather.","cn":"落下的那一滴：空气再也托不住的水以天气的形式落下。"},{"senses":"S4 · S5","en":"TWO RETURN ROADS: across the surface into rivers, or down into rock.","cn":"两条归路：或沿地表汇入河流，或向下进入岩层。"},{"senses":"S6","en":"BALANCE: the closed loop can be audited as a budget of inputs and outputs.","cn":"平衡：这个闭合回路可以当作收支账来核算。"},{"senses":"S7 · S8","en":"MODEL AND METAPHOR: the arrows teach the loop, and any returning circulation borrows its name.","cn":"模型与比喻：箭头把回路教给人，而任何会返回的循环都借用它的名字。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Water cycle is a native-English compound with one Greek-derived member, so its pieces are readable: the substance plus a word for a round.","cn":"water cycle 是以英语本族词为主、含一个希腊来源成分的复合词，因此可以逐块读出：物质加「一圈」。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"There is no Latin root for water here; the Latin element is cyclus, which Rome itself borrowed from Greek kyklos. Latin has its own circulus for a ring, a different formation, so it is not listed as a cognate.","cn":"这里没有表示水的拉丁词根；拉丁成分是 cyclus，而这个词是罗马自己从希腊语 kyklos 借来的。拉丁语另有表示圆环的 circulus，构词来源不同，因此不作为同源词列出。"},"items":[{"word":"water","structure":"water (Old English wæter, native word for the liquid)","meaning":"the liquid itself; the substance that moves round","meaningCN":"水本身；循环中移动的物质","example":"Water covers most of the planet's surface.","exampleCN":"水覆盖了这颗行星的大部分表面。"},{"word":"cycle","structure":"cycle (Greek kyklos, circle, via Latin cyclus)","meaning":"a round that returns to its start","meaningCN":"回到起点的一轮","example":"The seasons form a yearly cycle.","exampleCN":"四季构成一年的循环。"},{"word":"hydrology","structure":"hydro- (Greek hydōr, water) + -logy (Greek logos, study)","meaning":"the science of water on and under the earth","meaningCN":"研究地表与地下水的科学","example":"Hydrology models how rain reaches rivers.","exampleCN":"水文学模拟降雨如何到达河流。"},{"word":"hydrological","structure":"hydrology + -ical (relating to)","meaning":"relating to the study or behaviour of water","meaningCN":"与水的研究或行为有关的","example":"The map shows hydrological boundaries.","exampleCN":"这张图显示水文边界。"},{"word":"hydrosphere","structure":"hydro- (water) + sphere (Greek sphaira, ball)","meaning":"all the water of the planet taken as one layer","meaningCN":"把行星上全部水当作一个圈层","example":"The hydrosphere exchanges heat with the atmosphere.","exampleCN":"水圈与大气交换热量。"},{"word":"evaporation","structure":"e- (out) + vapor (steam) + -ation (process)","meaning":"the change from liquid to vapour","meaningCN":"由液态变为水汽的过程","example":"Evaporation from the sea feeds every cloud.","exampleCN":"海面的蒸发供养每一朵云。"},{"word":"condensation","structure":"con- (together) + dens- (thick) + -ation (process)","meaning":"the change from vapour back to droplets","meaningCN":"由水汽变回小水滴的过程","example":"Condensation on the cold glass formed drops.","exampleCN":"冷玻璃上的凝结形成了水滴。"},{"word":"precipitation","structure":"pre- (before, down) + capit- (head) + -ation (process)","meaning":"water falling from clouds as rain, snow or hail","meaningCN":"水以雨、雪或冰雹的形式从云中落下","example":"Annual precipitation in the valley is low.","exampleCN":"这个谷地的年降水量很低。"},{"word":"runoff","structure":"run + off (verb phrase turned noun)","meaning":"water that flows away over the ground","meaningCN":"沿地面流走的水","example":"Paved streets increase runoff.","exampleCN":"铺了路面的街道会增大径流。"},{"word":"watershed","structure":"water + shed (a divide that separates)","meaning":"the ridge that divides two drainage areas","meaningCN":"分开两个汇水区的分水岭","example":"The watershed sends rain to two different rivers.","exampleCN":"分水岭把雨水送往两条不同的河。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"cyclus","structure":"cyclus (Latin, borrowed from Greek kyklos, circle)","meaning":"a circle, a recurring round","meaningCN":"圆圈；反复的一轮"}]}},{"word":"hydrological cycle","ipa_uk":"/haɪˈdrɒl.ə.dʒɪ.kəl ˈsaɪkl/","ipa_us":"/haɪˈdrɑː.lə.dʒɪ.kəl ˈsaɪkl/","definition_zh":"水文循环；以水文学术语表述的水在陆地、海洋与大气间的往复过程","definition_en":"the continuous circulation of water through evaporation, atmospheric transport, precipitation, storage and runoff, viewed as a subject of hydrology","core_image":"一张流域剖面图上，雨水从云层落下，一部分入河，一部分下渗，箭头最终回到海洋与云","scene":"水文站的剖面图上，雨线从云里落到山坡，一部分汇入河道，一部分钻进土层。On the hydrologist's cross-section, the hydrological cycle is drawn as arrows from cloud to slope, river and sea.","sceneCN":"这里 hydrological cycle 指「从水文学角度描述的水在陆地、海洋与大气间的往复」（第 1 个义项：把蒸发、输送、降水、蓄存与径流作为整体研究的水文过程）；句意为在水文工作者的剖面上，这一循环被画成从云到山坡、河流再回到海洋的箭头。可辨识物件：剖面图、云、山坡、河道、下渗箭头。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"水文循环；水循环（学术用语，不可数）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"global hydrological cycle","zh":"全球水文循环"},{"phrase":"hydrological cycle model","zh":"水文循环模型"},{"phrase":"alter the hydrological cycle","zh":"改变水文循环"},{"phrase":"hydrological cycle intensity","zh":"水文循环强度"},{"phrase":"hydrological cycle observation","zh":"水文循环观测"}],"forms":[{"label":"通常形式（不可数）","form":"hydrological cycle"},{"label":"复数（指多个流域或多次循环）","form":"hydrological cycles"},{"label":"美式同义术语","form":"hydrologic cycle"},{"label":"通俗同义术语","form":"water cycle"},{"label":"相关学科名词","form":"hydrology"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"hydrology","pos":"n.","zh":"水文学"},{"word":"hydrologist","pos":"n.","zh":"水文工作者；水文学家"},{"word":"hydrologic","pos":"adj.","zh":"水文的（美式拼写）"},{"word":"hydrograph","pos":"n.","zh":"水位（或流量）过程线；水文图"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The whole cycle as a subject","titleCN":"作为研究对象的完整循环","definition":"the complete set of water transfers treated as one system by hydrology","definitionCN":"水文学把全部水的转移当作一个系统来处理的整体","example":"The course begins with the hydrological cycle as a single system.","exampleCN":"这门课先把水文循环当作一个系统来讲。","why":"Hydrology needs a name for the object it studies, and that object is not one river or one rainstorm but the whole set of transfers linked into a loop.","whyCN":"水文学需要给它研究的对象一个名字，而这个对象不是某条河或某场暴雨，而是连成回路的整套转移。"},{"no":"02","title":"Evaporation and transpiration","titleCN":"蒸发与蒸腾：水离开水面和植物","definition":"the upward loss of water from open water, soil and plant leaves","definitionCN":"水从开阔水面、土壤与植物叶片向上散失的部分","example":"In summer, evaporation and transpiration dominate the cycle's upward arm.","exampleCN":"夏季，蒸发与蒸腾主导循环的上升分支。","why":"Plants are part of the loop, not bystanders: they pull water from soil and release it through leaves, so the upward arm has two sources.","whyCN":"植物是回路的一部分而非旁观者：它们从土壤吸水、经叶片释放，因此上升分支有两个来源。"},{"no":"03","title":"Atmospheric transport","titleCN":"大气输送：水汽从一个地方移到另一个地方","definition":"the movement of vapour by winds from where it evaporated to where it will fall","definitionCN":"水汽被风从其蒸发地移动到其将降落之处的过程","example":"Atmospheric transport carries ocean vapour hundreds of kilometres inland.","exampleCN":"大气输送把海洋水汽带到内陆数百公里处。","why":"The loop is not local: the place that loses water and the place that receives it are usually far apart, and wind is the link.","whyCN":"这个回路不是局地的：失水的地方与得水的地方通常相距很远，风就是中间的连接。"},{"no":"04","title":"Precipitation over a basin","titleCN":"流域降水：水回到地面","definition":"the return of water to the land or sea surface as rain, snow or hail","definitionCN":"水以雨、雪或冰雹形式回到陆地或海面的部分","example":"Precipitation over the basin is measured at a network of gauges.","exampleCN":"流域内的降水由一组雨量计测量。","why":"For a hydrologist, rain is an input term in an equation, so it must be measured rather than merely observed.","whyCN":"对水文工作者来说，降雨是方程里的一个输入项，因此必须测量，而不只是「看到下雨」。"},{"no":"05","title":"Storage in soil and rock","titleCN":"蓄存：水停留在土壤与岩层中","definition":"water held temporarily in soil moisture, aquifers, lakes, snow and ice","definitionCN":"暂存于土壤水、含水层、湖泊、积雪与冰中的水","example":"Storage delays the cycle: water may stay underground for decades.","exampleCN":"蓄存使循环发生延迟：水可能在地下停留数十年。","why":"Not every drop moves at the same speed. Storage is the memory of the cycle, and it explains why a dry year can be followed by a wet one.","whyCN":"并非每一滴水都以同样速度移动。蓄存是这个循环的记忆，也解释了为什么旱年之后可能跟着一个湿年。"},{"no":"06","title":"Runoff and discharge","titleCN":"径流与排泄：水离开流域","definition":"the water that leaves a basin through streams, rivers and groundwater outflow","definitionCN":"经溪流、河流与地下水流出离开流域的水","example":"Discharge at the gauge is the basin's runoff term.","exampleCN":"测站测到的流量就是流域的径流项。","why":"Every basin has an exit, and what passes that exit is what the upstream area failed to store or evaporate.","whyCN":"每个流域都有一个出口，通过出口的水就是上游地区没能蓄住或蒸发的部分。"},{"no":"07","title":"The basin-scale balance","titleCN":"流域尺度平衡：把各项写成方程","definition":"the equation in which precipitation equals evaporation, runoff and change in storage","definitionCN":"把降水与蒸发、径流和蓄量变化相等的方程","example":"The basin-scale balance closed to within five per cent last year.","exampleCN":"去年流域尺度的收支平衡误差在百分之五以内。","why":"Once every transfer has a name, the loop can be written as an equation, and an equation is what makes prediction possible.","whyCN":"一旦每种转移都有了名字，这个回路就能写成一个方程，而方程正是预测成为可能的原因。"},{"no":"08","title":"The intensified cycle","titleCN":"加强的循环：变暖下的加速","definition":"the observed speeding-up of water transfers as the atmosphere warms","definitionCN":"大气变暖后被观测到的水的转移加快","example":"A warmer atmosphere intensifies the hydrological cycle, with heavier bursts and longer dry spells.","exampleCN":"更暖的大气加强水文循环，带来更强的暴雨和更长的干旱期。","why":"Warm air holds more vapour, so the same loop can carry more water per round; the stages do not change, only their speed and size.","whyCN":"暖空气能容纳更多水汽，因此同一个回路每一轮能搬运更多水；环节不变，只是速度和规模变了。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"The phrase is Greek in its technical parts and English in its grammar: hydōr supplies the water, logos supplies the study, and cycle supplies the round. Dates are approximate.","cn":"这个短语的技术成分来自希腊语，语法外壳是英语：hydōr 提供「水」，logos 提供「研究」，cycle 提供「一圈」。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK HYDŌR","en":"Greek hydōr, genitive hydatos, meant water; English uses the combining form hydro- or hydr-, as in hydrology and hydroelectric.","cn":"希腊语 hydōr（属格 hydatos）意为水；英语使用组合形式 hydro- 或 hydr-，如 hydrology 与 hydroelectric。"},{"era":"GREEK LOGOS","en":"Logos meant word, account or reasoned study; the suffix -logia produced names of sciences, and English -logy followed that pattern.","cn":"logos 指言词、账目或有条理的研究；后缀 -logia 用来构成学科名称，英语 -logy 沿用了这一模式。"},{"era":"HYDROLOGY","en":"Hydrology, the study of water on the earth, is recorded in English from the seventeenth century, and hydrological is its adjective.","cn":"hydrology 指研究地球上水的学问，英语自十七世纪起有记载，hydrological 是它的形容词。"},{"era":"THE PHRASE","en":"The full phrase hydrological cycle belongs to twentieth-century technical English, when water budgets came to be taught as a single circulating system.","cn":"完整的 hydrological cycle 属于二十世纪技术英语，当时水量收支开始被当作一个循环系统来教授。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first attestation): the exact year and author of the first printed use of hydrological cycle cannot be fixed from standard references, so the dating here is a general estimate.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：hydrological cycle 首次印刷使用的确切年份与作者无法由通行资料确定，此处年代只是一般估计。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group holds terms built from the same Greek material; the second holds terms that describe parts or neighbours of the same system.","cn":"第一组是由同一批希腊语材料构成的术语；第二组是描述同一系统局部或邻近概念的术语。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"hydrologic cycle","ipa":"/ˌhaɪ.drəˈlɒdʒ.ɪk ˈsaɪkl/","tag":"American spelling","definition":"The same term with the shorter American adjective; the meaning is identical.","definitionCN":"同一术语的美式短形容词形式，含义完全相同。"},{"word":"water cycle","ipa":"/ˈwɔːtə ˌsaɪkl/","tag":"plain-language synonym","definition":"The everyday name for the same loop, used in schools rather than in journals.","definitionCN":"同一回路的日常名称，多用于学校而非期刊。"},{"word":"hydrological model","ipa":"/haɪˈdrɒl.ə.dʒɪ.kəl ˈmɒdl/","tag":"the tool, not the object","definition":"A computer representation of the cycle; the cycle is what the model tries to imitate.","definitionCN":"循环的计算机表示；循环才是模型试图模仿的对象。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"water budget","ipa":"/ˈwɔːtə ˌbʌdʒɪt/","tag":"the accounting view","definition":"The same transfers written as income and outgo, with no emphasis on motion.","definitionCN":"把同样的转移写成收入与支出，不强调运动本身。"},{"word":"catchment hydrology","ipa":"/ˈkætʃ.mənt haɪˈdrɒl.ə.dʒi/","tag":"one scale","definition":"The study of the cycle within one catchment, a part rather than the whole.","definitionCN":"研究一个集水区内的循环，是整体的一部分。"},{"word":"circulation","ipa":"/ˌsɜː.kjəˈleɪ.ʃən/","tag":"general term","definition":"Any closed repeated movement; the hydrological cycle is the water case of it.","definitionCN":"任何闭合的重复运动；水文循环是它在水的方面的实例。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: the Greek pieces, the paired adjective, and the two arms hydrologists actually measure.","cn":"正常联想：希腊语构件、成对的形容词，以及水文工作者真正测量的两条分支。"},"normal":[{"en":"hydro- is Greek for water, so hydrology is literally 'water study'.","cn":"hydro- 在希腊语中就是水，所以 hydrology 字面就是「水的学问」。"},{"en":"-logy names a science, as in biology, geology and climatology.","cn":"-logy 用来命名学科，如生物学、地质学与气候学。"},{"en":"The American form drops the -logical ending to -logic: hydrologic cycle.","cn":"美式形式把 -logical 缩为 -logic，成为 hydrologic cycle。"},{"en":"Two arms are measured: the upward arm (evaporation plus transpiration) and the downward arm (precipitation).","cn":"被测量的是两条分支：上升分支（蒸发加蒸腾）与下降分支（降水）。"},{"en":"A basin closes its accounts: input equals output plus storage change.","cn":"一个流域要平账：输入等于输出加蓄量变化。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Abstractly, the phrase is a machine with no off switch: the same water is reassigned to a new stage forever.","cn":"抽象地看，这个短语是一台没有开关的机器：同一批水永远被重新分配到下一个环节。"},{"en":"It is also a memory system: storage is what lets one season pay for another.","cn":"它也是一个记忆系统：蓄存让一个季节为另一个季节买单。"},{"en":"Speed is the only variable: warming does not add stages, it only shortens the time each stage takes.","cn":"速度是唯一的变量：变暖不增添环节，只是缩短每个环节所占的时间。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Hydrologists treat the hydrological cycle as a set of linked reservoirs and fluxes.","cn":"水文工作者把水文循环当作一组相连的储库与通量。"},{"en":"Urbanisation changes the hydrological cycle by replacing soil with concrete.","cn":"城市化用混凝土取代土壤，从而改变水文循环。"},{"en":"The hydrological cycle of a small catchment can be modelled in a few equations.","cn":"一个小集水区的水文循环可以用几个方程来模拟。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「海卓逻辑（hydro-logic）+ 圈」——用水文的逻辑把水的一圈算清楚 → 水文循环","word":"hydrological cycle"},"root":"希腊语 hydōr「水」+ logos「言说、研究」+ kyklos「圆圈」，经拉丁语进入英语，二十世纪构成专业术语。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow the same loop as hydrology sees it: the whole system, its upward arm, its transport, its fall, its storage, its exit, its balance, and its recent speed-up.","cn":"八个义项沿水文学所见的同一回路展开：整体系统、上升分支、输送、降落、蓄存、出口、收支平衡，以及近年来的加速。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a cross-section with arrows — cloud, slope, river, rock, sea, and back to cloud.","cn":"核心意象：一张带箭头的剖面图——云、山坡、河流、岩层、海洋，再回到云。"},"chain":["WATER SOURCE","UPWARD ARM","ATMOSPHERIC LINK","RETURN","STORAGE","DISCHARGE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1","en":"WHOLE SYSTEM: the term names the object hydrology studies before it names any part.","cn":"整体系统：这个术语先命名水文学研究的对象，再命名其中任何局部。"},{"senses":"S2 · S3","en":"TWO UPWARD LINKS: water leaves by evaporation and transpiration, then travels as vapour.","cn":"两条上升链：水经蒸发与蒸腾离开，再以水汽形式输送。"},{"senses":"S4","en":"THE INPUT: precipitation is the measurable income of every basin.","cn":"输入项：降水是每个流域可测量的收入。"},{"senses":"S5 · S6","en":"HOLD AND RELEASE: storage delays water, discharge releases it.","cn":"存与放：蓄存让水延迟，排泄把水放出。"},{"senses":"S7 · S8","en":"BALANCE AND SPEED: the loop can be closed as an equation, and warming changes only its rate.","cn":"平衡与速度：这个回路可以写成闭合方程，而变暖只改变它的速率。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"The phrase is assembled from two Greek morphemes plus one Greek noun for a round, which makes it a readable technical label rather than an opaque borrowing.","cn":"这个短语由两个希腊语素加一个表示「一圈」的希腊名词组装而成，因此是可读的技术标签，而不是不透明的借词。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"No Latin root is involved: hydōr is Greek, and Latin itself borrowed the Greek forms hydr- and cyclus. Latin aqua means water but is not the same root, so no Latin entries are listed.","cn":"这里不涉及拉丁词根：hydōr 是希腊语，拉丁语本身也是借入希腊形式 hydr- 与 cyclus。拉丁语 aqua 虽指水，却不是同一词根，因此不列拉丁条目。"},"items":[{"word":"hydro-","structure":"hydro- (Greek hydōr, water)","meaning":"water; relating to water","meaningCN":"水；与水的","example":"Hydroelectric plants use falling water.","exampleCN":"水电站利用下落的水。"},{"word":"-logy","structure":"-logy (Greek -logia, from logos, account or study)","meaning":"the study of the named subject","meaningCN":"对所指对象的系统研究","example":"Climatology studies long-term weather.","exampleCN":"气候学研究长期天气。"},{"word":"hydrology","structure":"hydro- + -logy","meaning":"the science of water on and under the earth","meaningCN":"研究地表水与地下水的科学","example":"Hydrology supplies the numbers for water planning.","exampleCN":"水文学为水资源规划提供数据。"},{"word":"hydrological","structure":"hydrology + -ical (relating to)","meaning":"relating to hydrology","meaningCN":"与水文学相关的","example":"Hydrological maps mark basin boundaries.","exampleCN":"水文图会标出流域边界。"},{"word":"hydrologist","structure":"hydrology + -ist (person who practises)","meaning":"a person who studies water","meaningCN":"研究水的人","example":"A hydrologist measured the river's flow.","exampleCN":"一位水文工作者测量了河流的流量。"},{"word":"hydrosphere","structure":"hydro- + -sphere (Greek sphaira, ball)","meaning":"the water layer of the planet","meaningCN":"行星的水圈层","example":"The hydrosphere includes ice and vapour.","exampleCN":"水圈包括冰与水汽。"},{"word":"hydrograph","structure":"hydro- + -graph (Greek graphein, to write)","meaning":"a plotted record of flow against time","meaningCN":"流量随时间变化的绘制记录","example":"The hydrograph peaks a day after the storm.","exampleCN":"流量过程线在暴雨后一天达到峰值。"},{"word":"evapotranspiration","structure":"evaporation + transpiration (Latin spirare, to breathe)","meaning":"combined loss of water from soil and plants","meaningCN":"土壤与植物共同散失的水","example":"Evapotranspiration returns half the rain to the air.","exampleCN":"蒸散作用把一半的雨水送回空中。"},{"word":"precipitation","structure":"pre- (down) + capit- (head) + -ation (process)","meaning":"water falling from the atmosphere","meaningCN":"从大气中落下的水","example":"Precipitation is the cycle's main input.","exampleCN":"降水是这一循环的主要输入。"},{"word":"runoff","structure":"run + off","meaning":"water that flows away over the land","meaningCN":"沿陆地流走的水","example":"Runoff carries sediment to the river.","exampleCN":"径流把泥沙带到河里。"}],"latinEntries":[]}},{"word":"groundwater","ipa_uk":"/ˈɡraʊnd.wɔːtə/","ipa_us":"/ˈɡraʊnd.wɑː.tər/","definition_zh":"地下水；储存在土壤孔隙与岩石裂隙中的水","definition_en":"water held in the pores and cracks of soil and rock beneath the earth's surface","core_image":"剖开的地层像海绵，缝隙里积满水，水位面在土层中划出一条平线","scene":"干旱季节，村里的井仍能提出清水，因为水藏在地下的砂砾缝隙里。Even in the dry season the village well still yields clear groundwater from the sandy layers below.","sceneCN":"这里 groundwater 指「储存于地表以下土壤与岩石孔隙中的水」（第 1 个义项：位于饱和带、可被井取出的地下水体）；句意为即使在旱季，村里的井仍能从下面的砂层中取出清澈的地下水。可辨识物件：井口、绳索、水桶、砂砾层、含水缝。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"地下水（不可数，指地下饱和带中的水）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"groundwater recharge","zh":"地下水补给"},{"phrase":"groundwater depletion","zh":"地下水超采（枯竭）"},{"phrase":"groundwater contamination","zh":"地下水污染"},{"phrase":"groundwater level","zh":"地下水位"},{"phrase":"groundwater flow","zh":"地下水流"},{"phrase":"groundwater irrigation","zh":"地下水灌溉"}],"forms":[{"label":"通常形式（不可数）","form":"groundwater"},{"label":"分写拼写（英式旧式）","form":"ground water"},{"label":"复数（指多个含水系统，罕用）","form":"groundwaters"},{"label":"作定语","form":"groundwater"},{"label":"相关名词（含水层）","form":"aquifer"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"groundwater-fed","pos":"adj.","zh":"由地下水补给的"},{"word":"groundwater-dependent","pos":"adj.","zh":"依赖地下水的"},{"word":"groundwaters","pos":"n.","zh":"地下水体（复数，指多个系统）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Water below the surface","titleCN":"地表以下的水","definition":"water stored in the saturated zone of soil and rock beneath the land surface","definitionCN":"储存于陆面以下土壤与岩石饱和带中的水","example":"Half the village drinks groundwater from a single well.","exampleCN":"村里一半人喝的是同一口井的地下水。","why":"Rain that sinks instead of running off does not disappear; it fills the empty spaces in soil and rock and stays there, out of sight.","whyCN":"没有流走而渗下去的雨并没有消失；它填满土壤与岩石中的空隙并留在那里，只是看不见。"},{"no":"02","title":"Below the water table","titleCN":"潜水面以下的水","definition":"the water in the zone where every pore is already full, above the water table","definitionCN":"潜水面以下、所有孔隙都已被水充满的带中的水","example":"Above the water table the soil is damp; below it, every pore is full of groundwater.","exampleCN":"潜水面以上的土壤是湿的；在它以下，每个孔隙都充满地下水。","why":"The defining line is saturation: above it pores hold air as well as water, below it there is no room left for air.","whyCN":"决定性的界线是饱和：界线以上孔隙里还有空气，界线以下则不再有空气的位置。"},{"no":"03","title":"A source of supply","titleCN":"供水水源","definition":"water drawn from wells and springs for drinking, farming and industry","definitionCN":"从井与泉中取出、用于饮用、农业与工业的水","example":"The city's supply comes from groundwater pumped two hundred metres down.","exampleCN":"这座城市的供水来自两百米深处抽出的地下水。","why":"Because it is stored and shielded from evaporation, groundwater is the most reliable source in regions with a long dry season.","whyCN":"由于被储存起来且不受蒸发影响，地下水是旱季漫长地区最可靠的来源。"},{"no":"04","title":"The counterpart of surface water","titleCN":"与地表水相对的一类","definition":"the water category opposed to rivers, lakes and reservoirs in law and management","definitionCN":"在法律与管理中与河流、湖泊、水库相对的水类","example":"The permit separates rights over surface water from rights over groundwater.","exampleCN":"这份许可把地表水权与地下水权分开。","why":"The two categories behave differently: surface water responds to rain within hours, groundwater within months or years.","whyCN":"两类水的行为不同：地表水在几小时内响应降雨，地下水则要数月或数年。"},{"no":"05","title":"Water inside an aquifer","titleCN":"含水层中的水","definition":"the water held and transmitted by a permeable rock unit","definitionCN":"由可渗透岩层储存并传输的水","example":"The sandstone aquifer holds groundwater that is thousands of years old.","exampleCN":"砂岩含水层中的地下水已有数千年之久。","why":"An aquifer is the container; groundwater is the contents. The same water is named for the rock only when the rock can hold and move it.","whyCN":"含水层是容器，地下水是内容物；只有当岩层能储存并输送水时，其中的水才以这种岩层来命名。"},{"no":"06","title":"Overdraft and pollution","titleCN":"超采与污染：被透支的水","definition":"the water resource that can be depleted or contaminated by human use","definitionCN":"会因人类使用而枯竭或被污染的水资源","example":"Decades of pumping have left the groundwater salty and depleted.","exampleCN":"数十年的抽水使地下水变得含盐且枯竭。","why":"Because the store refills slowly, taking water faster than recharge is like spending capital instead of interest.","whyCN":"由于储库补充很慢，取水快于补给就像花本金而不是花利息。"},{"no":"07","title":"The hidden base flow","titleCN":"隐性的基流","definition":"the water that seeps into streams between storms and keeps them flowing in dry weather","definitionCN":"在两次暴雨之间渗入溪流、使溪流在旱天仍不断流的水","example":"Even without rain, the stream survives on groundwater.","exampleCN":"即使不下雨，这条溪流也靠地下水维持。","why":"A river in dry weather is mostly an exposed edge of the water table, so the invisible store is what keeps the visible channel alive.","whyCN":"旱天的河流很大程度上是潜水面露出的边缘，因此看不见的储库才是让看得见的水道活着的原因。"},{"no":"08","title":"Abstract: a hidden reserve","titleCN":"比喻：隐而不露的储备","definition":"any resource kept out of sight that can be drawn on later","definitionCN":"任何藏而不露、日后可取用的资源","example":"The company has groundwater of goodwill to draw on in hard times.","exampleCN":"这家公司在困难时期有可以动用的善意储备。","why":"The image transfers easily: something valuable, invisible, slowly renewed, and easy to overdraw.","whyCN":"这个意象很容易迁移：有价值、看不见、补充缓慢，而且容易被透支。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Groundwater is an English compound of two native Old English words. The closed spelling is recent, and the geological sense grew out of the older meaning of ground as the earth's surface. Dates are approximate.","cn":"groundwater 是两个古英语本族词构成的英语复合词。连写形式出现较晚，其地质学含义由 ground「地表」的旧义发展而来。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"OLD ENGLISH GRUND","en":"Grund meant the bottom, foundation or surface of the earth; its deeper origin is uncertain, and no single Indo-European root is agreed for it.","cn":"grund 指底部、地基或地面；其更早来源不确定，学界未就单一印欧词根达成一致。"},{"era":"OLD ENGLISH WÆTER","en":"Wæter continues Proto-Germanic *watōr and belongs to the same Indo-European family as Greek hydōr and Latin unda, the last link being less certain.","cn":"wæter 延续原始日耳曼语 *watōr，与希腊语 hydōr、拉丁语 unda 同属一个印欧词族，其中与 unda 的联系较不确定。"},{"era":"EIGHTEENTH AND NINETEENTH CENTURIES","en":"Geologists wrote the two words separately as ground water while describing wells, springs and the layers that supply them.","cn":"地质学者在描述井、泉与供水岩层时，把这两个词分写为 ground water。"},{"era":"THE CLOSED FORM","en":"The single-word spelling groundwater spread in the twentieth century, when the resource became a subject of its own in engineering and law.","cn":"二十世纪，当这一资源成为工程与法律的独立对象时，连写形式 groundwater 流行开来。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (deep etymology and first attestation): the origin of grund before Old English is unsettled, and dictionaries do not fix the first use of the closed spelling.","cn":"来源不确定（深层词源与首见年代）：grund 在古英语之前的来源尚无定论，辞书也未确定连写形式的首次使用。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group holds look-alike and spelling variants; the second holds the water terms it is most often confused with.","cn":"第一组是形近词与拼写变体；第二组是最容易与之混淆的水类术语。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"ground water","ipa":"/ˈɡraʊnd ˌwɔːtə/","tag":"open spelling","definition":"The older two-word spelling of the same term, still seen in older geological texts.","definitionCN":"同一术语较早的分写形式，仍见于较早的地质文献。"},{"word":"underground","ipa":"/ˌʌn.dəˈɡraʊnd/","tag":"place, not substance","definition":"Below the surface as a position or direction; it does not name water.","definitionCN":"表示地表以下的位置或方向，并不指水本身。"},{"word":"ground","ipa":"/ɡraʊnd/","tag":"the surface itself","definition":"The solid surface of the earth; only the compound names the water inside it.","definitionCN":"地球的固体表面；只有复合词才指其中的水。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"aquifer","ipa":"/ˈæk.wɪ.fə/","tag":"the container","definition":"The rock or sediment that holds and transmits groundwater; the water is its contents.","definitionCN":"储存并输送地下水的岩层或沉积物；地下水是其中的内容物。"},{"word":"soil moisture","ipa":"/sɔɪl ˈmɔɪs.tʃə/","tag":"above the table","definition":"Water in the unsaturated layer, held by soil particles and available to roots.","definitionCN":"非饱和层中的水，被土粒吸附并可被根系利用。"},{"word":"surface water","ipa":"/ˈsɜː.fɪs ˌwɔːtə/","tag":"the visible counterpart","definition":"Water in rivers, lakes and reservoirs, exposed to the air and quick to respond to rain.","definitionCN":"河流、湖泊与水库中的水，暴露于空气并对降雨响应迅速。"},{"word":"spring","ipa":"/sprɪŋ/","tag":"where it surfaces","definition":"A place where groundwater reaches the surface on its own, not a store of water.","definitionCN":"地下水自行到达地表之处，而非水的储库。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: the two native words, the saturation line, and the two categories water managers actually use.","cn":"正常联想：两个本族词、饱和界线，以及水资源管理者真正使用的两个类别。"},"normal":[{"en":"ground + water is literally 'the water of the ground', so the compound needs no memorising.","cn":"ground 加 water 字面就是「地面的水」，这个复合词不需要另记。"},{"en":"The water table is the top surface of the groundwater, like the surface of a hidden lake.","cn":"潜水面就是地下水的顶面，像一座看不见的湖的水面。"},{"en":"Recharge is income, discharge is spending, and overdraft is pumping faster than recharge.","cn":"补给是收入，排泄是支出，超采就是抽水快于补给。"},{"en":"Groundwater is to an aquifer what milk is to a bottle: contents and container.","cn":"地下水与含水层的关系，就像牛奶与瓶子的关系：内容物与容器。"},{"en":"In dry weather a stream is fed by groundwater, which is why it keeps flowing without rain.","cn":"旱天溪流由地下水补给，所以不下雨也不断流。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Abstractly, groundwater is stored time: water that fell long ago and has not yet left.","cn":"抽象地看，地下水是被储存的时间：很久以前落下、至今尚未离开的水。"},{"en":"It is capital rather than income, so spending it feels free until the account is empty.","cn":"它是本金而不是利息，因此花用它在账空之前感觉像是免费的。"},{"en":"Anything valuable, unseen and slowly renewed follows the same pattern — including trust and reputation.","cn":"任何有价值、看不见、补充缓慢的东西都遵循同一模式——包括信任与声誉。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Groundwater provides about half of the world's drinking water.","cn":"地下水提供了全世界约一半的饮用水。"},{"en":"Nitrates from farms can reach groundwater and stay there for years.","cn":"农场的硝酸盐会进入地下水并在那里留存多年。"},{"en":"Where groundwater is mined faster than it refills, the land itself begins to sink.","cn":"在地下水开采快于补给的地方，土地本身会开始下沉。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「地（ground）+ 水（water）」——藏在地面下缝隙里的水 → 地下水","word":"groundwater"},"root":"古英语 grund「地面、底部」+ wæter「水」，英语本族复合词，十九世纪起用于地质学。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses go downward and then back out: water below the surface, the saturated store, its use as supply, its contrast with surface water, its container, its depletion, its hidden return to rivers, and finally the metaphor of a reserve.","cn":"八个义项先向下再向外：地表以下的水、饱和储库、作为水源的用途、与地表水的对照、它的容器、它的枯竭、它暗中回到河流，最后是「储备」的比喻。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a cutaway of soil and rock, pores full of water, a flat water line across the section.","cn":"核心意象：土壤与岩石的剖面，孔隙充满水，一条平直的水位线横贯其间。"},"chain":["SURFACE","PORE SPACE","SATURATION","STORED WATER","WITHDRAWAL","RETURN TO STREAM"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S2","en":"FROM DRY TO FULL: the same water is named at the surface and again below the saturation line.","cn":"从干到满：同一批水在地表被命名一次，在饱和线以下又被命名一次。"},{"senses":"S3 · S4","en":"TWO CATEGORIES OF SUPPLY: what is pumped from below is managed against what flows above.","cn":"两类供水：从地下抽取的水与从地表流过的水被分开管理。"},{"senses":"S5","en":"CONTENTS AND CONTAINER: the aquifer holds the water, and the water takes the aquifer's name.","cn":"内容与容器：含水层储存水，水也随含水层得名。"},{"senses":"S6","en":"OVERDRAFT: a slow-filling store can be spent faster than it refills.","cn":"透支：补充缓慢的储库可以被花得比补充更快。"},{"senses":"S7 · S8","en":"HIDDEN RETURN AND HIDDEN RESERVE: the unseen store feeds rivers, and the same image serves for any reserve.","cn":"隐性的回归与隐性的储备：看不见的储库供养河流，同一意象也可用于任何储备。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Groundwater is a transparent native compound, so its affix work is mostly compounding and adjective formation rather than prefixation.","cn":"groundwater 是透明的本族复合词，因此它的构词工作主要是复合与形容词化，而非加前缀。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"There is no Latin root here; both members are native Old English. The Latin-based vocabulary of the topic enters through borrowings such as aquifer, which is treated separately.","cn":"这里没有拉丁词根；两个成分都是古英语本族词。这一主题的拉丁语词汇通过 aquifer 一类借词进入，另作处理。"},"items":[{"word":"ground","structure":"ground (Old English grund, bottom or surface of the earth)","meaning":"the solid surface; the lower part","meaningCN":"固体表面；下方部分","example":"The ground was frozen hard.","exampleCN":"地面冻得很硬。"},{"word":"water","structure":"water (Old English wæter)","meaning":"the liquid itself","meaningCN":"水本身","example":"Water seeps slowly through sand.","exampleCN":"水会缓慢地渗过沙子。"},{"word":"groundwater","structure":"ground + water (compound noun)","meaning":"water held beneath the surface","meaningCN":"储存于地表以下的水","example":"Groundwater is cleaner than the river here.","exampleCN":"这里的地下水比河水干净。"},{"word":"groundwater-fed","structure":"groundwater + -fed (supplied with food or water)","meaning":"kept flowing by groundwater","meaningCN":"由地下水维持水流的","example":"A groundwater-fed wetland stayed green all summer.","exampleCN":"一片由地下水补给的湿地整个夏天都保持绿色。"},{"word":"groundwater-dependent","structure":"groundwater + dependent (relying on)","meaning":"needing groundwater to survive","meaningCN":"依靠地下水才能存续的","example":"Groundwater-dependent plants wither when the table drops.","exampleCN":"依赖地下水的植物在水位下降时枯萎。"},{"word":"water table","structure":"water + table (English compound of two native words)","meaning":"the upper surface of the saturated zone","meaningCN":"饱和带的上表面","example":"The water table fell by two metres.","exampleCN":"地下水位下降了两米。"},{"word":"recharge","structure":"re- (again) + charge (to load, from Latin carricare)","meaning":"the refilling of a groundwater store","meaningCN":"地下水储库的再补充","example":"Winter rain provides most recharge.","exampleCN":"冬季降雨提供大部分补给。"},{"word":"discharge","structure":"dis- (away) + charge (to load)","meaning":"water leaving the ground or a channel","meaningCN":"离开地下或河道的水","example":"The spring's discharge never stops.","exampleCN":"这眼泉的排出量从未停止。"}],"latinEntries":[]}},{"word":"underground","ipa_uk":"/ˌʌn.dəˈɡraʊnd/","ipa_us":"/ˌʌn.dɚˈɡraʊnd/","definition_zh":"地下的；在地面以下；秘密的；地下组织；（英）地铁","definition_en":"beneath the surface of the earth; also hidden from public view or kept secret","core_image":"街面上的人流车流之下，一条亮着灯的通道平行延伸，入口只是一道向下的梯口","scene":"施工围挡里，工人沿竖梯下到街面之下的通道，头顶的车流声渐渐变远。Workers descend a shaft into the underground tunnels beneath the busy street.","sceneCN":"这里 underground 指「位于地表以下的」（第 2 个义项：作定语，表示某空间或设施在地面之下）；句意为工人沿竖井下到繁忙街道下方的地下通道。可辨识物件：围挡、竖梯、隧道壁灯、头顶路面。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"地下的；地面以下的"},{"tag":"adv.","zh":"在地下；向地下"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"（英）地铁；地下组织"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"underground railway","zh":"地下铁路"},{"phrase":"underground water","zh":"地下水（旧式说法）"},{"phrase":"go underground","zh":"转入地下；隐匿起来"},{"phrase":"underground movement","zh":"地下运动；秘密组织"},{"phrase":"underground parking","zh":"地下停车场"},{"phrase":"underground economy","zh":"地下经济；灰色经济"}],"forms":[{"label":"原级（形容词／副词）","form":"underground"},{"label":"比较级（少用）","form":"more underground"},{"label":"最高级（少用）","form":"most underground"},{"label":"作名词（地铁，英式）","form":"the underground"},{"label":"复数（指多条地下线路，少用）","form":"undergrounds"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"undergrounder","pos":"n.","zh":"地下工作者；地下组织成员（罕用）"},{"word":"undergrounding","pos":"n.","zh":"管线入地；地下化（工程用语）"},{"word":"undergroundness","pos":"n.","zh":"地下状态；隐秘性（罕用）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Adverb: below the surface","titleCN":"副词：在地面以下","definition":"in or into the space beneath the surface of the earth","definitionCN":"在地面以下的空间里，或进入地面以下","example":"The cables run underground for three kilometres.","exampleCN":"这些电缆在地下延伸三公里。","why":"Under supplies the position below, ground supplies the surface, and the compound simply puts a thing on the far side of that surface.","whyCN":"under 提供「在下方」的位置，ground 提供「地面」这一参照，复合词只是把某物放到这个表面的另一侧。"},{"no":"02","title":"Adjective: situated below ground","titleCN":"形容词：地下的（作定语）","definition":"located, built or happening beneath the earth's surface","definitionCN":"位于、建造于或发生在地表以下的","example":"The hospital has an underground car park.","exampleCN":"这家医院有一个地下停车场。","why":"Before a noun the same compound stops describing where an action happens and starts labelling the thing itself: an underground tunnel is a tunnel of that kind.","whyCN":"放在名词前时，这个复合词不再描述动作发生的地点，而给事物本身贴标签：地下隧道就是这一类隧道。"},{"no":"03","title":"Secret and illegal","titleCN":"秘密的；非法的","definition":"hidden from the authorities or from public view, often because it is forbidden","definitionCN":"躲开当局或公众视线的，常因被禁止而隐秘","example":"The group ran an underground newspaper during the occupation.","exampleCN":"占领期间，这个团体办了一份地下报纸。","why":"What is physically below ground cannot be seen, so the word lends its image to anything driven out of sight by power.","whyCN":"物理上位于地面以下的东西看不见，于是这个词把它的意象借给一切被权力赶出视线的事物。"},{"no":"04","title":"The British subway","titleCN":"英式地铁","definition":"an urban railway running mainly in tunnels, called the underground or the tube","definitionCN":"主要在隧道中运行的城市铁路，英式称 the underground 或 the tube","example":"She takes the underground from King's Cross every morning.","exampleCN":"她每天早上从国王十字站坐地铁。","why":"London's Metropolitan Railway went below the streets in 1863, and the service took the plainest possible name from where it ran.","whyCN":"伦敦的大都会铁路于一八六三年驶入街道之下，这项服务就从它运行的位置取了最朴素的名字。"},{"no":"05","title":"Adverb: in hiding","titleCN":"副词：转入地下、隐匿","definition":"into a state of hiding from authorities or public attention","definitionCN":"进入躲避当局或公众注意的状态","example":"After the arrest, the rest of the cell went underground.","exampleCN":"抓捕之后，小组其余成员转入地下。","why":"The phrase go underground is a movement verb plus a place: disappearing from view is treated as moving to a place below the visible world.","whyCN":"go underground 是移动动词加地点：从视线中消失被当作移动到可见世界之下的一处地方。"},{"no":"06","title":"Underground culture","titleCN":"地下文化；非主流","definition":"art, music or film produced outside the commercial mainstream","definitionCN":"在商业主流之外产生的艺术、音乐或电影","example":"The band began in the underground scene before signing a record deal.","exampleCN":"这支乐队先在地下圈子活动，后来才签约。","why":"Here below ground means below the visible market: not illegal, but deliberately out of the mainstream's sight.","whyCN":"这里「地下」指在可见市场之下：并不违法，只是刻意避开主流视野。"},{"no":"07","title":"Built space below ground","titleCN":"地下建筑空间","definition":"rooms, shelters, stations and stores built beneath the surface","definitionCN":"建在地表以下的房间、掩体、车站与仓库","example":"The bunker was an underground city with its own power supply.","exampleCN":"那座掩体是一座自带供电的地下城市。","why":"The word shifts from a direction to a built environment: once people dig rooms, below-ground space becomes a place with its own architecture.","whyCN":"这个词从方向变成了建成环境：一旦人们挖出房间，地下空间就成了有自身建筑的一处场所。"},{"no":"08","title":"Abstract: what flows beneath","titleCN":"比喻：在表层之下流动的东西","definition":"an influence or current that operates out of sight beneath the visible surface","definitionCN":"在可见表层之下暗中运作的影响或潮流","example":"An underground of resentment fed the sudden protest.","exampleCN":"一股潜藏的怨气助长了那场突然的抗议。","why":"Underground is the perfect image for what is real but not shown: it is not absent, only covered.","whyCN":"「地下」是形容「真实却未显露之物」的完美意象：它并非不存在，只是被覆盖住了。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Underground joins two native Old English words. The adverb appears in the sixteenth century, the railway noun in the nineteenth, and the political sense follows from the idea of being out of sight.","cn":"underground 由两个古英语本族词合成。副词义十六世纪出现，地铁名词义在十九世纪，政治含义则由「不被看见」这一观念引申而来。"},"items":[{"era":"OLD ENGLISH UNDER","en":"Under is a native preposition of position, from Proto-Germanic *under and an Indo-European root usually reconstructed as *ndher, meaning below.","cn":"under 是本族方位介词，来自原始日耳曼语 *under 及通常重构为 *ndher 的印欧词根，意为「在下方」。"},{"era":"OLD ENGLISH GRUND","en":"Grund meant bottom, foundation or the earth's surface; its deeper origin is uncertain and no single Indo-European root is agreed.","cn":"grund 指底部、地基或地面；其更早来源不确定，学界未就单一印欧词根达成一致。"},{"era":"SIXTEENTH CENTURY ADVERB","en":"The adverb underground is recorded in the sixteenth century in the plain local sense of being or going below the surface.","cn":"副词 underground 在十六世纪有记载，用的就是「在地面以下」或「到地面以下」的本义。"},{"era":"NINETEENTH CENTURY NOUN","en":"In the 1860s the word became a noun for a railway running in tunnels, above all the London underground, and later for any secret organisation.","cn":"十九世纪六十年代，这个词成为运行于隧道中的铁路的名词，尤指伦敦地铁，后来又指任何秘密组织。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (deep etymology): grund has no settled Indo-European origin, and the exact date of the first political use of underground is not fixed by standard references.","cn":"来源不确定（深层词源）：grund 没有定论的印欧语来源，而 underground 政治用法的最早年代也未被通行资料确定。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group holds words that look or sound close; the second holds words with overlapping meaning but a different image.","cn":"第一组是形近或音近的词；第二组是含义交叠但意象不同的词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"under ground","ipa":"/ˈʌn.də ɡraʊnd/","tag":"open phrase","definition":"Two words meaning 'beneath the earth', but never the fixed adjective or the railway noun.","definitionCN":"分写的两个词，表示「在地面之下」，但不是那个固定形容词，也不指地铁。"},{"word":"underneath","ipa":"/ˌʌn.dəˈniːθ/","tag":"near neighbour","definition":"Directly beneath something, often touching it; it has no secret or cultural sense.","definitionCN":"紧贴在某物下方、常相接触；它没有秘密或文化含义。"},{"word":"undergrowth","ipa":"/ˈʌn.də.ɡrəʊθ/","tag":"same first element","definition":"Low plants growing under taller ones; the second element is growth, not ground.","definitionCN":"在高大植物下生长的小植物；第二个成分是 growth，不是 ground。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"subterranean","ipa":"/ˌsʌb.təˈreɪ.ni.ən/","tag":"Latin-based synonym","definition":"Below the earth, borrowed from Latin sub plus terra; it is formal and has no secret sense.","definitionCN":"地表以下，借自拉丁语 sub 加 terra；语体正式，且没有秘密含义。"},{"word":"buried","ipa":"/ˈber.id/","tag":"covered by soil","definition":"Placed in the ground and covered; a thing is buried, a space is underground.","definitionCN":"被放入土中并覆盖；物是「被埋」，空间才是「地下」。"},{"word":"clandestine","ipa":"/klænˈdes.tɪn/","tag":"secret only","definition":"Kept secret by design; it carries no physical sense of being below ground.","definitionCN":"刻意保密；它不含「在地面以下」的物理意义。"},{"word":"subway","ipa":"/ˈsʌb.weɪ/","tag":"American counterpart","definition":"The American word for an urban underground railway, and also a pedestrian underpass in Britain.","definitionCN":"美式指城市地下铁路；在英国则指行人地下通道。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: the two native words, the 1863 railway, and the two real families built with under-.","cn":"正常联想：两个本族词、一八六三年的铁路，以及两个真实由 under- 构成的词族。"},"normal":[{"en":"under + ground is readable at once: the place beneath the ground.","cn":"under 加 ground 一看就懂：地面之下的地方。"},{"en":"London's underground railway opened in 1863, which is why the British still say the underground.","cn":"伦敦的地下铁路于一八六三年开通，所以英国人至今说 the underground。"},{"en":"underground water is the old way of saying groundwater, and both name the same store.","cn":"underground water 是 groundwater 的旧说法，两者指同一处储水。"},{"en":"under- builds a family: undersea, underwater, undergrowth, underpass.","cn":"under- 构成一族词：海底的、水下的、林下灌丛、地下通道。"},{"en":"go underground means 'hide', because hiding is imagined as descending out of sight.","cn":"go underground 意为「隐匿」，因为躲藏被想象成下到看不见的地方。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Abstractly, underground divides the world into a visible surface and an invisible depth, and everything can be sorted into one or the other.","cn":"抽象地看，underground 把世界分成可见的表层与不可见的深处，任何事物都可归入其中之一。"},{"en":"What is underground is not gone; it is simply out of the light, which is why the word suits both secret politics and hidden feelings.","cn":"位于地下的东西并未消失，只是不在光里，所以这个词既适合秘密政治，也适合隐藏的情绪。"},{"en":"The word is a promise about depth: something continues below the line even when the surface looks empty.","cn":"这个词是对深度的一个承诺：即使表层看起来空无一物，线下仍有什么在继续。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The city stores most of its drinking water in underground tanks.","cn":"这座城市把大部分饮用水储存在地下水池里。"},{"en":"The movement was forced underground after the new law was passed.","cn":"新法律通过后，这场运动被迫转入地下。"},{"en":"Take the underground to the museum; the entrance is right by the station.","cn":"坐地铁去博物馆，入口就在车站旁边。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「安德（under，在下面）+ 格朗德（ground，地面）」——钻到地面下面去 → 地下的","word":"underground"},"root":"古英语 under「在下方」+ grund「地面、底部」，英语本族复合词。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses descend step by step: a position, a label, a secret, a railway, a hiding, a subculture, a built space, and finally any current beneath the visible surface.","cn":"八个义项逐级下沉：一个位置、一个定语标签、一种秘密、一条铁路、一种隐匿、一种亚文化、一处建成空间，最后是任何表层之下的潮流。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a stair going down from the street into a lit corridor under the pavement.","cn":"核心意象：一段从街面下行的楼梯，通向路面之下一条亮灯的走廊。"},"chain":["SURFACE LINE","DESCENT","HIDDEN SPACE","BUILT TUNNEL","CONCEALMENT","SUBCULTURE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S2","en":"POSITION AND LABEL: the same word tells where something is and what kind of thing it is.","cn":"位置与标签：同一个词既说明某物在哪里，也说明它是哪一类。"},{"senses":"S3 · S5","en":"OUT OF SIGHT: secrecy and hiding reuse the physical image of being covered.","cn":"不被看见：秘密与隐匿复用了「被覆盖」的物理意象。"},{"senses":"S4","en":"THE NAMED RAILWAY: a real tunnel system turns the direction into a proper noun.","cn":"被命名的铁路：真实的隧道系统把方向变成了专名。"},{"senses":"S6 · S7","en":"BELOW THE MAINSTREAM: culture and architecture both build a world under the visible one.","cn":"主流之下：文化与建筑都在可见世界之下造出另一个世界。"},{"senses":"S8","en":"BENEATH THE SURFACE: what is hidden is still present, only unlit.","cn":"表层之下：隐藏之物仍然存在，只是不在光里。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Underground is built from a preposition and a noun, and the first element under- is one of the most productive prefixes in English.","cn":"underground 由介词与名词构成，其中第一个成分 under- 是英语中构词能力最强的前缀之一。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"There is no Latin root here. The Latin-based synonym subterranean comes from sub plus terra, a separate formation with a different history, so no Latin entries are listed.","cn":"这里没有拉丁词根。拉丁来源的同义词 subterranean 出自 sub 加 terra，是另一套构词、另一段历史，因此不列拉丁条目。"},"items":[{"word":"under","structure":"under (native preposition, below)","meaning":"below or beneath","meaningCN":"在……下方","example":"The cat slept under the table.","exampleCN":"猫在桌子下面睡着了。"},{"word":"under-","structure":"under- (prefix of position or insufficiency)","meaning":"below; also not enough","meaningCN":"在下方；也可表示不足","example":"The project was underfunded.","exampleCN":"这个项目资金不足。"},{"word":"underground","structure":"under + ground","meaning":"below the surface; hidden","meaningCN":"地表以下；隐秘的","example":"The station is underground.","exampleCN":"这个车站位于地下。"},{"word":"underwater","structure":"under + water","meaning":"below the surface of water","meaningCN":"水面以下的","example":"Underwater cameras recorded the reef.","exampleCN":"水下摄影机记录了珊瑚礁。"},{"word":"undersea","structure":"under + sea","meaning":"below the sea, usually of the seabed","meaningCN":"海面以下的，通常指海底","example":"Undersea cables carry most internet traffic.","exampleCN":"海底电缆承载大部分互联网流量。"},{"word":"undergrowth","structure":"under + growth","meaning":"low plants beneath taller ones","meaningCN":"高大植物下层的低矮植物","example":"The path was lost in the undergrowth.","exampleCN":"小路消失在灌丛里。"},{"word":"underpass","structure":"under + pass","meaning":"a road or path passing beneath another","meaningCN":"从另一条路下方穿过的通道","example":"Use the underpass to cross the ring road.","exampleCN":"走地下通道穿过环路。"},{"word":"underlie","structure":"under + lie","meaning":"to be the hidden cause or base of something","meaningCN":"成为某物隐藏的原因或基础","example":"Several faults underlie the dispute.","exampleCN":"这场争端背后有几处症结。"},{"word":"underneath","structure":"under + neath (an old word for below)","meaning":"directly below and often covered","meaningCN":"正下方，且常被遮住","example":"A label was stuck underneath the box.","exampleCN":"盒子底下贴着一张标签。"}],"latinEntries":[]}},{"word":"aquifer","ipa_uk":"/ˈæk.wɪ.fə/","ipa_us":"/ˈæk.wə.fɚ/","definition_zh":"含水层；能够储存并输送地下水的透水岩层或沉积层","definition_en":"a body of permeable rock or sediment that can store and transmit groundwater","core_image":"一层多孔的砂岩夹在两层致密泥岩之间，水在砂粒缝隙中缓慢横向流动","scene":"田边的钻井上，水泵把百尺之下砂层里的水抽上地面，农人接进灌溉渠。The pump lifts water from a sandstone aquifer far below the field.","sceneCN":"这里 aquifer 指「能储存并输送地下水的透水岩层」（第 1 个义项：由孔隙或裂隙透水、可作为地下水储库的岩层体）；句意为水泵把田地深处砂岩含水层中的水抽上来。可辨识物件：钻机、出水管、灌溉渠、砂岩层、泥岩隔水层。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"含水层；蓄水岩层"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"sandstone aquifer","zh":"砂岩含水层"},{"phrase":"confined aquifer","zh":"承压含水层"},{"phrase":"unconfined aquifer","zh":"潜水含水层"},{"phrase":"aquifer recharge","zh":"含水层补给"},{"phrase":"aquifer depletion","zh":"含水层枯竭"},{"phrase":"aquifer storage","zh":"含水层储水"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"aquifer"},{"label":"复数","form":"aquifers"},{"label":"相关形容词","form":"aquiferous"},{"label":"相关名词（隔水层）","form":"aquiclude"},{"label":"相关名词（水文地质学）","form":"hydrogeology"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"aquiferous","pos":"adj.","zh":"含水的；透水蓄水的"},{"word":"aquiclude","pos":"n.","zh":"隔水层；不透水层"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"A water-bearing rock body","titleCN":"含水岩层：能存水也能过水","definition":"a rock or sediment unit porous and permeable enough to hold and transmit usable amounts of water","definitionCN":"孔隙与透水性足以储存并输送可用水量的岩层或沉积层","example":"The town draws its water from a shallow aquifer.","exampleCN":"这座镇子从一处浅层含水层取水。","why":"The word needs two conditions at once: enough empty space to store water, and enough connection between spaces to let it move toward a well.","whyCN":"这个词同时要求两个条件：有足够空隙存水，且空隙彼此连通，让水能朝井的方向移动。"},{"no":"02","title":"The confined aquifer","titleCN":"承压含水层：被隔水层压住","definition":"an aquifer lying between impermeable layers, so its water is under pressure","definitionCN":"夹在不透水层之间、其中的水承受压力的含水层","example":"A confined aquifer can push water up a well without any pump.","exampleCN":"承压含水层无需水泵就能把水顶到井口。","why":"If the water is sealed under a lid of clay, the weight upstream raises its pressure, and a well becomes a release valve.","whyCN":"如果水被黏土层封在下面，上游的重力会提高它的压力，井口就成了泄压口。"},{"no":"03","title":"The unconfined aquifer","titleCN":"潜水含水层：水面自由","definition":"an aquifer whose upper limit is the water table, open to recharge from above","definitionCN":"上界为潜水面、可接受上方补给的含水层","example":"In an unconfined aquifer the water level simply follows the water table.","exampleCN":"在潜水含水层中，水位就随潜水面升降。","why":"With no lid, rain sinks straight in and the surface of the saturated zone is free to rise and fall with the seasons.","whyCN":"没有盖子，雨水直接渗入，饱和带的水面便随季节自由升降。"},{"no":"04","title":"A source of supply","titleCN":"供水水源：井与钻孔的对象","definition":"the underground layer that wells and boreholes are drilled into for supply","definitionCN":"为供水而打井、钻孔所指向的地下岩层","example":"Farmers drilled into the aquifer to irrigate the orchard.","exampleCN":"农民钻入含水层为果园灌溉。","why":"Supply is not the water alone but the layer that yields it at a usable rate, so the layer itself becomes the resource in planning.","whyCN":"供水不只是水本身，而是能以可用速率出水的那一层，因此在规划中这一层本身就成了资源。"},{"no":"05","title":"A hydrogeological unit","titleCN":"水文地质单元：图上的一块","definition":"a mapped unit with defined boundaries, properties and flow behaviour","definitionCN":"具有确定边界、性质与流动行为并可在图上标出的单元","example":"The model divides the basin into four aquifer units.","exampleCN":"模型把这个流域分成四个含水层单元。","why":"Once the layer is given boundaries and numbers, it stops being a place and becomes a unit that can be modelled and assigned rights.","whyCN":"一旦这一层被划定边界并赋以数值，它就不再只是一个地方，而成为可模拟、可分配权利的单元。"},{"no":"06","title":"Storage and recharge","titleCN":"储水与回灌：把水放回去","definition":"the layer used to bank water underground for later recovery","definitionCN":"用于把水存到地下、日后取回的那一层","example":"The city injects treated storm water into the aquifer each winter.","exampleCN":"这座城市每年冬天把处理过的雨水注入含水层。","why":"If the rock already holds water, it can also hold more; the aquifer becomes a bank with slow deposits and faster withdrawals.","whyCN":"如果岩层本来就能存水，它也能存更多；含水层于是成了一家存款慢、取款快的银行。"},{"no":"07","title":"Vulnerability to pollution","titleCN":"污染脆弱性：容易被弄脏的储库","definition":"an aquifer considered in terms of how easily contaminants reach and persist in it","definitionCN":"从污染物进入与滞留难易程度来看的含水层","example":"The shallow aquifer is vulnerable to nitrate from the fields above.","exampleCN":"浅层含水层容易受到上方农田硝酸盐的影响。","why":"A porous layer with a thin cover admits pollution quickly and cleans it slowly, so vulnerability becomes a property of the layer itself.","whyCN":"覆盖薄而多孔的岩层让污染进得快、清得慢，因此脆弱性成了这一层自身的属性。"},{"no":"08","title":"Abstract: a deep reserve","titleCN":"比喻：深处的储备","definition":"any large hidden store that can be drawn on over time","definitionCN":"任何可长期取用的巨大隐藏储备","example":"The archive is an aquifer of forgotten detail for the historian.","exampleCN":"对历史学者而言，这座档案馆是一座被遗忘细节的深藏水库。","why":"The image keeps its key features: invisible, capacious, slowly refilled, and easy to drain without noticing.","whyCN":"这个意象保留了关键特征：看不见、容量大、补充缓慢，而且在不知不觉中容易被抽干。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Aquifer is a learned Latin coinage, not an inherited word: aqua supplies water and -fer supplies bearing. It entered English through geology in the nineteenth century.","cn":"aquifer 是学术性的拉丁语新造词，而非承继词：aqua 提供「水」，-fer 提供「承载」。它在十九世纪经地质学进入英语。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN AQUA","en":"Aqua was the ordinary Latin word for water and survives in aquarium, aquatic and aqueduct; it is a different root from Greek hydōr.","cn":"aqua 是拉丁语中表示水的普通词，留存于 aquarium、aquatic 与 aqueduct；它与希腊语 hydōr 是不同的词根。"},{"era":"LATIN FERRE","en":"Ferre meant to carry or bear, and its combining form -fer appears in many scientific adjectives such as carboniferous and coniferous.","cn":"ferre 意为携带、承载，其组合形式 -fer 出现在许多科学形容词中，如 carboniferous 与 coniferous。"},{"era":"THE COINAGE","en":"The compound is generally regarded as a modern Latin formation in which the two Latin elements were joined to name a water-bearing stratum.","cn":"这个复合词一般被认为是近代拉丁语构词，把两个拉丁成分组合起来，用于命名含水岩层。"},{"era":"NINETEENTH CENTURY ENGLISH","en":"English geology adopted aquifer in the early nineteenth century, when groundwater stopped being described simply as water in wells and became a layer with properties.","cn":"英国地质学在十九世纪初采纳 aquifer，当时地下水不再只被描述为井中之水，而成为具有性质的一层。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (coiner and first date): the exact author and year of the first use of aquifer are not fixed in standard dictionaries, so the dating here is an estimate.","cn":"来源不确定（首创者与首见年代）：aquifer 首次使用的确切作者与年份在通行辞书中未定，此处的年代只是估计。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group holds the Latin-shaped neighbours that are easiest to confuse; the second holds the layers and water bodies that are close in meaning.","cn":"第一组是最易混淆的拉丁词形近邻；第二组是含义相近的岩层与水体。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"aqueduct","ipa":"/ˈæk.wɪ.dʌkt/","tag":"carries water, not stores it","definition":"A channel or bridge built to convey water; the second element means 'lead', not 'bear'.","definitionCN":"为输水而建的渠道或渡槽；第二个成分意为「引导」，不是「承载」。"},{"word":"aqua","ipa":"/ˈæk.wə/","tag":"the Latin element","definition":"Water as a Latin word and a combining form; it is one piece of aquifer, not another kind of layer.","definitionCN":"作为拉丁词与组合成分的「水」；它是 aquifer 的一个构件，而不是另一类岩层。"},{"word":"aquiferous","ipa":"/ˌæk.wɪˈfer.əs/","tag":"adjective form","definition":"The adjective meaning 'water-bearing'; it describes a layer rather than naming one.","definitionCN":"意为「含水的」形容词；它描述岩层，而不给岩层命名。"},{"word":"aquiclude","ipa":"/ˈæk.wɪ.kluːd/","tag":"the opposite layer","definition":"A layer that holds water but will not transmit it; the second element means 'shut'.","definitionCN":"能含水却不导水的岩层；第二个成分意为「关闭」。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"groundwater","ipa":"/ˈɡraʊnd.wɔːtə/","tag":"contents","definition":"The water inside the layer; an aquifer is the container and groundwater is what it holds.","definitionCN":"岩层中的水；含水层是容器，地下水是所装之物。"},{"word":"aquiclude","ipa":"/ˈæk.wɪ.kluːd/","tag":"the confining layer","definition":"A bed that blocks flow and therefore defines the boundaries of an aquifer.","definitionCN":"阻止水流、因而界定含水层边界的岩层。"},{"word":"reservoir","ipa":"/rɪˈzɜː.vwɑː/","tag":"general store","definition":"Any natural or artificial store of water; only the aquifer is specifically a rock layer.","definitionCN":"任何天然或人工的储水体；只有含水层特指岩层。"},{"word":"water table","ipa":"/ˈwɔːtə ˌteɪbl/","tag":"the upper limit","definition":"The top surface of the saturated zone, not the layer that contains it.","definitionCN":"饱和带的上表面，而不是包含它的岩层。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: the two Latin pieces, the pair with aquiclude, and the pressure difference between the two aquifer types.","cn":"正常联想：两个拉丁成分、与 aquiclude 的成对关系，以及两类含水层的压力差别。"},"normal":[{"en":"aqua is water, -fer is bearing: an aquifer is literally a water-bearer.","cn":"aqua 是水，-fer 是承载：aquifer 字面就是「载水者」。"},{"en":"aquiclude has -clude, to shut: the layer that shuts water out, the exact opposite of the aquifer.","cn":"aquiclude 含 -clude「关闭」：把水关在外面的岩层，正好与含水层相反。"},{"en":"Confined means a lid of impermeable rock; unconfined means no lid at all.","cn":"confined 表示有不透水岩层做盖；unconfined 表示完全没有盖。"},{"en":"An aquifer stores and transmits; a tank stores only. That is why the word needs both pore space and connection.","cn":"含水层既储存又输送，水箱只储存；所以这个词同时要求孔隙空间与连通性。"},{"en":"The adjective is aquiferous, so the geology family keeps the Latin -fer throughout.","cn":"形容词是 aquiferous，地质学词族始终保留拉丁的 -fer。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Abstractly, an aquifer is a sponge made of stone: the rock is the solid, the water is the content, and the pores are the roads.","cn":"抽象地看，含水层是一块石头做的海绵：岩石是固体，水是内容，孔隙是道路。"},{"en":"It is also a slow bank: deposits arrive by gravity over years, withdrawals happen in minutes.","cn":"它也是一家缓慢的银行：存款靠重力经年累月到达，取款却只需几分钟。"},{"en":"Any system that hides capacity inside solid structure follows this model — including institutions and memory.","cn":"任何把容量藏在坚固结构内部的系统都遵循这个模型——包括制度与记忆。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The aquifer under the plain holds enough water for a century of farming.","cn":"平原下的含水层储存的水足够农业用一百年。"},{"en":"Salt water has crept into the coastal aquifer as pumping lowered its pressure.","cn":"抽水降低了压力，海水因此侵入沿海含水层。"},{"en":"Geologists map an aquifer by measuring how easily water moves through the rock.","cn":"地质学家通过测量水穿过岩石的难易程度来绘制含水层。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「阿夸（aqua，水）+ 弗（-fer，带着）」——带着水的那层石头 → 含水层","word":"aquifer"},"root":"拉丁语 aqua「水」+ -fer（ferre「携带、承载」），近代拉丁语新造词，十九世纪进入英语地质学。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one layer: the rock that holds and moves water, its two pressure types, its use as supply, its status as a mapped unit, its banking and pollution, and finally its use as an image of a deep reserve.","cn":"八个义项围绕同一岩层展开：能存水也能过水的岩层、两种压力类型、作为供水对象、作为图上单元、储水回灌与污染，最后是作为「深处储备」的意象。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a porous sandstone bed between two tight clay beds, water creeping sideways through the sand.","cn":"核心意象：夹在两层致密黏土之间的多孔砂岩层，水在砂粒间横向缓行。"},"chain":["POROUS ROCK","PORE SPACE","CONNECTION","STORED WATER","PRESSURE","WELL"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1","en":"TWO CONDITIONS: storage space plus connected pores make a rock an aquifer.","cn":"两个条件：储水空间加上连通的孔隙，才使岩层成为含水层。"},{"senses":"S2 · S3","en":"WITH OR WITHOUT A LID: pressure or freedom at the top separates the two types.","cn":"有盖或无盖：顶部受压还是自由，区分了两种类型。"},{"senses":"S4","en":"THE WELL: supply is the layer yielding water at a usable rate.","cn":"井：供水指的是以可用速率出水的那一层。"},{"senses":"S5 · S7","en":"BOUNDARIES AND RISK: mapped units have edges, and edges admit pollution.","cn":"边界与风险：被制图的单元有边界，而边界会放进污染。"},{"senses":"S6 · S8","en":"BANK AND METAPHOR: water can be deposited underground, and the same image serves any hidden capacity.","cn":"银行与比喻：水可以存到地下，而同一意象可用于任何隐藏容量。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Aquifer is built from two Latin morphemes that also build a visible technical family, so the word can be read from its parts.","cn":"aquifer 由两个拉丁语素构成，这两个语素还构成一个可见的技术词族，因此可以从构件读出词义。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin basis is aqua, water, and ferre, to bear. The same two elements recur in aquiferous and in the contrasting aquiclude, where claudere, to shut, replaces ferre.","cn":"拉丁语基础是 aqua「水」与 ferre「承载」。同样两个成分也见于 aquiferous，以及与之相对、以 claudere「关闭」替换 ferre 的 aquiclude。"},"items":[{"word":"aqua","structure":"aqua (Latin, water)","meaning":"water","meaningCN":"水","example":"Aquatic plants live in water.","exampleCN":"水生植物生活在水中。"},{"word":"-fer","structure":"-fer (Latin ferre, to bear or carry)","meaning":"bearing or carrying","meaningCN":"承载、携带","example":"Coniferous trees bear cones.","exampleCN":"针叶树结球果。"},{"word":"aquifer","structure":"aqua + -fer","meaning":"a water-bearing rock layer","meaningCN":"含水的岩层","example":"The aquifer supplies the whole valley.","exampleCN":"这个含水层供养整个谷地。"},{"word":"aquiferous","structure":"aqua + -fer + -ous (full of, having)","meaning":"water-bearing","meaningCN":"含水的、带水的","example":"The aquiferous sandstone is drilled for water.","exampleCN":"人们在这层含水砂岩中钻井取水。"},{"word":"aquiclude","structure":"aqua + claudere (Latin, to shut)","meaning":"a layer that holds but does not transmit water","meaningCN":"能含水却不导水的岩层","example":"Clay forms an aquiclude above the sand.","exampleCN":"黏土在砂层之上形成隔水层。"},{"word":"aqueduct","structure":"aqua + ducere (Latin, to lead)","meaning":"a channel built to carry water","meaningCN":"为输水而建的渠道","example":"The old aqueduct still crosses the valley.","exampleCN":"古老的渡槽仍横跨谷地。"},{"word":"aquaculture","structure":"aqua + cultura (Latin, cultivation)","meaning":"farming of water organisms","meaningCN":"水生生物的养殖","example":"Aquaculture supplies much of the world's fish.","exampleCN":"水产养殖提供世界上很大一部分鱼。"},{"word":"aquatic","structure":"aqua + -atic (relating to)","meaning":"living or happening in water","meaningCN":"在水中生活或发生的","example":"Aquatic insects colonised the pond.","exampleCN":"水生昆虫占据了这口池塘。"},{"word":"groundwater","structure":"ground + water (native compound, not Latin)","meaning":"the water an aquifer holds","meaningCN":"含水层所储存的水","example":"Groundwater flows through the pores.","exampleCN":"地下水在孔隙中流动。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"aqua","structure":"aqua (Latin noun, water)","meaning":"water","meaningCN":"水"},{"word":"ferre","structure":"ferre (Latin verb, to bear or carry)","meaning":"to carry, to bear","meaningCN":"携带、承载"},{"word":"aquifer","structure":"aquifer (New Latin, water-bearing)","meaning":"a water-bearing layer","meaningCN":"含水的岩层"},{"word":"aquiferous","structure":"aquifer + -ous (New Latin adjective)","meaning":"water-bearing","meaningCN":"含水的"}]}},{"word":"water table","ipa_uk":"/ˈwɔːtə ˌteɪbl/","ipa_us":"/ˈwɔːtər ˌteɪbəl/","definition_zh":"潜水面；地下水位面；也指建筑外墙上的滴水线脚","definition_en":"the upper surface of the saturated zone underground, where pores are just filled with water","core_image":"剖面里一条平直的水线，线下岩土颜色变深，线上的孔隙还留着空气","scene":"打井的钻杆提上来的土由湿变干，师傅说已经越过了那条界线。The drill brings up dry sand once it rises above the water table.","sceneCN":"这里 water table 指「地下饱和带的上界面，即地下水位面」（第 1 个义项：孔隙刚好被水充满的那一层界面）；句意为钻杆升到潜水面以上后带上来的就是干沙。可辨识物件：钻杆、湿沙与干沙、井口、地层剖面。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"潜水面；地下水位"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"（建筑）滴水线脚；外墙防雨挑檐"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"water table depth","zh":"地下水位埋深"},{"phrase":"rising water table","zh":"上升的地下水位"},{"phrase":"lower the water table","zh":"降低地下水位"},{"phrase":"water table fluctuation","zh":"地下水位波动"},{"phrase":"perched water table","zh":"上层滞水水位"},{"phrase":"water table contour","zh":"潜水面等值线"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"water table"},{"label":"复数","form":"water tables"},{"label":"同义术语（学术）","form":"water level"},{"label":"同义术语（地质）","form":"groundwater table"},{"label":"相关名词（潜水面）","form":"phreatic surface"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"water-table","pos":"adj.","zh":"潜水面的；地下水位相关的（作定语）"},{"word":"water-table decline","pos":"n.","zh":"地下水位下降"},{"word":"water-table map","pos":"n.","zh":"潜水面图；地下水位图"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The upper surface of saturation","titleCN":"饱和带上界面：水刚好充满孔隙","definition":"the boundary below which every pore in soil or rock is filled with water","definitionCN":"其下方土壤或岩石的每个孔隙都被水充满的那条界线","example":"Below the water table, the sample came out dripping.","exampleCN":"在潜水面以下取出的样品是滴着水的。","why":"The line is not a physical sheet but a level: at it, the pore space passes from partly air-filled to completely water-filled.","whyCN":"这条线不是一片实物薄层，而是一个高度：在此处，孔隙空间从部分含气转为完全充水。"},{"no":"02","title":"A measurable level","titleCN":"可测量的水位：井里的水面","definition":"the level at which water stands in an observation well open to the aquifer","definitionCN":"在与含水层连通的观测井中水所停住的高度","example":"The logger records the water table every hour.","exampleCN":"记录仪每小时记录一次地下水位。","why":"Hydrologists cannot see the whole surface, so they let a well stand in for it: the level in the pipe is the level of the surrounding pores.","whyCN":"水文工作者看不到整个水面，于是用一口井来代表它：管中的水位就是周围孔隙的水位。"},{"no":"03","title":"A seasonal rise and fall","titleCN":"季节性升降","definition":"the water table as a level that rises with recharge and falls in dry periods","definitionCN":"随补给上升、在旱季下降的那个水位","example":"The water table climbs two metres after the spring rains.","exampleCN":"春季降雨之后，地下水位上升两米。","why":"Because the surface is free in an unconfined aquifer, it behaves like the top of a slowly filling tank that leaks into streams.","whyCN":"在潜水含水层中这个面是自由的，它的行为就像一只缓慢注水、又向河流渗漏的水箱顶面。"},{"no":"04","title":"The source of base flow","titleCN":"基流的来源","definition":"the level whose intersection with a valley floor feeds streams between storms","definitionCN":"与谷底相交处向溪流供水、维持两次暴雨之间水流的水位","example":"Where the water table meets the streambed, the river keeps flowing.","exampleCN":"潜水面与河床相接处，河水就能持续流动。","why":"A stream in dry weather is simply the exposed edge of the saturated zone, so the level decides whether the channel is wet.","whyCN":"旱天的溪流不过是饱和带露出的边缘，因此这个水位决定河道是否有水。"},{"no":"05","title":"Depth below the surface","titleCN":"埋深：离地面有多深","definition":"the distance from ground level down to the water table, a standard site measurement","definitionCN":"从地面向下到潜水面的距离，是场地测量的标准项目","example":"Builders measured a water table depth of six metres.","exampleCN":"施工方测得的潜水面埋深为六米。","why":"The same level matters differently depending on how far down it lies: a shallow table limits foundations, a deep one costs more to pump.","whyCN":"同一个水位因埋深不同而意义不同：浅水位限制地基，深水位则抽水成本更高。"},{"no":"06","title":"A falling level","titleCN":"下降的水位：超采的信号","definition":"the water table considered as an indicator of over-pumping and drying wells","definitionCN":"作为过度抽水与井水枯竭指标的那个水位","example":"Years of pumping sent the water table down thirty metres.","exampleCN":"多年抽水使地下水位下降了三十米。","why":"If withdrawals exceed recharge, the level must drop, so the level itself becomes the cheapest warning instrument.","whyCN":"如果取水超过补给，水位必然下降，因此水位本身就成了最廉价的警报器。"},{"no":"07","title":"The architectural ledge","titleCN":"建筑中的滴水线脚","definition":"a projecting band on a wall that throws rainwater clear of the surface below","definitionCN":"墙面上向外挑出的带状构件，把雨水甩离下方的墙面","example":"The old facade has a stone water table above the basement.","exampleCN":"这座老建筑在地下室上方有一条石制滴水线脚。","why":"This is an older use of the same two words: a table is a flat projecting course, and it shed water exactly as its name says.","whyCN":"这是同两个词较早的用法：table 指平直的挑出线脚，而它确实像名字所说的那样把水甩开。"},{"no":"08","title":"Abstract: the hidden threshold","titleCN":"比喻：看不见的门槛","definition":"an invisible limit above which something is absent and below which it is present","definitionCN":"在其上方某物缺席、在其下方某物存在的隐形界线","example":"There is a water table of patience, and once it drops, nothing grows.","exampleCN":"耐心也有一个看不见的水位，一旦降到线下，什么都长不出来。","why":"The image works because the line is invisible yet decisive: nothing above it, everything below it.","whyCN":"这个意象有效，是因为这条线看不见却具有决定作用：线上什么都没有，线下什么都有。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Water table joins a native word for water to a word borrowed from Latin through French. The architectural sense is older than the groundwater sense.","cn":"water table 把本族的「水」与一个经法语借自拉丁语的词组合起来。建筑义比地下水义更早。"},"items":[{"era":"OLD ENGLISH WÆTER","en":"Wæter continues Proto-Germanic *watōr and belongs to the same Indo-European family as Greek hydōr.","cn":"wæter 延续原始日耳曼语 *watōr，与希腊语 hydōr 同属一个印欧词族。"},{"era":"LATIN TABULA","en":"Tabula meant a board, tablet or flat slab; Old French turned it into table, and English borrowed that form in the twelfth century.","cn":"tabula 指木板、书写板或平板；古法语把它变成 table，英语在十二世纪借入这一形式。"},{"era":"THE BUILDING SENSE","en":"In seventeenth-century building practice a table was a flat projecting course, and a water table was the ledge that threw rain off a wall.","cn":"在十七世纪的建筑做法中，table 指平直的挑出线脚，而 water table 就是把雨水甩离墙面的挑檐。"},{"era":"THE GROUNDWATER SENSE","en":"Nineteenth-century engineers borrowed the same phrase for the flat surface of water underground, which looked like a level table under the land.","cn":"十九世纪的工程师把这个短语借来指地下水的平坦水面，因为它看起来像地表之下的一张水平桌面。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first attestation of the groundwater sense): standard dictionaries do not fix the first use of water table in this sense, so the dating is approximate.","cn":"来源不确定（地下水义的首见年代）：通行辞书未确定该义项的首次使用，年代为约数。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group holds spelling and wording variants that are easy to mix up; the second holds neighbouring water levels that are not the same surface.","cn":"第一组是容易混淆的拼写与措辞变体；第二组是相邻但并不等同的水位概念。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"water-table","ipa":"/ˈwɔːtə ˌteɪbl/","tag":"hyphenated attributive","definition":"The hyphenated form used before a noun, as in water-table map; the noun itself is written open.","definitionCN":"作定语时用连字符，如潜水面图；名词本身则分写。"},{"word":"water level","ipa":"/ˈwɔːtə ˌlevl/","tag":"measured height","definition":"A measured height of water anywhere; it can be a river gauge or a well reading, not necessarily the saturated surface.","definitionCN":"任何地方测得的水面高度；可以是河水位或井中读数，不必是饱和带界面。"},{"word":"table water","ipa":"/ˈteɪbl ˌwɔːtə/","tag":"word order","definition":"Bottled drinking water served at table; the two words are reversed and the meaning is unrelated.","definitionCN":"餐桌上供应的瓶装饮用水；两词顺序颠倒，意义无关。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"phreatic surface","ipa":"/ˈfriː.æt.ɪk ˈsɜː.fɪs/","tag":"technical synonym","definition":"The formal geological name for the same surface, from Greek phrear, a well.","definitionCN":"同一界面的正式地质名称，出自希腊语 phrear「井」。"},{"word":"potentiometric surface","ipa":"/pəˌten.tʃi.əˈmet.rɪk ˈsɜː.fɪs/","tag":"confined case","definition":"The imaginary level to which water would rise in a confined aquifer, not the actual saturated top.","definitionCN":"承压含水层中水会升到的假想高度，而不是实际的饱和顶面。"},{"word":"capillary fringe","ipa":"/kəˈpɪl.ər.i frɪndʒ/","tag":"just above it","definition":"The moist zone held by surface tension immediately above the water table.","definitionCN":"紧贴潜水面之上、由表面张力维持的湿润带。"},{"word":"aquifer","ipa":"/ˈæk.wɪ.fə/","tag":"the layer, not the level","definition":"The rock body that contains the saturated zone; the table is only its top surface.","definitionCN":"包含饱和带的那块岩体；潜水面只是它的上表面。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: the two real words, the older building ledge, and the four things hydrologists actually measure at this line.","cn":"正常联想：两个真实词、较早的建筑挑檐，以及水文工作者真正在这一线上测量的四件事。"},"normal":[{"en":"Imagine a table under the ground: its flat top is the water table.","cn":"想象地下有一张桌子，它平坦的桌面就是潜水面。"},{"en":"The same phrase once named a stone ledge that threw rain off a wall, so both senses are about a level surface shedding water.","cn":"这个短语早年指名把雨水甩离墙面的石挑檐，所以两个义项都与「把水挡开的水平面」有关。"},{"en":"Above the line the pores hold air; below it they hold only water.","cn":"线上孔隙含空气，线下孔隙只含水。"},{"en":"A well is a window: the level inside it is the level outside.","cn":"一口井就是一扇窗：井内的水位就是井外的水位。"},{"en":"If the level falls year after year, the pump is taking more than the rain brings.","cn":"如果水位年年下降，说明抽水多于降雨补给。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Abstractly, the water table is an invisible horizontal rule drawn through the earth, dividing full from partly empty.","cn":"抽象地看，潜水面是一条穿过大地的隐形水平线，把「充满」与「半空」分开。"},{"en":"It is also a moving baseline: what counts as deep today may be shallow after a wet decade.","cn":"它也是一条移动的基准线：今天算深的，湿十年之后可能就算浅了。"},{"en":"Any system with a hidden threshold behaves this way: nothing shows until the level crosses it.","cn":"任何有隐形阈值的系统都是如此：在水位越过它之前，什么都看不出来。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The water table in the valley has dropped by more than a metre since the wells were drilled.","cn":"自这些井打成以来，谷地的地下水位下降了一米多。"},{"en":"Where the water table is shallow, foundations need extra waterproofing.","cn":"在地下水位浅的地方，地基需要额外防水。"},{"en":"Contour lines on the map join points of equal water table height.","cn":"图上的等值线把潜水面高度相同的点连起来。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「水（water）+ 桌面（table）」——地下有一张水平桌面，桌面就是水位 → 潜水面","word":"water table"},"root":"古英语 wæter「水」+ 经古法语借入的拉丁语 tabula「木板、平板」，十七世纪先指建筑挑檐，十九世纪转指地下水位面。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one level: the saturation boundary, its measurement in a well, its seasonal movement, its role in streams, its depth, its decline, the older building ledge, and finally any invisible threshold.","cn":"八个义项围绕同一条水位线展开：饱和界面、井中测量、季节升降、对溪流的补给、埋深、下降、较早的建筑挑檐，最后是任何隐形门槛。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a flat water line across a soil section, dark wet ground below it and lighter damp ground above.","cn":"核心意象：横贯土壤剖面的一条平水线，线下土色深而湿，线上较浅而微湿。"},"chain":["SURFACE","DRY PORES","SATURATION LINE","FULL PORES","PRESSURE LEVEL","BASE FLOW"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S2","en":"THE LINE ITSELF: a boundary in the pores, made visible by a well.","cn":"线本身：孔隙中的一条界线，借一口井显现出来。"},{"senses":"S3","en":"UP AND DOWN: recharge raises it, dry seasons lower it.","cn":"上下移动：补给抬升它，旱季压低它。"},{"senses":"S4 · S5","en":"WHERE IT MEETS THE WORLD: streams are fed at its outcrop, and its depth sets building limits.","cn":"与世界的接触：溪流在它的出露处获得补给，而它的埋深决定施工限制。"},{"senses":"S6","en":"A FALLING SIGNAL: a dropping level is the cheapest proof of over-pumping.","cn":"下降的信号：水位降低是过度抽水最廉价的证据。"},{"senses":"S7 · S8","en":"THE OLD LEDGE AND THE METAPHOR: a projecting course sheds water, and any hidden threshold borrows the image.","cn":"旧日挑檐与比喻：挑出的线脚甩开雨水，而任何隐形门槛都借用这个意象。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Water table is a two-word compound whose second member came into English through French and Latin, so its pieces carry two different histories.","cn":"water table 是双词复合词，第二个成分经法语与拉丁语进入英语，因此两个构件各自带着不同的历史。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin element is tabula, a board or flat slab, which also gives table, tablet, tabular and tabulate. The first element has no Latin root at all.","cn":"拉丁成分是 tabula「木板、平板」，它也衍生出 table、tablet、tabular 与 tabulate。第一个成分则完全没有拉丁词根。"},"items":[{"word":"water","structure":"water (Old English wæter)","meaning":"the liquid","meaningCN":"水","example":"Water fills the pores below the line.","exampleCN":"水充满线下的孔隙。"},{"word":"table","structure":"table (Latin tabula, board, through Old French)","meaning":"a flat surface or slab","meaningCN":"平面；平板","example":"The stone table stood in the courtyard.","exampleCN":"石桌立在院子里。"},{"word":"water table","structure":"water + table (compound noun)","meaning":"the upper surface of the saturated zone","meaningCN":"饱和带的上表面","example":"The water table rose after the storm.","exampleCN":"暴雨之后地下水位上升了。"},{"word":"tablet","structure":"table + -et (diminutive suffix)","meaning":"a small flat slab, hence a pill or a screen","meaningCN":"小片平板，引申为药片或平板设备","example":"She wrote on a clay tablet.","exampleCN":"她在泥板上写字。"},{"word":"tabular","structure":"tabula + -ar (relating to)","meaning":"arranged in rows and columns","meaningCN":"按行列排列的","example":"The data are presented in tabular form.","exampleCN":"数据以表格形式呈现。"},{"word":"tabulate","structure":"tabula + -ate (to make)","meaning":"to arrange data in a table","meaningCN":"把数据列成表","example":"They tabulated the well readings.","exampleCN":"他们把各井读数列成表。"},{"word":"phreatic","structure":"Greek phrear (well) + -ic (relating to)","meaning":"relating to the saturated zone","meaningCN":"与饱和带相关的","example":"The phreatic surface is another name for the water table.","exampleCN":"潜水面是 water table 的另一个名称。"},{"word":"groundwater","structure":"ground + water (native compound)","meaning":"the water below the table","meaningCN":"水位线以下的水","example":"Groundwater sits below the water table.","exampleCN":"地下水位于潜水面之下。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"tabula","structure":"tabula (Latin noun, board or tablet)","meaning":"a board, a flat slab, a written tablet","meaningCN":"木板；平板；书写板"},{"word":"tabella","structure":"tabula + -ella (Latin diminutive)","meaning":"a small tablet","meaningCN":"小写字板"},{"word":"tabulatum","structure":"tabula + -atum (Latin, a boarded structure)","meaning":"a floor or storey of boards","meaningCN":"木板的楼层"}]}},{"word":"infiltration","ipa_uk":"/ˌɪn.fɪlˈtreɪ.ʃən/","ipa_us":"/ˌɪn.fɪlˈtreɪ.ʃən/","definition_zh":"下渗；入渗；（军事或秘密的）渗透；浸润","definition_en":"the movement of water into soil or rock through the surface; also the secret entry of people or ideas into an organisation","core_image":"雨水停在松土表面，先是一层暗色湿斑，随后整片土色变深，水沿着颗粒缝隙向下走","scene":"雨停之后，坡上的水不再往低处流，而是一点点钻进松土，表层很快变暗。After the rain, infiltration carries the water into the loose soil instead of down the slope.","sceneCN":"这里 infiltration 指「地表水进入土壤或岩层的下渗过程」（第 1 个义项：水从地表穿过界面进入多孔介质）；句意为雨停后水不再沿坡流走，而是渗进松土。可辨识物件：坡面、湿斑、松土颗粒、下渗箭头。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"下渗；入渗（水文）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"渗透；潜入（军事、政治）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"浸润（医学）；浸渗（材料）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"infiltration rate","zh":"下渗率；入渗速率"},{"phrase":"infiltration capacity","zh":"下渗容量"},{"phrase":"soil infiltration","zh":"土壤下渗"},{"phrase":"infiltration trench","zh":"渗沟；入渗沟"},{"phrase":"infiltration of the enemy","zh":"对敌方的渗透"},{"phrase":"local infiltration","zh":"局部浸润（医学）"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"infiltration"},{"label":"复数（指多次渗透行动）","form":"infiltrations"},{"label":"动词","form":"infiltrate"},{"label":"形容词","form":"infiltrative"},{"label":"施动者名词","form":"infiltrator"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"infiltrate","pos":"v.","zh":"渗入；潜入"},{"word":"infiltrator","pos":"n.","zh":"渗透者；潜入者"},{"word":"infiltrative","pos":"adj.","zh":"浸润性的；渗透性的"},{"word":"infiltrant","pos":"n.","zh":"渗入物；浸润剂"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Water entering the soil","titleCN":"下渗：水从地表进入土壤","definition":"the process by which water on the ground surface passes into soil or rock","definitionCN":"地表水穿过界面进入土壤或岩石的过程","example":"Sandy soil allows rapid infiltration after a storm.","exampleCN":"沙质土壤在暴雨后下渗很快。","why":"The word begins with in-, movement inward, and that is exactly what happens at the surface: water stops being runoff and becomes soil water.","whyCN":"这个词以表示「向内」的 in- 开头，而地表发生的正是这件事：水不再是径流，而变成土壤水。"},{"no":"02","title":"Rate and capacity","titleCN":"下渗率与下渗容量","definition":"the speed at which water enters the soil, and the maximum the soil can absorb","definitionCN":"水进入土壤的速度，以及土壤能吸收的最大量","example":"Heavy rain exceeded the infiltration capacity, so water ran off.","exampleCN":"暴雨超过了下渗容量，因此水从地表流走。","why":"Once entry has a speed, it has a ceiling: the soil can only open so fast, and everything above that ceiling becomes surface flow.","whyCN":"一旦「进入」有了速度，也就有了上限：土壤开口只能那么快，超过上限的部分就变成地表流。"},{"no":"03","title":"Entry versus percolation","titleCN":"入渗与渗滤的区别","definition":"the entry step at the surface, distinguished from the downward travel of water inside the soil","definitionCN":"发生在表面的进入环节，区别于水在土壤内部的向下运移","example":"Infiltration is the door; percolation is the corridor behind it.","exampleCN":"入渗是门，渗滤是门后的走廊。","why":"Hydrology separates the two because a surface can be sealed at the door while the soil behind it is still able to transmit water.","whyCN":"水文学把两者分开，因为地表这道「门」可以被封住，而门后的土壤仍然能够导水。"},{"no":"04","title":"Military penetration","titleCN":"军事渗透：穿过防线","definition":"the movement of soldiers or units through or past an enemy line in small groups","definitionCN":"小股部队穿过或绕过敌方防线的行动","example":"The patrol reported infiltration across the border at night.","exampleCN":"巡逻队报告夜间有人越过边界渗透。","why":"The military sense keeps the physical image: small units pass through a line the way water passes through pores, without breaking it.","whyCN":"军事义保留了物理意象：小股部队像水穿过孔隙一样穿过多道防线，而不把防线打破。"},{"no":"05","title":"Secret entry into an organisation","titleCN":"秘密潜入：进入组织内部","definition":"the placement of agents or members inside a group in order to influence or report on it","definitionCN":"把人员安插进某个团体，以便影响它或向其汇报","example":"The infiltration of the union took years to uncover.","exampleCN":"对工会的渗透用了多年才被揭出。","why":"Here the pores are people: entry is gradual, quiet and distributed, which is why it is harder to detect than an outright attack.","whyCN":"这里孔隙换成了人：进入是渐进的、安静的、分散的，所以比正面攻击更难发现。"},{"no":"06","title":"Medical infiltration","titleCN":"医学浸润：药液或细胞渗进组织","definition":"the spread of a liquid or of cells into surrounding tissue","definitionCN":"液体或细胞扩散进入周围组织","example":"The dentist used local infiltration to numb the gum.","exampleCN":"牙医用局部浸润麻醉牙龈。","why":"The same inward movement appears in the body: an anaesthetic or a tumour spreads into tissue rather than staying in one place.","whyCN":"同样的向内运动也出现在身体里：麻醉剂或肿瘤扩散进入组织，而不是停留在一处。"},{"no":"07","title":"Ideas entering a system","titleCN":"观念渗透：慢慢进入一个体系","definition":"the gradual spread of ideas, terms or practices into an institution or culture","definitionCN":"观念、术语或做法逐渐进入某个机构或文化","example":"The infiltration of market language into schools worried the teachers.","exampleCN":"市场语言渗入学校让教师们感到担忧。","why":"Ideas travel like water: they do not announce themselves, they enter through many small openings and change the colour of everything.","whyCN":"观念的传播像水：它们不宣告自己，而是从许多小口进入，最后改变整体的颜色。"},{"no":"08","title":"Impregnation of a material","titleCN":"材料浸渗：把另一种物质灌进孔隙","definition":"the filling of pores in a solid with resin, oil or another substance","definitionCN":"用树脂、油或其他物质填充固体中的孔隙","example":"Vacuum infiltration sealed the porous casting.","exampleCN":"真空浸渗把多孔铸件封住了。","why":"In engineering the direction is deliberate: something is made to enter the pores on purpose, so the porous body becomes solid.","whyCN":"在工程中方向是被刻意安排的：让人为地把某种物质送入孔隙，使多孔体变得致密。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Infiltration is a Medieval Latin noun built on filtrum, a word for felt that Latin borrowed from Germanic. The English noun appears in the seventeenth century. Dates are approximate.","cn":"infiltration 是建立在中古拉丁语 filtrum 之上的名词，而 filtrum 是拉丁语从日耳曼语借来的「毛毡」一词。英语名词在十七世纪出现。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"MEDIEVAL LATIN FILTRUM","en":"Filtrum meant felt or a felt strainer; it is generally considered a borrowing into Latin from a Germanic word related to German Filz, felt.","cn":"filtrum 指毛毡或毛毡滤器；一般认为它是拉丁语从日耳曼语借入的词，与德语 Filz「毛毡」相关。"},{"era":"LATIN IN-","en":"The prefix in- marks movement into or onto something, as in influx and inject, and it directs the whole action inward.","cn":"前缀 in- 表示进入或向某物之上，如 influx 与 inject，它把整个动作指向内部。"},{"era":"INFILTRARE","en":"Medieval Latin infiltrare meant to filter in or to pass through a strainer, a technical verb of alchemy and medicine before it became a noun.","cn":"中古拉丁语 infiltrare 意为「滤入」或「穿过滤器」，在成为名词之前是炼金术与医学的技术动词。"},{"era":"SEVENTEENTH CENTURY ENGLISH","en":"English infiltration first names the action of filtering in, then extends to military penetration and later to soil water entering the ground.","cn":"英语 infiltration 先指「滤入」的动作，随后扩展到军事渗透，再后来用于水进入土壤。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first date of each sense): the earliest English use is not fixed precisely, and the order in which the military and hydrological senses developed is only approximately dated.","cn":"来源不确定（各义项首见年代）：最早的英语用例未被精确确定，军事义与水文义的发展先后也只有大致年代。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group holds words that differ by a letter or a suffix; the second holds the water processes most often confused with infiltration.","cn":"第一组是只差一个字母或后缀的词；第二组是常与下渗混淆的水文过程。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"infiltration","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɪlˈtreɪ.ʃən/","tag":"the noun","definition":"The action or result; the verb drops the -tion and ends in -ate.","definitionCN":"指动作或结果；动词去掉 -tion，以 -ate 结尾。"},{"word":"filtration","ipa":"/fɪlˈtreɪ.ʃən/","tag":"without in-","definition":"Filtering alone, with no inward prefix: the process of passing a liquid through a filter.","definitionCN":"只有「过滤」，没有表示向内的前缀：让液体通过滤器。"},{"word":"inflection","ipa":"/ɪnˈflek.ʃən/","tag":"one letter away","definition":"A change in the form of a word or in pitch; it has nothing to do with filtering.","definitionCN":"词形或语调的变化；与过滤毫无关系。"},{"word":"infiltrate","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɪlˈtreɪt/","tag":"the verb","definition":"To enter by passing through pores or lines; the noun for the action is infiltration.","definitionCN":"穿过孔隙或防线进入；其动作名词为 infiltration。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"percolation","ipa":"/ˌpɜː.kəˈleɪ.ʃən/","tag":"inside the soil","definition":"The downward movement of water within soil after it has already entered.","definitionCN":"水进入土壤之后在土体内部的向下运动。"},{"word":"runoff","ipa":"/ˈrʌn.ɒf/","tag":"the alternative","definition":"Water that fails to enter and flows over the surface instead.","definitionCN":"没能进入土壤、改沿地表流走的水。"},{"word":"seepage","ipa":"/ˈsiː.pɪdʒ/","tag":"slow leakage","definition":"Slow movement of water through soil, rock or a structure, often unintended.","definitionCN":"水缓慢穿过土壤、岩石或结构物，常为意外的渗漏。"},{"word":"penetration","ipa":"/ˌpen.əˈtreɪ.ʃən/","tag":"general entry","definition":"Entry into or through something by force or depth; it lacks the porous, gradual image.","definitionCN":"以力量或深度进入或穿过某物；没有多孔、渐进的高象。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: the felt strainer behind the word, the in- prefix, and the pair with percolation.","cn":"正常联想：词后的「毛毡滤器」、in- 前缀，以及与渗滤的成对关系。"},"normal":[{"en":"The root filtrum is felt: the first filters were mats of felt that let water through.","cn":"词根 filtrum 是毛毡：最早的滤器就是让水穿过的毛毡垫。"},{"en":"in- points inward, so infiltration is entry, not exit.","cn":"in- 指向内部，所以下渗是「进入」，不是「出去」。"},{"en":"Infiltration is the door, percolation is the corridor, runoff is the water that never got in.","cn":"下渗是门，渗滤是走廊，径流是从没进门的那些水。"},{"en":"In the army the line is the surface and small units are the water.","cn":"在军队里，防线就是地表，小股部队就是水。"},{"en":"The medical sense is the same word: an anaesthetic filters into the tissue around the needle.","cn":"医学义是同一个词：麻醉剂从针尖渗入周围组织。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Abstractly, infiltration is entry without breaking: the boundary stays intact while something passes through it.","cn":"抽象地看，渗透是不破坏边界的进入：某物穿过去，而边界仍然完整。"},{"en":"It is also a slow takeover: many small entries, each harmless, add up to a changed whole.","cn":"它也是一种缓慢的接管：许多单独无害的小进入，累积起来就改变了整体。"},{"en":"Anything that enters quietly through many openings — water, ideas, people — follows this pattern.","cn":"任何从许多开口安静进入的东西——水、观念、人——都遵循这个模式。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Compacted soil loses infiltration capacity and sends the rain straight to the river.","cn":"压实的土壤失去下渗能力，把雨水直接送进河里。"},{"en":"The report warned of infiltration by foreign agents in the ministry.","cn":"报告警告该部门存在外国人员的渗透。"},{"en":"Resin infiltration turned the porous metal part into a pressure-tight component.","cn":"树脂浸渗把多孔金属件变成了耐压部件。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「印（in，往里）+ 滤（filtr）+ 渗」——水往滤垫里进去 → 下渗、渗透","word":"infiltration"},"root":"中古拉丁语 in-「向内」+ filtrum「毛毡、滤垫」（拉丁语借自日耳曼语）+ -atio（动作名词后缀）。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses all describe entry through a boundary: water into soil, its rate, its contrast with percolation, soldiers through a line, agents into a group, fluid into tissue, ideas into a system, and resin into pores.","cn":"八个义项都描述「穿过边界进入」：水进入土壤、其速率、与渗滤的对照、士兵穿过防线、人员进入组织、液体进入组织、观念进入体系、树脂进入孔隙。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a dark wet patch spreading downward into loose soil, the surface itself unbroken.","cn":"核心意象：一块暗色湿斑向松土内部扩散，而地表本身并未破裂。"},"chain":["SURFACE","OPENING","ENTRY","INSIDE","SPREAD","CHANGED BODY"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S2","en":"THE DOOR AND ITS SPEED: entry happens at a rate, and the rate has a ceiling.","cn":"门与速度：进入有速率，而速率有上限。"},{"senses":"S3","en":"DOOR VERSUS CORRIDOR: infiltration is crossing the surface, percolation is travelling inside.","cn":"门与走廊：下渗是穿过表面，渗滤是在内部行进。"},{"senses":"S4 · S5","en":"LINES AND ORGANISATIONS: small units pass through defences; agents pass into groups.","cn":"防线与组织：小股部队穿过多道防线；人员进入团体。"},{"senses":"S6 · S7","en":"TISSUE AND CULTURE: fluid and ideas both spread quietly into a body.","cn":"组织与文化：液体与观念都安静地扩散进一个整体。"},{"senses":"S8","en":"DELIBERATE FILLING: engineering reverses the worry and makes entry useful.","cn":"有意的填充：工程把这种担忧反转，让进入变得有用。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Infiltration has a prefix, a root and a noun suffix, and the root also builds the everyday word filter.","cn":"infiltration 由前缀、词根与名词后缀构成，而这个词根也构成日常词 filter。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin base is filtrum, felt, which Latin took from Germanic. Its Latin verbs were infiltrare and its nouns infiltratio; English filter descends from the same Medieval Latin word.","cn":"拉丁语基础是 filtrum「毛毡」，这个词是拉丁语从日耳曼语借入的。其拉丁动词为 infiltrare，名词为 infiltratio；英语 filter 也出自同一中古拉丁词。"},"items":[{"word":"filter","structure":"filter (Medieval Latin filtrum, felt, from Germanic)","meaning":"a material or device that lets liquid through while holding back solids","meaningCN":"让液体通过而拦住固体的材料或装置","example":"The filter removed the sediment.","exampleCN":"滤器除去了沉积物。"},{"word":"filtration","structure":"filter + -ation (process)","meaning":"passing a liquid through a filter","meaningCN":"让液体通过滤器的过程","example":"Filtration cleaned the sample.","exampleCN":"过滤净化了样品。"},{"word":"filtrate","structure":"filtr- + -ate (that which has passed through)","meaning":"the liquid that has passed through a filter","meaningCN":"已经穿过过滤器的液体","example":"The filtrate was clear.","exampleCN":"滤液是清澈的。"},{"word":"infiltrate","structure":"in- (into) + filtr- (felt, filter) + -ate (verb)","meaning":"to enter through pores or lines","meaningCN":"穿过孔隙或防线进入","example":"Water infiltrates the sandy bank.","exampleCN":"水渗入沙质河岸。"},{"word":"infiltration","structure":"infiltrate + -ion (action or result)","meaning":"the act or result of entering through a boundary","meaningCN":"穿过边界进入的动作或结果","example":"Infiltration rose after the grass was removed.","exampleCN":"草被清除后下渗量上升。"},{"word":"infiltrator","structure":"infiltrate + -or (person who does)","meaning":"a person who enters secretly","meaningCN":"秘密进入的人","example":"The infiltrator posed as a volunteer.","exampleCN":"那名渗透者冒充志愿者。"},{"word":"infiltrative","structure":"infiltrate + -ive (tending to)","meaning":"tending to spread into surrounding tissue","meaningCN":"倾向于向周围组织扩散的","example":"The growth was infiltrative rather than contained.","exampleCN":"这个增生是浸润性的，而不是局限的。"},{"word":"percolation","structure":"per- (through) + colare (to strain) + -ion","meaning":"downward travel of water inside soil","meaningCN":"水在土体内部的向下运移","example":"Percolation continues long after infiltration stops.","exampleCN":"下渗停止之后，渗滤仍持续很久。"},{"word":"seepage","structure":"seep + -age (process or result)","meaning":"slow unintended leakage","meaningCN":"缓慢而非预期的渗漏","example":"Seepage weakened the dam's base.","exampleCN":"渗漏削弱了坝基。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"filtrum","structure":"filtrum (Medieval Latin, felt or strainer, from Germanic)","meaning":"felt; a felt strainer","meaningCN":"毛毡；毛毡滤器"},{"word":"infiltrare","structure":"in- + filtrare (Medieval Latin verb)","meaning":"to filter in, to pass through a strainer","meaningCN":"滤入；穿过滤器"},{"word":"infiltratio","structure":"infiltrare + -tio (Medieval Latin action noun)","meaning":"a filtering in","meaningCN":"滤入；渗入"}]}},{"word":"permeable","ipa_uk":"/ˈpɜː.mi.ə.bl̩/","ipa_us":"/ˈpɝː.mi.ə.bəl/","definition_zh":"可渗透的；能透水的；可穿过的","definition_en":"allowing liquids or gases to pass through the pores or structure","core_image":"一整块砂质铺装上，雨水落地即消失，旁边的黏土面上还积着一汪水","scene":"雨落在砂质路面上，水几秒之内就消失，而旁边的黏土路面还积着水。Rain vanishes within seconds on the permeable pavement beside the clay path.","sceneCN":"这里 permeable 指「允许液体或气体穿过其孔隙或结构的」（第 1 个义项：材料对流体开放、能通过而不被破坏）；句意为雨水在可渗透铺装上几秒内就消失，而旁边黏土路面仍有积水。可辨识物件：砂质铺装、积水、黏土面、下渗水痕。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"可渗透的；透水的"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"可穿过的；易受影响的（比喻）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"permeable membrane","zh":"半透膜；可透膜"},{"phrase":"permeable rock","zh":"透水岩层"},{"phrase":"permeable pavement","zh":"透水铺装"},{"phrase":"permeable to water","zh":"对水可渗透的"},{"phrase":"permeable boundary","zh":"可穿透边界"},{"phrase":"permeable soil","zh":"透水土壤"}],"forms":[{"label":"原级","form":"permeable"},{"label":"比较级","form":"more permeable"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most permeable"},{"label":"否定形式","form":"impermeable"},{"label":"名词","form":"permeability"},{"label":"动词","form":"permeate"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"permeability","pos":"n.","zh":"渗透性；渗透率；磁导率"},{"word":"impermeable","pos":"adj.","zh":"不可渗透的；不透水的"},{"word":"semipermeable","pos":"adj.","zh":"半透的"},{"word":"permeate","pos":"v.","zh":"渗透；弥漫"},{"word":"permeation","pos":"n.","zh":"渗透；弥漫"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Letting fluid through","titleCN":"允许流体通过","definition":"having pores or openings that allow a liquid or gas to pass through","definitionCN":"具有孔隙或开口，允许液体或气体穿过","example":"Sandstone is permeable; clay is not.","exampleCN":"砂岩是可渗透的，黏土则不是。","why":"The word names a property of the material, not an action: what matters is whether the path through it exists at all.","whyCN":"这个词命名的是材料的属性，不是动作：关键在于穿过它的路径是否存在。"},{"no":"02","title":"A water-bearing layer","titleCN":"透水岩层：能过水的地层","definition":"describing rock or sediment through which groundwater can move at a usable rate","definitionCN":"描述地下水能以可用速率通过的岩石或沉积层","example":"The permeable gravel admits water far faster than the silt beside it.","exampleCN":"这层透水砾石让水通过的速度远快于旁边的粉砂。","why":"In geology the property is what separates an aquifer from an aquiclude, so the adjective does classifying work.","whyCN":"在地质学中，这一属性把含水层与隔水层区分开，因此这个形容词承担分类功能。"},{"no":"03","title":"A semipermeable membrane","titleCN":"半透膜：选择性通过","definition":"allowing some substances but not others to cross, as in living cells","definitionCN":"允许某些物质通过而阻止另一些，如活细胞膜","example":"The cell's permeable membrane lets water in but holds the proteins.","exampleCN":"细胞膜让水进入，却把蛋白质留在里面。","why":"A membrane can be open to one thing and closed to another, so the adjective does not mean 'open to everything'.","whyCN":"膜可以对某物开放而对另一物关闭，因此这个形容词并不意味着「对一切都开放」。"},{"no":"04","title":"A boundary light can cross","titleCN":"可被光穿过的边界","definition":"transmitting radiation, sound or particles rather than blocking them","definitionCN":"能透过辐射、声音或粒子而不是阻挡它们","example":"The thin skin of the drum is permeable to sound.","exampleCN":"鼓面的薄皮可以透声。","why":"The same geometry applies to waves and particles: the boundary does not stop the flow if its structure lets it through.","whyCN":"同一几何关系也适用于波与粒子：只要结构允许通过，边界就挡不住这股流。"},{"no":"05","title":"Open to influence","titleCN":"易受影响的","definition":"easily entered or affected by ideas, feelings or outside pressure","definitionCN":"容易被观念、情绪或外界压力进入或影响的","example":"A young audience is permeable to new ideas.","exampleCN":"年轻的受众容易接受新观念。","why":"A mind with gaps in its defences behaves like porous rock: influence goes in without breaking anything.","whyCN":"防御有缝隙的心智就像多孔岩石：影响进入时并不打破什么。"},{"no":"06","title":"Breathable materials","titleCN":"透气透湿的材料","definition":"allowing air or moisture vapour through, as in technical clothing and building wraps","definitionCN":"允许空气或水汽通过，如功能服装与建筑膜材","example":"The jacket is permeable enough to let sweat escape.","exampleCN":"这件外套的透气性足以让汗气排出。","why":"Comfort depends on a selective flow: water vapour may leave while rain is still held out.","whyCN":"舒适依赖一种选择性流动：水汽可以出去，而雨水仍被挡住。"},{"no":"07","title":"An engineering boundary condition","titleCN":"工程中的可渗透边界条件","definition":"describing a model boundary through which fluid is allowed to flow","definitionCN":"描述允许流体通过的模型边界","example":"The model treats the riverbed as a permeable boundary.","exampleCN":"模型把河床处理为可渗透边界。","why":"In a simulation the adjective marks a condition: at this edge, water may cross, so pressure is not simply reflected back.","whyCN":"在模拟中这个形容词标记一种条件：在这个边界上水可以通过，因此压力不会简单地被反射回去。"},{"no":"08","title":"Abstract: not sealed off","titleCN":"比喻：不设防、不封闭","definition":"of a system or person, lacking a seal against outside flows","definitionCN":"指系统或人对外部的流入没有密封","example":"Borders are permeable to money in a way they are not to people.","exampleCN":"边界对资金的通透程度，与对人的并不相同。","why":"The word is neutral: a permeable border can be a virtue for trade and a weakness for security.","whyCN":"这个词是中性的：可渗透的边界对贸易可能是优点，对安全则可能是弱点。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Permeable is a Latin adjective taken into English through French: per- through, meare to pass, -bilis able to be. Dates are approximate.","cn":"permeable 是经法语进入英语的拉丁形容词：per- 表示「穿过」，meare 表示「通过」，-bilis 表示「能被……的」。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN MEARE","en":"Meare meant to go or pass, and it also underlies meatus, a passage, and the English word meatus used for a body opening.","cn":"meare 意为行走、通过，它也构成 meatus「通道」，英语解剖学中的 meatus 即指身体开口。"},{"era":"LATIN PER-","en":"Per- marks movement through or across something, as in pervade and perforate, so the adjective already contains a direction.","cn":"per- 表示穿过或越过某物，如 pervade 与 perforate，因此这个形容词本身已含有方向。"},{"era":"PERMEABILIS","en":"Latin permeabilis meant that can be passed through, built from permeare, to pass through, plus the suffix -bilis.","cn":"拉丁语 permeabilis 意为「能被穿过的」，由 permeare「穿过」加后缀 -bilis 构成。"},{"era":"SIXTEENTH CENTURY ENGLISH","en":"English permeable appears in the sixteenth century, and its negative impermeable follows the same Latin model with in-.","cn":"英语 permeable 在十六世纪出现，其否定形式 impermeable 按同样的拉丁模式加 in- 构成。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first attestation and route): dictionaries differ on whether the English form came directly from Latin or through French perméable, and the earliest date is given only approximately.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代与借入路径）：辞书对英语形式是直接来自拉丁语还是经法语 perméable 传入说法不一，最早年代也只给约数。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group holds the related forms that differ only in ending; the second holds adjectives that sound similar but mean something else.","cn":"第一组是只在词尾上不同的相关形式；第二组是听起来相近、意思不同的形容词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"permeability","ipa":"/ˌpɜː.mi.əˈbɪl.ə.ti/","tag":"the noun","definition":"The property itself; the adjective describes a thing that has it.","definitionCN":"指属性本身；形容词则描述具有该属性的事物。"},{"word":"permeance","ipa":"/ˈpɜː.mi.əns/","tag":"the noun in magnetics","definition":"The magnetic equivalent of conductance; it is a quantity, not the adjective's head form.","definitionCN":"磁导的对应量；它是一个量，而不是该形容词的原形。"},{"word":"impermeable","ipa":"/ɪmˈpɜː.mi.ə.bl/","tag":"negated form","definition":"The same adjective with in- changed to im- before p: it means the exact opposite.","definitionCN":"同一形容词把 in- 在 p 前变为 im-：意思正好相反。"},{"word":"permeate","ipa":"/ˈpɜː.mi.eɪt/","tag":"the verb","definition":"To pass through and spread within; the adjective describes the capacity, the verb the event.","definitionCN":"穿过并在内部扩散；形容词说能力，动词说事件。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"porous","ipa":"/ˈpɔː.rəs/","tag":"holes, not necessarily connection","definition":"Full of pores; a porous material stores fluid but may not let it flow through.","definitionCN":"充满孔隙；多孔材料能存流体，却不一定能让它流过去。"},{"word":"pervious","ipa":"/ˈpɜː.vi.əs/","tag":"Latin synonym","definition":"A rarer word for allowing passage, built from Latin via, a way, rather than from meare.","definitionCN":"较少见的「可透过」同义词，由拉丁语 via「道路」构成，而非 meare。"},{"word":"transparent","ipa":"/trænsˈpær.ənt/","tag":"light only","definition":"Allowing light through so objects can be seen; it is not about liquids.","definitionCN":"允许光通过而能看见后面的物体；与液体无关。"},{"word":"absorbent","ipa":"/əˈbɔː.bənt/","tag":"taking in, not passing on","definition":"Taking fluid in and holding it; a permeable body lets fluid continue through.","definitionCN":"吸收流体并留在内部；可渗透体则让流体继续通过。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: the three Latin pieces, the paired negatives, and the useful contrast with porous.","cn":"正常联想：三个拉丁构件、成对的否定形式，以及同 porous 的有用对照。"},"normal":[{"en":"per- is through, meare is pass, -able is can: 'can be passed through'.","cn":"per- 是穿过，meare 是通过，-able 是能够：合起来就是「能被穿过」。"},{"en":"Before p, in- becomes im-, which is why the opposite is impermeable.","cn":"在 p 之前，in- 变为 im-，所以反义词是 impermeable。"},{"en":"-ability replaces -able: permeable gives permeability.","cn":"-ability 替换 -able：permeable 变出 permeability。"},{"en":"Porous is about holes; permeable is about holes that connect into a path.","cn":"porous 说的是有孔；permeable 说的是这些孔连成了通路。"},{"en":"A raincoat is impermeable to rain but permeable to sweat vapour — if it is well made.","cn":"一件好雨衣对雨水不可渗透，对汗气却可渗透。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Abstractly, permeable means the wall has doors, and impermeable means the wall has none.","cn":"抽象地看，permeable 意味着墙上有门，impermeable 意味着墙上没有门。"},{"en":"Permeability is a two-way property: it does not say whether crossing is good, only that crossing is possible.","cn":"可渗透性是一种双向属性：它不判断穿越是好是坏，只说明穿越是可能的。"},{"en":"Every defence is judged by this word: what it lets through defines it as much as what it keeps out.","cn":"每一种防御都用这个词来评判：它放行什么，与它挡住什么同样定义它。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The permeable layer lets rain reach the aquifer within hours.","cn":"透水层让雨水在数小时内到达含水层。"},{"en":"A membrane that is permeable to water but not to salt can desalinate seawater.","cn":"对水可渗透、对盐不可渗透的膜可以对海水脱盐。"},{"en":"The regime proved permeable to outside criticism only in its final year.","cn":"这个政权直到最后一年才对外界批评变得不那么封闭。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「泼（per，穿过）+ 米（mea，通过）+ 能（-able）」——水能穿过它 → 可渗透的","word":"permeable"},"root":"拉丁语 per-「穿过」+ meare「通过」+ -abilis「能被……的」。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one property: fluid crossing a material, the layer that classifies it, the selective membrane, the wave boundary, the open mind, the breathable fabric, the model edge, and finally any unsealed system.","cn":"八个义项围绕同一属性展开：流体穿过材料、用于分类的岩层、选择性膜、波边界、开放的心智、透气织物、模型边界，最后是任何未密封的系统。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: two pavements side by side, rain disappearing into one and pooling on the other.","cn":"核心意象：两块并排的铺装，雨在一边消失，在另一边积成水洼。"},"chain":["OUTSIDE","OPENING","PASSAGE","INSIDE","FLOW","EMERGENCE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S2","en":"THE PROPERTY AND ITS USE: the adjective describes a material, and geology uses it to sort layers.","cn":"属性与用途：这个形容词描述材料，地质学用它给岩层分类。"},{"senses":"S3 · S4","en":"SELECTIVE PASSAGE: membranes and boundaries admit some flows and refuse others.","cn":"选择性通过：膜与边界放行某些流，拒绝另一些。"},{"senses":"S5","en":"THE OPEN MIND: influence enters without breaking the person.","cn":"开放的心智：影响进入，而不使人破裂。"},{"senses":"S6 · S7","en":"ENGINEERED FLOW: clothing and models are designed around a chosen permeability.","cn":"被设计的流动：服装与模型都围绕选定的渗透性来设计。"},{"senses":"S8","en":"NO SEAL: a system is called permeable when nothing closes it off.","cn":"没有密封：当没有任何东西把系统封住时，就称它是可渗透的。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Permeable is built from a Latin prefix, a Latin verb and a Latin suffix, and the same three pieces build the whole family.","cn":"permeable 由拉丁前缀、拉丁动词与拉丁后缀构成，同一套三个构件也构成整个词族。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin base is meare, to pass, with per- through and -bilis able to be. Permeare and permeabilis supply the verb and the adjective; impermeabilis adds the negative prefix.","cn":"拉丁语基础是 meare「通过」，配 per-「穿过」与 -bilis「能被……的」。permeare 与 permeabilis 提供动词与形容词；impermeabilis 则加否定前缀。"},"items":[{"word":"permeate","structure":"per- (through) + meare (to pass) + -ate (verb)","meaning":"to pass through and spread within","meaningCN":"穿过并在内部扩散","example":"Salt permeated the whole block.","exampleCN":"盐分渗遍了整块材料。"},{"word":"permeation","structure":"permeate + -ion (action)","meaning":"the process of passing through","meaningCN":"穿过的过程","example":"Permeation is slow at low pressure.","exampleCN":"低压下渗透很慢。"},{"word":"permeable","structure":"per- + meare + -abilis (able to be)","meaning":"able to be passed through","meaningCN":"能被穿过的","example":"The bed is permeable to water.","exampleCN":"这一层对水是可渗透的。"},{"word":"permeability","structure":"permeable + -ity (quality)","meaning":"the quality of being passable","meaningCN":"可被穿过的性质","example":"Permeability falls as clay content rises.","exampleCN":"黏土含量升高时渗透性下降。"},{"word":"impermeable","structure":"im- (not) + permeable","meaning":"not able to be passed through","meaningCN":"不能被穿过的","example":"Impermeable clay seals the pond.","exampleCN":"不透水的黏土封住了池塘。"},{"word":"semipermeable","structure":"semi- (half) + permeable","meaning":"allowing only some substances through","meaningCN":"只允许某些物质通过","example":"A semipermeable membrane separates salt from water.","exampleCN":"半透膜把盐与水分开。"},{"word":"pervious","structure":"per- (through) + via (way) + -ous","meaning":"allowing passage, a synonym from a different root","meaningCN":"允许通过的，词根不同的同义词","example":"Pervious concrete absorbs rain.","exampleCN":"透水混凝土会吸收雨水。"},{"word":"porous","structure":"pore (Greek poros, passage) + -ous","meaning":"full of pores","meaningCN":"充满孔隙的","example":"Porous rock stores water but may not transmit it.","exampleCN":"多孔岩石能存水，却不一定能导水。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"meare","structure":"meare (Latin verb, to go or pass)","meaning":"to pass, to go","meaningCN":"通过；行走"},{"word":"permeare","structure":"per- (through) + meare (Latin verb)","meaning":"to pass through","meaningCN":"穿过"},{"word":"permeabilis","structure":"permeare + -bilis (Latin adjective)","meaning":"that can be passed through","meaningCN":"能被穿过的"}]}},{"word":"permeability","ipa_uk":"/ˌpɜː.mi.əˈbɪl.ə.ti/","ipa_us":"/ˌpɝː.mi.əˈbɪl.ə.t̬i/","definition_zh":"渗透性；渗透率；磁导率；（膜的）通透性","definition_en":"the degree to which a material allows a fluid, field or substance to pass through it","core_image":"两根并排的砂柱与黏土柱，同一压力下水面下降速度截然不同，刻度尺记录差距","scene":"同样的压力下，水在砂柱中下降得远比在黏土柱中快，仪器把这一差别记成数值。At equal pressure, water sinks much faster through the sand column, and the test reports that difference as permeability.","sceneCN":"这里 permeability 指「材料允许流体通过的程度」（第 1 个义项：以流量与压力差之比衡量的渗透能力）；句意为同一压力下水在砂柱中下降更快，试验把这一差别记为渗透性。可辨识物件：砂柱、黏土柱、水位刻度、压力装置。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"渗透性；渗透率（岩土）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"磁导率（物理）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"通透性（生物膜）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"permeability of the rock","zh":"岩石的渗透性"},{"phrase":"low permeability","zh":"低渗透性"},{"phrase":"relative permeability","zh":"相对渗透率"},{"phrase":"magnetic permeability","zh":"磁导率"},{"phrase":"membrane permeability","zh":"膜通透性"},{"phrase":"permeability test","zh":"渗透试验"}],"forms":[{"label":"通常形式（不可数）","form":"permeability"},{"label":"复数（指多种渗透性，罕用）","form":"permeabilities"},{"label":"形容词","form":"permeable"},{"label":"否定名词","form":"impermeability"},{"label":"动词","form":"permeate"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"permeable","pos":"adj.","zh":"可渗透的"},{"word":"impermeability","pos":"n.","zh":"不可渗透性；不透水性"},{"word":"permeate","pos":"v.","zh":"渗透；弥漫"},{"word":"permeameter","pos":"n.","zh":"渗透仪；磁导计"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The general property","titleCN":"渗透性：让流体通过的能力","definition":"the property of a material that allows a fluid to move through its pores or structure","definitionCN":"材料允许流体通过其孔隙或结构的属性","example":"The permeability of the soil decides how fast rain disappears.","exampleCN":"土壤的渗透性决定雨水消失得多快。","why":"This is the abstract noun of permeable: the adjective says a thing can be crossed, the noun names that capacity as a measurable quantity.","whyCN":"这是 permeable 的抽象名词：形容词说某物可被穿过，名词把这种能力命名为可测量的量。"},{"no":"02","title":"Permeability as a rock parameter","titleCN":"渗透率：达西定律中的参数","definition":"the coefficient in Darcy's law that expresses how readily a porous medium transmits a fluid","definitionCN":"达西定律中表示多孔介质导流难易程度的系数","example":"The core sample has a permeability of one darcy.","exampleCN":"岩芯样品的渗透率为一达西。","why":"Once flow is written as a law, the material needs a number in the equation, and that number is what the noun denotes in petroleum and hydrogeology.","whyCN":"一旦流动被写成定律，材料就必须在方程中有一个数值，而这个数值就是石油与水文地质中该名词所指。"},{"no":"03","title":"Hydraulic conductivity","titleCN":"渗透系数：工程上的传导度","definition":"the field-scale measure of how easily water moves through soil, combining the medium and the fluid","definitionCN":"在场地尺度上衡量水穿过土壤难易的指标，兼含介质与流体性质","example":"Engineers quote permeability as metres per second in the site report.","exampleCN":"工程师在场地报告中以米每秒给出渗透系数。","why":"Field practice needs a rate, not a pure material constant, so the same word is used for the combined quantity that predicts drawdown.","whyCN":"现场实践需要的是速率，而不是纯材料常数，因此同一个词也用来指能预测降深的综合量。"},{"no":"04","title":"Magnetic permeability","titleCN":"磁导率：材料对磁场的响应","definition":"the ratio of magnetic flux density to magnetic field strength in a medium","definitionCN":"介质中磁通密度与磁场强度之比","example":"Iron has a much higher permeability than air.","exampleCN":"铁的磁导率远高于空气。","why":"The concept transfers from water to fields: a medium either lets the influence pass easily or resists it.","whyCN":"这一概念从水迁移到场：介质要么让影响容易通过，要么对它有所抵抗。"},{"no":"05","title":"Membrane permeability","titleCN":"膜通透性：生物膜的选择性","definition":"the ease with which substances cross a cell membrane or artificial membrane","definitionCN":"物质穿过细胞膜或人工膜的难易程度","example":"Cold increases the permeability of the cell membrane.","exampleCN":"低温会提高细胞膜的通透性。","why":"In biology the property is selective and adjustable: the membrane changes what it lets through as conditions change.","whyCN":"在生物学中这一属性是选择性的、可调的：条件变化时膜会改变它放行的东西。"},{"no":"06","title":"Relative permeability","titleCN":"相对渗透率：多相共存时","definition":"the reduced permeability of one fluid when another fluid also occupies the pores","definitionCN":"当另一种流体也占据孔隙时，某一种流体的有效渗透率折减","example":"Relative permeability falls sharply as water fills the pores.","exampleCN":"水充满孔隙时，相对渗透率急剧下降。","why":"Two fluids compete for the same passages, so each one's ability to move depends on how much space the other has taken.","whyCN":"两种流体争夺同一批通道，因此每一种的流动能力都取决于另一种占去了多少空间。"},{"no":"07","title":"A classification index","titleCN":"岩土分类指标","definition":"a measured value used to classify soils and rocks for engineering design","definitionCN":"用于工程设计中的土石分类的实测值","example":"The consultant classified the site by permeability and grain size.","exampleCN":"顾问按渗透性与粒径对场地进行分类。","why":"A single number can sort materials into groups, so permeability becomes part of the vocabulary of classification rather than of flow alone.","whyCN":"一个数值就能把材料分成组，因此渗透性不只属于流动，也成了分类词汇的一部分。"},{"no":"08","title":"Abstract: susceptibility","titleCN":"比喻：易受影响的程度","definition":"the degree to which a system or person admits outside influence","definitionCN":"系统或人容纳外界影响的程度","example":"The committee's permeability to lobbyists became a public issue.","exampleCN":"委员会对游说者的易受影响程度成了公共议题。","why":"The measurement language carries over neatly: influence has a flow, defences have a resistance, and the ratio can be estimated.","whyCN":"测量语言可以整齐地迁移过来：影响有流量，防御有阻力，而两者的比值可以被估计。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Permeability is the abstract noun of permeable, formed with the Latin suffix -itas, which English renders as -ity. The technical senses were added later. Dates are approximate.","cn":"permeability 是 permeable 的抽象名词，用拉丁后缀 -itas 构成，英语作 -ity。技术义项是后来附加的。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN MEARE","en":"Meare, to pass, gives the core idea; the same verb underlies permeare, to pass through, and the noun meatus, a passage.","cn":"meare「通过」给出核心意思；同一动词构成 permeare「穿过」与名词 meatus「通道」。"},{"era":"LATIN -ITAS","en":"The suffix -itas named a quality, and French -ité and English -ity continue it, which is why the noun ends in -bility rather than -bleness.","cn":"后缀 -itas 命名一种性质，法语 -ité 与英语 -ity 延续了它，所以这个名词以 -bility 结尾，而不是 -bleness。"},{"era":"PERMEABILITAS","en":"Medieval Latin permeabilitas paired the adjective with the quality suffix, and English borrowed the pattern rather than inventing a new one.","cn":"中古拉丁语 permeabilitas 把形容词与性质后缀配对，英语沿用了这一模式，而非另造新形式。"},{"era":"PHYSICS AND ENGINEERING","en":"In the nineteenth century the word acquired precise measured senses in magnetism and in the flow of fluids through porous media.","cn":"十九世纪，这个词在磁学与流体穿过多孔介质的研究中获得了精确的测量义。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first technical use): the exact date when permeability was first used as a measured magnetic or hydraulic quantity is not fixed in standard references.","cn":"来源不确定（技术义首见）：permeability 首次作为可测的磁学量或水力量的确切年代未被通行资料确定。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group holds the derived forms that are easiest to mix up; the second holds quantities and properties that neighbour permeability without being the same measurement.","cn":"第一组是最易混淆的派生形式；第二组是与渗透性相邻但并非同一测量的量与属性。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"permeableness","ipa":"/ˈpɜː.mi.ə.bl.nəs/","tag":"native suffix","definition":"A rare synonym built with the native -ness; the technical noun uses the Latin -ity instead.","definitionCN":"用本族后缀 -ness 构成的罕用同义词；技术名词则用拉丁 -ity。"},{"word":"impermeability","ipa":"/ˌɪm.pɜː.mi.əˈbɪl.ə.ti/","tag":"negated noun","definition":"The same noun with im-, meaning the inability to be passed through.","definitionCN":"同一名词加 im-，表示不能被穿过。"},{"word":"perviousness","ipa":"/ˈpɜː.vi.əs.nəs/","tag":"different root","definition":"The quality of allowing passage, but built on Latin via, a way, not on meare.","definitionCN":"允许通过的性质，但构自拉丁语 via「道路」，而非 meare。"},{"word":"porosity","ipa":"/pəˈrɒs.ə.ti/","tag":"space, not flow","definition":"The fraction of the volume that is pore space; high porosity does not guarantee high permeability.","definitionCN":"孔隙所占的体积比例；孔隙率高并不保证渗透性高。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"conductivity","ipa":"/ˌkɒn.dʌkˈtɪv.ə.ti/","tag":"flow measure","definition":"The ability of a medium to carry a flow; hydraulic conductivity is permeability expressed with fluid properties included.","definitionCN":"介质输导流动的能力；水力传导度是包含流体性质后的渗透性表达。"},{"word":"transmissivity","ipa":"/ˌtræns.mɪˈsɪv.ə.ti/","tag":"layer thickness included","definition":"Permeability multiplied by the thickness of the aquifer, a property of the whole layer.","definitionCN":"渗透性乘以含水层厚度，是整个岩层的属性。"},{"word":"permittivity","ipa":"/ˌpɜː.mɪˈtɪv.ə.ti/","tag":"electric, not magnetic","definition":"The electric counterpart of magnetic permeability, describing a medium's response to an electric field.","definitionCN":"磁导率的电学对应量，描述介质对电场的响应。"},{"word":"susceptibility","ipa":"/səˈsep.tə.bɪl.ə.ti/","tag":"the abstract cousin","definition":"The degree of being affected; it shares the measurement frame but not the porous image.","definitionCN":"受影响的容易程度；它共享测量框架，但没有多孔意象。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: the -ity suffix, the four fields that borrow the word, and the real distinction from porosity.","cn":"正常联想：-ity 后缀、借用这个词的四个领域，以及与孔隙率的真实区别。"},"normal":[{"en":"-ity turns an adjective into a measurable quality, as in porosity and conductivity.","cn":"-ity 把形容词变成可测的性质，如孔隙率与传导度。"},{"en":"The word is used in four fields: soil water, petroleum, magnetism and cell membranes.","cn":"这个词用于四个领域：土壤水、石油、磁学与细胞膜。"},{"en":"Porosity asks how much empty space there is; permeability asks whether the spaces connect.","cn":"孔隙率问有多少空隙；渗透性问这些空隙是否连通。"},{"en":"In Darcy's law the permeability is the material's own number, with the fluid accounted separately.","cn":"在达西定律中，渗透率是材料自身的数值，流体性质另行计入。"},{"en":"Relative permeability exists because two fluids cannot both use the whole pore space.","cn":"相对渗透率之所以存在，是因为两种流体无法同时占满全部孔隙。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Abstractly, permeability is the ratio of what gets through to what pushes: a measure of openness under pressure.","cn":"抽象地看，渗透性是「通过的量」与「推动的力」之比：压力下开放程度的度量。"},{"en":"It is a property that only appears in relation: the same wall is permeable to air and sealed to water.","cn":"它是一种只在关系中显现的属性：同一堵墙对空气开放，对水却密封。"},{"en":"Any boundary can be described this way, which is why the word slips so easily from rock to law and to people.","cn":"任何边界都可以这样描述，所以这个词能轻易从岩石滑向法律与人。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Permeability, not porosity, controls how quickly a well can be refilled.","cn":"决定一口井能多快回水的是渗透性，而不是孔隙率。"},{"en":"The membrane's permeability to potassium changes when the cell is excited.","cn":"细胞兴奋时，膜对钾的通透性会改变。"},{"en":"Steel's high magnetic permeability is why it is used in transformer cores.","cn":"钢的高磁导率正是它被用于变压器铁芯的原因。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「泼米啊（permea）+ 比例（-bility）」——水能穿过去多少，要用数值量出来 → 渗透性","word":"permeability"},"root":"拉丁语 per-「穿过」+ meare「通过」+ -itas（性质后缀，英语作 -ity）。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses measure one capacity: the general property, the rock constant, the field rate, the magnetic ratio, the membrane's selectivity, the multi-fluid case, the classification index, and finally the susceptibility of a system.","cn":"八个义项都在度量同一种能力：一般属性、岩石常数、场地速率、磁学比值、膜的选择性、多流体情形、分类指标，最后是系统的易受影响程度。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: two columns under one pressure, water falling fast in sand and slowly in clay.","cn":"核心意象：同一压力下的两根柱子，水在砂中落得快、在黏土中落得慢。"},"chain":["PRESSURE","MEDIUM","PASSAGE","THROUGHPUT","RATIO","MEASURED VALUE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S2","en":"PROPERTY AND CONSTANT: the capacity becomes a number in Darcy's law.","cn":"属性与常数：这种能力在达西定律中变成一个数值。"},{"senses":"S3","en":"FIELD RATE: engineers need metres per second, so the constant is combined with the fluid.","cn":"场地速率：工程师需要米每秒，于是常数与流体性质合并。"},{"senses":"S4","en":"FIELD VERSION: magnetism reuses the same ratio for a different medium.","cn":"场论版本：磁学把同一比值用于另一种介质。"},{"senses":"S5 · S6","en":"SELECTIVITY AND COMPETITION: membranes choose, and two fluids share the same pores.","cn":"选择与竞争：膜做选择，而两种流体共用同一批孔隙。"},{"senses":"S7 · S8","en":"INDEX AND METAPHOR: the number classifies materials, and the same number rates openness in people and institutions.","cn":"指标与比喻：这个数值给材料分类，也用同一数值评价人与机构的开放程度。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Permeability shares its stem with permeable and adds the Latin quality suffix; the family is regular enough to predict each member.","cn":"permeability 与 permeable 共享词干，并加上拉丁性质后缀；这个词族足够规则，可以预测每个成员。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The stem is Latin meare, to pass, with per- through. The quality suffix -itas appears in English as -ity, and the same pattern produces conductivity and porosity.","cn":"词干是拉丁语 meare「通过」，配 per-「穿过」。性质后缀 -itas 在英语中作 -ity，同一模式也构成 conductivity 与 porosity。"},"items":[{"word":"permeable","structure":"per- + meare + -abilis","meaning":"able to be passed through","meaningCN":"能被穿过的","example":"Sand is permeable to water.","exampleCN":"沙子对水是可渗透的。"},{"word":"permeability","structure":"permeable + -ity (quality)","meaning":"the quality of being passable","meaningCN":"可被穿过的性质","example":"Permeability is measured in darcies.","exampleCN":"渗透率以达西为单位测量。"},{"word":"impermeability","structure":"im- (not) + permeability","meaning":"the quality of not being passable","meaningCN":"不可被穿过的性质","example":"The clay's impermeability keeps the pond full.","exampleCN":"黏土的不透水性让池塘蓄得住水。"},{"word":"permeate","structure":"per- + meare + -ate","meaning":"to pass through and spread","meaningCN":"穿过并扩散","example":"Water permeated the sandstone.","exampleCN":"水渗入了砂岩。"},{"word":"permeameter","structure":"permea- + -meter (measuring device)","meaning":"an instrument for measuring permeability","meaningCN":"测量渗透性的仪器","example":"The permeameter tests each core sample.","exampleCN":"渗透仪测试每一块岩芯样品。"},{"word":"porosity","structure":"porous + -ity (quality)","meaning":"the share of volume that is pore space","meaningCN":"孔隙所占的体积份额","example":"Porosity is high but permeability is low in this shale.","exampleCN":"这种页岩孔隙率高，但渗透性低。"},{"word":"conductivity","structure":"conduct + -ivity (quality)","meaning":"the ability to carry a flow","meaningCN":"输导流动的能力","example":"Hydraulic conductivity includes the fluid's viscosity.","exampleCN":"水力传导度包含流体的黏度。"},{"word":"transmissivity","structure":"transmit + -ivity (quality)","meaning":"permeability times aquifer thickness","meaningCN":"渗透性乘以含水层厚度","example":"Transmissivity describes the whole layer.","exampleCN":"导水系数描述的是整个岩层。"},{"word":"permittivity","structure":"permit + -ivity (quality)","meaning":"the electric analogue of magnetic permeability","meaningCN":"磁导率的电学对应量","example":"Permittivity governs charge in a medium.","exampleCN":"介电常数决定介质中的电荷行为。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"meare","structure":"meare (Latin verb, to pass)","meaning":"to pass","meaningCN":"通过"},{"word":"permeabilis","structure":"per- + meare + -bilis (Latin adjective)","meaning":"passable","meaningCN":"可穿过的"},{"word":"permeabilitas","structure":"permeabilis + -itas (Medieval Latin noun)","meaning":"passableness, the quality of being passable","meaningCN":"可穿过的性质"}]}},{"word":"impermeable","ipa_uk":"/ɪmˈpɜː.mi.ə.bl̩/","ipa_us":"/ɪmˈpɝː.mi.ə.bəl/","definition_zh":"不可渗透的；不透水的；不受影响的","definition_en":"not allowing a liquid or gas to pass through; also not open to influence","core_image":"黏土压实的池底上积着一层水，水面平静，几小时过去也没有一滴渗下去","scene":"雨落在黏土压实的池底上，水停成一片，几个小时也渗不下去。Rain gathers on the clay-lined pond bottom because the compacted layer is impermeable.","sceneCN":"这里 impermeable 指「不允许液体或气体穿过其结构的」（第 1 个义项：材料对流体封闭、不形成通路）；句意为雨水积在黏土衬砌的池底，因为压实的这一层不透水。可辨识物件：池底黏土、积水、水面反光、岸边草。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"不可渗透的；不透水的"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"不受影响的；听不进劝的（比喻）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"impermeable layer","zh":"不透水层；隔水层"},{"phrase":"impermeable membrane","zh":"不透膜"},{"phrase":"impermeable clay","zh":"不透水黏土"},{"phrase":"impermeable to water","zh":"对水不可渗透的"},{"phrase":"impermeable liner","zh":"防渗衬层"},{"phrase":"impermeable surface","zh":"不透水面"}],"forms":[{"label":"原级","form":"impermeable"},{"label":"比较级","form":"more impermeable"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most impermeable"},{"label":"肯定形式","form":"permeable"},{"label":"名词","form":"impermeability"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"impermeability","pos":"n.","zh":"不可渗透性；不透水性"},{"word":"impermeably","pos":"adv.","zh":"不可渗透地（罕用）"},{"word":"impermeant","pos":"adj.","zh":"不能透入的（生物膜用语，罕用）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Closed to fluid","titleCN":"对流体封闭","definition":"having a structure that does not permit water, air or another fluid to pass through","definitionCN":"结构不允许水、空气或其他流体穿过","example":"The liner is impermeable, so the pond holds water all year.","exampleCN":"衬层不透水，所以池塘全年蓄得住水。","why":"The negative prefix does not mean 'hard' but 'no passage': the material's pores are absent, closed or unconnected.","whyCN":"这个否定前缀并非表示「坚硬」，而是表示「没有通路」：材料的孔隙不存在、闭合或不连通。"},{"no":"02","title":"The confining layer","titleCN":"隔水层：把水挡在下面","definition":"a rock or soil layer that blocks the vertical movement of groundwater","definitionCN":"阻止地下水垂向运移的岩石或土层","example":"A bed of impermeable clay seals the aquifer below.","exampleCN":"一层不透水黏土把下面的含水层封住。","why":"Geology needs an opposite to aquifer, and this adjective supplies it: what cannot transmit water can still confine it.","whyCN":"地质学需要一个与含水层相对的概念，而这个形容词正好提供：不能导水的层仍然能封住水。"},{"no":"03","title":"Clothing and packaging","titleCN":"不透气的衣物与包装","definition":"describing fabrics or wrappings that block liquid water or water vapour","definitionCN":"描述阻挡液态水或水汽的织物或包装","example":"The impermeable wrapper kept the sample dry in the rain.","exampleCN":"不透水的包装让样品在雨中保持干燥。","why":"In daily use the barrier is usually against rain or moisture, so the property is valued rather than criticised.","whyCN":"在日常使用中，这道屏障通常是挡雨或挡潮，因此这一属性被看重，而不是被批评。"},{"no":"04","title":"A physical barrier","titleCN":"不可穿透的物理边界","definition":"not permitting another medium, wave or particle to cross","definitionCN":"不允许另一种介质、波或粒子穿过","example":"The lead sheet is impermeable to X-rays.","exampleCN":"铅板对 X 射线是不可穿透的。","why":"The same adjective covers any barrier whose structure stops a flow, whether the flow is water, gas or radiation.","whyCN":"同一形容词涵盖一切以结构阻挡流动的屏障，无论流动是水、气体还是辐射。"},{"no":"05","title":"Not open to influence","titleCN":"不受影响；听不进劝","definition":"refusing to be affected by argument, criticism or new ideas","definitionCN":"不接受论证、批评或新观念的影响","example":"He remained impermeable to every warning.","exampleCN":"他对所有警告都无动于衷。","why":"A mind imagined as a sealed surface cannot be entered; the metaphor turns a material property into a character judgement.","whyCN":"把心智想象成密封表面，就无法进入；这个比喻把材料属性变成了性格判断。"},{"no":"06","title":"Sealed containment","titleCN":"密封与封存","definition":"describing containers or enclosures that keep a substance from escaping","definitionCN":"描述防止物质逸出的容器或围护结构","example":"The waste is stored in impermeable drums.","exampleCN":"废料存放在不透水的桶里。","why":"Containment is the reverse direction of the same property: nothing gets in, and nothing gets out.","whyCN":"封存是同一属性的反方向：什么都进不来，也什么都出不去。"},{"no":"07","title":"An engineering boundary condition","titleCN":"工程中的不透水边界条件","definition":"describing a model boundary across which no flow is permitted","definitionCN":"描述不允许流动穿过的模型边界","example":"The model sets the bedrock as an impermeable boundary.","exampleCN":"模型把基岩设为不透水边界。","why":"In simulation the adjective marks a zero-flow condition, so water is reflected rather than transmitted.","whyCN":"在模拟中这个形容词标记零流量条件，因此水被反射而不是透过。"},{"no":"08","title":"Abstract: a closed system","titleCN":"比喻：封闭的系统","definition":"of a system or group, refusing entry to outside people, information or change","definitionCN":"指系统或群体拒绝外部人员、信息或变化进入","example":"An impermeable institution learns nothing from its own failures.","exampleCN":"一个封闭的机构无法从自身的失败中学到任何东西。","why":"The image is neutral in physics and negative in society: no passage means no contamination, but also no exchange.","whyCN":"这个意象在物理上是中性的，在社会上却是负面的：没有通道意味着没有污染，也意味着没有交流。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Impermeable is the Latin negative of permeable: in- becomes im- before p, and the rest of the word is unchanged. Dates are approximate.","cn":"impermeable 是 permeable 的拉丁否定形式：in- 在 p 前变为 im-，其余部分不变。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN IN-","en":"The negative prefix in- means not; before p, b and m it assimilates to im-, which is why the word begins with im- rather than in-.","cn":"否定前缀 in- 意为「不」；在 p、b、m 之前它同化为 im-，所以这个词以 im- 开头而不是 in-。"},{"era":"LATIN MEARE","en":"Meare, to pass, supplies the middle of the word, and permeare, to pass through, is the verb behind the positive adjective.","cn":"meare「通过」提供词的中段，而 permeare「穿过」是肯定形容词背后的动词。"},{"era":"IMPERMEABILIS","en":"Latin impermeabilis stated that something cannot be passed through; the form is a regular negated adjective, not an irregular coinage.","cn":"拉丁语 impermeabilis 表示某物不能被穿过；这是规则的否定形容词，并非不规则新造词。"},{"era":"ENGLISH USE","en":"English impermeable appears in the seventeenth century, first of physical barriers and later of layers, wrappings and finally people.","cn":"英语 impermeable 在十七世纪出现，先指物理屏障，后来指岩层、包装，最后用于人。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first attestation): standard dictionaries give only approximate dates for the first English use, and the order in which the technical senses appeared is not precisely fixed.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：通行辞书只给出英语首次使用的约数，各技术义项出现的先后也未被精确确定。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group holds the forms that differ only by prefix or ending; the second holds words that mean resistant or closed but are not about passage.","cn":"第一组是只在前后缀上不同的形式；第二组是表示「抵抗」或「封闭」但并不涉及穿过的词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"permeable","ipa":"/ˈpɜː.mi.ə.bl/","tag":"the positive form","definition":"The same adjective without the negative prefix; the two are exact opposites.","definitionCN":"去掉否定前缀的同一形容词；两者正好相反。"},{"word":"impervious","ipa":"/ɪmˈpɜː.vi.əs/","tag":"different root","definition":"Also meaning 'not allowing passage', but built on Latin via, a way, not on meare.","definitionCN":"同样表示「不允许通过」，但构自拉丁语 via「道路」，而非 meare。"},{"word":"impermeability","ipa":"/ˌɪm.pɜː.mi.əˈbɪl.ə.ti/","tag":"the noun","definition":"The property named as a noun; the adjective describes the object that has it.","definitionCN":"以名词形式命名的属性；形容词描述具有该属性的物体。"},{"word":"impermeably","ipa":"/ɪmˈpɜː.mi.ə.bli/","tag":"the adverb","definition":"The rare adverb form, used of a surface that seals something off.","definitionCN":"罕用的副词形式，用于描述把某物封住的表面。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"waterproof","ipa":"/ˈwɔː.tə.pruːf/","tag":"everyday word","definition":"Not letting water in, said of clothes and covers; it is practical rather than technical.","definitionCN":"不让水进入，用于衣物与遮盖物；偏实用而非技术。"},{"word":"sealed","ipa":"/siːld/","tag":"closed by a barrier","definition":"Closed against entry by a physical seal; the closure is made, not inherent.","definitionCN":"用实物封条封闭入口；封闭是被做出的，而非材料固有。"},{"word":"resistant","ipa":"/rɪˈzɪs.tənt/","tag":"opposing, not blocking","definition":"Withstanding an effect without necessarily blocking passage.","definitionCN":"能承受某种作用，但不一定阻断通过。"},{"word":"impenetrable","ipa":"/ɪmˈpen.ɪ.trə.bl/","tag":"cannot be entered","definition":"Impossible to enter or pierce, usually by force; it stresses entry, not flow.","definitionCN":"无法进入或刺穿，通常指凭力量；强调进入，而非流动。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: the im- assimilation, the exact pair with permeable, and the three places the word is used.","cn":"正常联想：im- 的同化、与 permeable 的精确配对，以及这个词被使用的三个场所。"},"normal":[{"en":"im- is in- before p, so impermeable is simply in- plus permeable.","cn":"im- 就是 p 前的 in-，所以 impermeable 就是 in- 加 permeable。"},{"en":"permeable and impermeable are exact opposites, like a door open and a door locked.","cn":"permeable 与 impermeable 正好相反，就像门开着与门锁着。"},{"en":"Geology pairs aquifer with aquiclude, and permeable with impermeable, in the same breath.","cn":"在地质学中，含水层与隔水层、可渗透与不可渗透总是成对出现。"},{"en":"A pond lined with clay holds water for the same reason a raincoat holds out rain.","cn":"黏土衬砌的池塘能蓄水，与雨衣能挡雨，道理相同。"},{"en":"The metaphor is easy: a person who hears no argument is a surface nothing can get through.","cn":"这个比喻很直接：听不进任何论证的人，就是什么也穿不过去的表面。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Abstractly, impermeable is a boundary with no doors, which protects and isolates in equal measure.","cn":"抽象地看，impermeable 是一堵没有门的边界，保护与隔绝的程度相同。"},{"en":"It is the mirror of permeability: every measure of openness has a measure of closure.","cn":"它是渗透性的镜像：每一个开放度都有一个相应的封闭度。"},{"en":"Systems choose one or the other by purpose: a bottle should be closed, a school should not.","cn":"系统按目的选择其一：瓶子应当密封，学校则不应当。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"An impermeable cap over the landfill keeps rainwater from entering the waste.","cn":"填埋场上不透水的封盖阻止雨水进入废物。"},{"en":"Some rocks are porous but impermeable, because the pores do not connect.","cn":"有些岩石多孔却不可渗透，因为孔隙并不连通。"},{"en":"Years of success had made the management impermeable to criticism.","cn":"多年的成功让管理层听不进批评。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「硬泼（im-，不）+ 米啊（permea，穿过）」——水穿不过去 → 不可渗透的","word":"impermeable"},"root":"拉丁语 in-（在 p 前作 im-，表示否定）+ permeabilis「可穿过的」。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one closed surface: no passage for water, a confining layer, rainproof cloth, a radiation barrier, a closed mind, sealed containment, a zero-flow boundary, and finally an isolated system.","cn":"八个义项围绕同一个封闭表面展开：水不能通过、隔水层、挡雨织物、辐射屏障、封闭的心智、密封封存、零流量边界，最后是孤立的系统。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a clay-lined pond bottom with a still sheet of water on it, nothing draining away.","cn":"核心意象：黏土衬砌的池底上停着一层静水，没有任何下渗。"},"chain":["OUTSIDE FLUID","SURFACE","NO PORE","BLOCKED PATH","HELD WATER","SEALED SYSTEM"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1","en":"NO PASSAGE: the defining fact is the absence of a connected path.","cn":"没有通路：定义性的事实是缺少连通的路径。"},{"senses":"S2 · S7","en":"CONFINEMENT AND MODELLING: the layer holds water down, and models record it as zero flow.","cn":"封闭与建模：这一层把水挡在下面，模型把它记为零流量。"},{"senses":"S3 · S4","en":"EVERYDAY BARRIERS: cloth against rain, lead against rays.","cn":"日常屏障：布挡雨，铅挡射线。"},{"senses":"S5","en":"THE CLOSED MIND: a person imagined as a surface nothing enters.","cn":"封闭的心智：把一个人想象成什么都进不去的表面。"},{"senses":"S6 · S8","en":"CONTAINMENT AND ISOLATION: nothing escapes, and nothing is exchanged.","cn":"封存与孤立：什么都出不去，也没有任何交换。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Impermeable is the negated twin of permeable, so the whole family can be read by adding or removing im-.","cn":"impermeable 是 permeable 的否定孪生词，因此整个词族可以通过加减 im- 来读。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin basis is meare, to pass, with per- through and -bilis able to be; impermeabilis simply prefixes the negative in-. Standard Latin also had impervius from via, a way, a parallel formation.","cn":"拉丁语基础是 meare「通过」，配 per-「穿过」与 -bilis「能被……的」；impermeabilis 只是在前加否定 in-。标准拉丁语另有由 via「道路」构成的 impervius，属并行构词。"},"items":[{"word":"permeable","structure":"per- + meare + -abilis","meaning":"able to be passed through","meaningCN":"能被穿过的","example":"The sand is permeable.","exampleCN":"沙子是可渗透的。"},{"word":"impermeable","structure":"im- (not) + permeable","meaning":"not able to be passed through","meaningCN":"不能被穿过的","example":"The clay is impermeable.","exampleCN":"黏土是不可渗透的。"},{"word":"impermeability","structure":"impermeable + -ity (quality)","meaning":"the quality of blocking passage","meaningCN":"阻断通过的性质","example":"Impermeability is tested with a falling-head apparatus.","exampleCN":"不透水性用变水头装置测试。"},{"word":"impermeably","structure":"impermeable + -ly (in the manner of)","meaning":"in a way that blocks passage","meaningCN":"以阻断通过的方式","example":"The membrane sealed impermeably against the frame.","exampleCN":"膜与框架之间封得不透水。"},{"word":"impervious","structure":"im- (not) + via (way) + -ous","meaning":"not allowing passage, from a different root","meaningCN":"不允许通过，词根不同","example":"The surface is impervious to rain.","exampleCN":"这个表面对雨是不可透过的。"},{"word":"permeate","structure":"per- + meare + -ate","meaning":"to pass through","meaningCN":"穿过","example":"Water permeates the sand.","exampleCN":"水穿过沙子。"},{"word":"waterproof","structure":"water + proof (proof against)","meaning":"resistant to water","meaningCN":"防水的","example":"The waterproof cover protected the sample.","exampleCN":"防水罩保护了样品。"},{"word":"seal","structure":"seal (Old French seel, from Latin sigillum, a small mark)","meaning":"to close against passage","meaningCN":"封闭以阻止通过","example":"Seal the jar before storing it.","exampleCN":"储存前把罐子封好。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"permeabilis","structure":"per- + meare + -bilis (Latin adjective)","meaning":"passable","meaningCN":"可穿过的"},{"word":"impermeabilis","structure":"in- + permeabilis (Latin adjective)","meaning":"not passable","meaningCN":"不可穿过的"},{"word":"impervius","structure":"in- + via (way) + -us (Latin adjective)","meaning":"not to be passed through, a parallel formation","meaningCN":"不可穿过的，属并行构词"}]}},{"word":"runoff","ipa_uk":"/ˈrʌn.ɒf/","ipa_us":"/ˈrʌn.ɔːf/","definition_zh":"径流；降水沿地表流走的水；决胜投票","definition_en":"water that flows over the land surface instead of entering the soil; also a final decisive vote","core_image":"暴雨打在光秃的坡面上，水连成薄片往下冲，土面被划出一道道细沟","scene":"暴雨过后，水从光秃的坡面直接冲进沟里，把土冲成一道道细沟。After the storm, runoff cut small gullies down the bare slope.","sceneCN":"这里 runoff 指「降水未能下渗、沿地表流走的水」（第 1 个义项：地表径流这一水文过程及其水量）；句意为暴雨之后径流在裸露坡面上冲出细沟。可辨识物件：坡面、流痕、细沟、坡底沟渠。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"径流；地表流水（不可数）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"决选；第二轮投票（美式）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"surface runoff","zh":"地表径流"},{"phrase":"runoff water","zh":"径流水"},{"phrase":"storm runoff","zh":"暴雨径流"},{"phrase":"agricultural runoff","zh":"农业径流"},{"phrase":"runoff election","zh":"决选；第二轮选举"},{"phrase":"reduce runoff","zh":"减少径流"}],"forms":[{"label":"通常形式（不可数，指水）","form":"runoff"},{"label":"复数（指多次径流事件，罕用）","form":"runoffs"},{"label":"动词短语（原形）","form":"run off"},{"label":"动词短语过去式","form":"ran off"},{"label":"动词短语现在分词","form":"running off"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"run-off","pos":"n.","zh":"径流；决选（连字符拼写变体）"},{"word":"runoff-fed","pos":"adj.","zh":"由径流补给的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Water flowing off the land","titleCN":"地表径流：沿地面流走的水","definition":"precipitation that fails to infiltrate and instead flows over the ground surface","definitionCN":"未能下渗、改沿地表流动的降水","example":"Steep slopes send most of the rain into runoff.","exampleCN":"陡坡把大部分雨水变成径流。","why":"The verb phrase run off says exactly what happens: the water runs, and it runs off the surface rather than into it.","whyCN":"动词短语 run off 正好说清了过程：水流走，而且是从地面流走，不是流进地面。"},{"no":"02","title":"Storm runoff","titleCN":"暴雨径流：短时间的大量水","definition":"the concentrated flow produced by a heavy rainfall event","definitionCN":"一场强降雨产生的集中水流","example":"Storm runoff reached the bridge within twenty minutes.","exampleCN":"暴雨径流在二十分钟内就到了桥下。","why":"A storm overloads the soil's capacity, so the overflow becomes a fast, concentrated pulse rather than a slow seep.","whyCN":"暴雨使土壤容量超载，溢出的水便成为快速集中的脉冲，而不是缓慢的渗透。"},{"no":"03","title":"Runoff as a volume","titleCN":"径流量：流域出口的总量","definition":"the total volume or depth of water leaving a catchment by surface flow","definitionCN":"经地表流离开流域的总水量或水深","example":"Annual runoff from the basin fell after the forest regrew.","exampleCN":"森林恢复后，流域的年径流量下降。","why":"Once measured at a gauge, the process becomes a quantity in the water budget, and the same word names both.","whyCN":"一旦在测站被测量，这个过程就成了水量收支中的一个量，同一个词同时指过程与数量。"},{"no":"04","title":"Agricultural runoff","titleCN":"农业径流：带着肥料与农药走","definition":"surface flow from farmland that carries soil, nutrients and chemicals","definitionCN":"从农田流出并携带泥土、养分与化学物质的地表水","example":"Agricultural runoff feeds algal blooms downstream.","exampleCN":"农业径流在下游滋养藻类暴发。","why":"The water does not travel alone: whatever is soluble or suspended on the field goes with it, so runoff becomes a transport agent.","whyCN":"水不是独自旅行的：田里能溶解或悬浮的东西都随它走，因此径流成了一种搬运媒介。"},{"no":"05","title":"Urban runoff","titleCN":"城市径流：不透水面的产物","definition":"rain falling on roads, roofs and paving that cannot infiltrate and must be drained","definitionCN":"落在道路、屋顶与铺装上、无法下渗而必须排走的水","example":"Urban runoff overwhelms the drains in every summer storm.","exampleCN":"每逢夏季暴雨，城市径流都会让排水系统超载。","why":"Paving removes the soil's door, so almost all the rain becomes runoff and the drainage system must do the work the ground used to do.","whyCN":"铺装去掉了土壤这道门，几乎所有雨水都变成径流，排水系统只好承担地面原本承担的工作。"},{"no":"06","title":"Snowmelt runoff","titleCN":"融雪径流：春天的一次集中放水","definition":"water released when accumulated snow melts and flows over the surface","definitionCN":"积雪融化后沿地表流走的水","example":"Snowmelt runoff fills the reservoirs in April and May.","exampleCN":"融雪径流在四、五月蓄满水库。","why":"Snow is storage in solid form, so its melt converts a winter reserve into a spring runoff pulse.","whyCN":"积雪是固态的蓄存，因此融雪把冬季的储备转换成春季的径流脉冲。"},{"no":"07","title":"The deciding vote","titleCN":"决选：第二轮投票","definition":"a second election held when no candidate won outright, or the vote that decides it","definitionCN":"无人直接胜出时举行的第二轮选举，或其决定性的投票","example":"The race went to a runoff in November.","exampleCN":"这场竞选在十一月进入决选。","why":"The political sense borrows the image of a surplus that has to be discharged: the first round fails to settle it, so a second flow decides.","whyCN":"政治义借用了「多余部分必须排走」的意象：第一轮没能定局，于是第二轮流动来做决定。"},{"no":"08","title":"Abstract: leakage of value","titleCN":"比喻：价值的外流","definition":"the loss of capital, talent or support out of a system that cannot retain it","definitionCN":"资本、人才或支持从无法留住它们的系统中流失","example":"Talent runoff followed the cuts in research funding.","exampleCN":"研究经费削减之后出现了人才外流。","why":"Runoff is what the system could not absorb; applied to people and money, the word describes the same failure to retain.","whyCN":"径流是系统没能吸收的部分；用于人与钱时，描述的是同一种留不住。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Runoff is a native English verb phrase turned into a noun. The water sense is nineteenth-century; the election sense is American and much later. Dates are approximate.","cn":"runoff 是由英语本族动词短语转成的名词。水的义项属十九世纪，选举义为美式用法，年代晚得多。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"OLD ENGLISH RUNNAN","en":"Runnan meant to run, and its past tense ran and participle running are irregular remnants of an old strong verb.","cn":"runnan 意为跑，其过去式 ran 与分词 running 是古老强变化动词的不规则遗留。"},{"era":"OLD ENGLISH OF","en":"Of here is the adverb meaning away or off, not the modern preposition of possession, so the phrase means 'run away'.","cn":"这里的 of 是表示「离开」的副词，而不是现代表示所属的介词，因此短语意为「跑开」。"},{"era":"THE VERB PHRASE","en":"To run off is recorded from the sixteenth century in the plain sense of flowing or escaping away from a place.","cn":"run off 这一动词短语自十六世纪有记载，本义就是「流走、跑离某处」。"},{"era":"THE NOUN","en":"In the nineteenth century engineers turned the phrase into a noun for the water that runs off a catchment, and the spelling became one word.","cn":"十九世纪，工程师把这个短语转为名词，指从流域流走的水，拼写也合并成一个词。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first dates of the two noun senses): dictionaries give only approximate dates for the water sense and for the American election sense, so the sequence here is an estimate.","cn":"来源不确定（两个名词义的首见年代）：辞书对水义与美式选举义都只给出约数，此处的先后只是估计。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group holds spelling and wording neighbours; the second holds water terms that overlap with runoff without being the same process.","cn":"第一组是拼写与措辞上的近邻；第二组是与径流交叠但并非同一过程的水文词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"run-off","ipa":"/ˈrʌn.ɒf/","tag":"hyphenated variant","definition":"The hyphenated spelling, still used in some publications and in the election sense.","definitionCN":"连字符拼写，仍见于部分出版物，也见于选举义。"},{"word":"run off","ipa":"/rʌn ˈɒf/","tag":"the verb phrase","definition":"Two words with stress on off: the verb meaning to flow away or to leave quickly.","definitionCN":"分写的两个词，重音在 off：动词义为流走或迅速离开。"},{"word":"runaway","ipa":"/ˈrʌn.ə.weɪ/","tag":"different second element","definition":"Someone or something that has escaped control; the second element is away, not off.","definitionCN":"失去控制的人或物；第二个成分是 away，不是 off。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"surface runoff","ipa":"/ˈsɜː.fɪs ˈrʌn.ɒf/","tag":"the explicit form","definition":"The same flow named by its surface, used to distinguish it from subsurface flow.","definitionCN":"同一股水流以「地表」明示，用来与地下流区分。"},{"word":"overland flow","ipa":"/ˈəʊ.və.lænd fləʊ/","tag":"hydrology synonym","definition":"The technical name for unchannelled sheet flow before it gathers into streams.","definitionCN":"尚未汇入溪流、未形成沟道前的片状水流的技术名称。"},{"word":"discharge","ipa":"/dɪsˈtʃɑːdʒ/","tag":"the measured outflow","definition":"The volume of water passing a point per unit time; runoff is the supply, discharge is the measured result.","definitionCN":"单位时间内通过某断面的水量；径流是来源，流量是测量结果。"},{"word":"infiltration","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɪlˈtreɪ.ʃən/","tag":"the opposite path","definition":"Water entering the soil, the fate that runoff does not take.","definitionCN":"水进入土壤，是径流没有走的那条路。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: the verb phrase behind the noun, the of that means off, and the two fields that borrow it.","cn":"正常联想：名词背后的动词短语、表示「离开」的 of，以及借用它的两个领域。"},"normal":[{"en":"run + off is readable: the water runs off the land instead of into it.","cn":"run 加 off 一看就懂：水从地面跑走，而不是跑进去。"},{"en":"Here of means off, not 'belonging to', so the phrase is 'run away', not 'run of'.","cn":"这里的 of 是「离开」，不是「属于」，所以短语是「跑开」，不是「跑……的」。"},{"en":"runoff is to a catchment what overflow is to a bucket.","cn":"径流之于流域，就像溢流之于水桶。"},{"en":"The election sense uses the same picture: the first round overflows and a second round settles it.","cn":"选举义用同一幅图景：第一轮「溢出」，第二轮才定局。"},{"en":"Paving turns rain into runoff, because it removes the door into the soil.","cn":"铺装把雨水变成径流，因为它去掉了进入土壤的那道门。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Abstractly, runoff is what a system cannot absorb, and therefore what it must get rid of.","cn":"抽象地看，径流是系统无法吸收、因而必须排走的部分。"},{"en":"It is a surplus with a direction: everything not held goes downhill and takes something with it.","cn":"它是有方向的剩余：留不住的部分都往低处走，并且带走一些东西。"},{"en":"Capital, talent and votes all have a runoff when the container is too full or too smooth to hold them.","cn":"当容器太满或太光滑而留不住时，资本、人才与选票都会出现「外流」。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Grass strips along the field edge trap sediment from runoff before it reaches the stream.","cn":"田边的草带在径流到达溪流前拦住其中的泥沙。"},{"en":"The city now taxes impermeable surfaces to pay for runoff control.","cn":"这座城市现在对不透水面征税，以支付径流控制费用。"},{"en":"The primary was so close that it forced a runoff three weeks later.","cn":"初选票数太接近，三周后不得不举行决选。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「跑（run）+ 离开（off）」——水从地面上跑掉了 → 径流","word":"runoff"},"root":"英语本族动词短语 run off「跑开、流走」名词化而成，十九世纪起用于水文。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow water that never enters the ground: the process, its storm form, its measured volume, its farm and city versions, its snowmelt form, the political second round, and finally any leakage of value.","cn":"八个义项都沿着「没能进入地面的水」展开：过程本身、暴雨形式、测得的量、农业与城市版本、融雪形式、政治上的第二轮，最后是任何价值外流。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a sheet of rainwater sliding down a bare slope, cutting thin channels as it goes.","cn":"核心意象：一层雨水沿裸坡下滑，边流边划出细沟。"},"chain":["RAIN","SOIL FULL","SURFACE FLOW","CONCENTRATION","CHANNEL","OUTFLOW"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1","en":"REFUSED ENTRY: the water runs because the ground will not take it.","cn":"被拒之门外：水之所以流走，是因为地面不接受它。"},{"senses":"S2 · S3","en":"EVENT AND AMOUNT: a storm makes a pulse, and a gauge turns it into a volume.","cn":"事件与数量：暴雨造出脉冲，测站把它变成水量。"},{"senses":"S4 · S5","en":"CARRIER: on farms and streets the water travels with whatever it picks up.","cn":"搬运者：在农田与街道上，水带着所拾取的一切同行。"},{"senses":"S6","en":"DELAYED RELEASE: snow holds water, and melt discharges it in spring.","cn":"延迟释放：雪把水存住，融化时在春天放出。"},{"senses":"S7 · S8","en":"SURPLUS DECIDES AND LEAVES: a second vote settles what the first could not, and value escapes when nothing retains it.","cn":"剩余做决定并离开：第二轮投票定下第一轮定不了的事，而留不住时价值便外流。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Runoff is a native verb phrase made into a noun, so its members are ordinary English words rather than bound affixes.","cn":"runoff 是由本族动词短语转成的名词，因此它的构件是普通英语词，而不是黏着词缀。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"No Latin root is involved: both members are native English. The Latin-based vocabulary of the topic enters through separate words such as infiltration and discharge, which are treated elsewhere.","cn":"这里不涉及拉丁词根：两个成分都是英语本族词。这一主题的拉丁语词汇通过 infiltration 与 discharge 等独立词进入，另作处理。"},"items":[{"word":"run","structure":"run (Old English rinnan, to flow or run)","meaning":"to flow or move quickly","meaningCN":"流动或快速移动","example":"The stream runs through the meadow.","exampleCN":"溪流穿过草地。"},{"word":"off","structure":"off (adverb of separation, away from a place)","meaning":"away from a surface or place","meaningCN":"离开某个表面或地方","example":"The rain slid off the roof.","exampleCN":"雨水从屋顶滑落。"},{"word":"runoff","structure":"run + off (verb phrase turned noun)","meaning":"water that runs off the land","meaningCN":"从地面流走的水","example":"Runoff filled the ditch.","exampleCN":"径流灌满了沟渠。"},{"word":"run-off","structure":"run + off (hyphenated spelling)","meaning":"the same noun in hyphenated form","meaningCN":"同一名词的连字符形式","example":"The run-off vote is next week.","exampleCN":"决选投票在下周。"},{"word":"runaway","structure":"run + away (verb phrase turned adjective or noun)","meaning":"having escaped control","meaningCN":"失去控制的","example":"A runaway train rolled downhill.","exampleCN":"一辆失控的列车滑下山坡。"},{"word":"overflow","structure":"over- (too much) + flow","meaning":"to flow over the edge of a container","meaningCN":"从容器边缘溢出","example":"The tank overflowed after the storm.","exampleCN":"暴雨之后水罐溢出了。"},{"word":"outflow","structure":"out- (outward) + flow","meaning":"movement out of a system","meaningCN":"从系统向外流出的运动","example":"The lake's outflow feeds the river.","exampleCN":"湖泊的出水补给这条河。"},{"word":"drainage","structure":"drain + -age (process or system)","meaning":"the removal of surplus water","meaningCN":"排除多余的水","example":"Drainage keeps the field workable.","exampleCN":"排水让田地在雨后仍可耕作。"}],"latinEntries":[]}},{"word":"surface runoff","ipa_uk":"/ˈsɜː.fɪs ˈrʌn.ɒf/","ipa_us":"/ˈsɝː.fɪs ˈrʌn.ɔːf/","definition_zh":"地表径流；降水在未下渗时沿地表流动形成的水流","definition_en":"precipitation that flows over the land surface without infiltrating, before it joins a channel","core_image":"沥青停车场上雨水连成薄片，沿边沟汇聚，几分钟内全部涌入雨水口","scene":"铺了沥青的停车场一落雨就几乎不吸水，水沿边沟汇进排水口。Paved parking lots shed surface runoff into the storm drains within minutes.","sceneCN":"这里 surface runoff 指「未下渗、沿地表面流动的水」（第 1 个义项：与地下流相对、发生在地表界面上的径流）；句意为铺装停车场把地表径流在几分钟内送入雨水口。可辨识物件：沥青面、边沟、雨水篦子、水膜。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"地表径流（不可数，水文用语）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"surface runoff water","zh":"地表径流水"},{"phrase":"surface runoff generation","zh":"地表径流生成"},{"phrase":"surface runoff coefficient","zh":"地表径流系数"},{"phrase":"reduce surface runoff","zh":"减少地表径流"},{"phrase":"surface runoff pollution","zh":"地表径流污染"}],"forms":[{"label":"通常形式（不可数）","form":"surface runoff"},{"label":"复数（指多次或多种径流事件）","form":"surface runoffs"},{"label":"简称","form":"runoff"},{"label":"同义术语（水文）","form":"overland flow"},{"label":"相关术语（地下流）","form":"subsurface flow"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"runoff","pos":"n.","zh":"径流（简称形式）"},{"word":"surface-runoff","pos":"adj.","zh":"地表径流的（作定语）"},{"word":"surface","pos":"n.","zh":"表面；地表"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The flow on the surface","titleCN":"地表上的流动：与地下流相对","definition":"water moving over the ground surface rather than through the soil","definitionCN":"在地表上移动、而非穿过土壤的水","example":"Surface runoff begins where rainfall exceeds the soil's capacity.","exampleCN":"地表径流从降雨超过土壤容量的那一刻开始。","why":"The two-word term fixes the location: this is the branch of runoff that stays on top, so it can be separated from what sinks.","whyCN":"这个双词术语固定了位置：这是停留在表面的那一支径流，因此可以与下渗部分分开。"},{"no":"02","title":"The storm pulse","titleCN":"暴雨脉冲：短时高强度","definition":"the rapid flow produced during intense rain before it reaches a channel","definitionCN":"强降雨期间产生、尚未到达沟道前的快速水流","example":"Surface runoff during the downpour exceeded the gutter's capacity.","exampleCN":"暴雨期间的地表径流超过了排水沟的容量。","why":"Intensity matters more than total depth: short heavy rain outpaces the surface, while gentle rain may never produce this flow at all.","whyCN":"强度比总量更重要：短时强雨超过了地表的吸收速度，而细雨可能根本不产生这种流。"},{"no":"03","title":"The urban version","titleCN":"城市版本：不透水面的产物","definition":"rain shed by roofs, roads and paving that must be drained artificially","definitionCN":"由屋顶、道路与铺装排出的雨水，必须靠人工排水","example":"Surface runoff from the new district doubled after the fields were paved.","exampleCN":"田地铺上路面后，新城区的地表径流翻了一倍。","why":"Paving replaces the soil's entry with a hard plane, so nearly all the rain has to travel sideways.","whyCN":"铺装用硬面取代了土壤的入口，因此几乎所有雨水都只能横向移动。"},{"no":"04","title":"The carrier of farm pollution","titleCN":"面源污染的载体","definition":"the flow that transports soil, fertiliser and pesticide from fields to water bodies","definitionCN":"把泥土、化肥与农药从农田搬到水体的那股水流","example":"Surface runoff carries nitrate from the fields into the lake.","exampleCN":"地表径流把农田的硝酸盐带进湖里。","why":"This flow is the main non-point route of pollution, because it starts everywhere on a field at once rather than at one pipe.","whyCN":"这股水流是面源污染的主要路径，因为它同时从田地的每一处开始，而不是出自一根管子。"},{"no":"05","title":"The erosion agent","titleCN":"侵蚀的动因","definition":"the flow whose energy detaches and carries soil particles downslope","definitionCN":"其能量把土粒剥离并带下坡的水流","example":"Surface runoff on the bare slope removed the topsoil in one season.","exampleCN":"裸坡上的地表径流在一个季节内带走了表土。","why":"Water only erodes when it moves as a sheet or in rills; once it is spread thin and slow, it carries nothing.","whyCN":"水只有以片流或细沟形式移动时才侵蚀；一旦铺得很薄、流得很慢，它就什么也搬不动。"},{"no":"06","title":"The basin's fast response","titleCN":"流域的快速响应","definition":"the part of a catchment's outflow that arrives quickly after rain","definitionCN":"降雨后迅速到达流域出口的那部分水量","example":"Surface runoff set the timing of the flood peak.","exampleCN":"地表径流决定了洪峰出现的时间。","why":"Flood forecasting separates the fast surface path from the slow subsurface path, because only the fast one explains a peak within hours.","whyCN":"洪水预报把快的地表路径与慢的地下路径分开，因为只有快路径能解释数小时内出现的洪峰。"},{"no":"07","title":"Rainwater management","titleCN":"雨水管理中的对象","definition":"the flow that green infrastructure tries to slow, spread or store","definitionCN":"绿色基础设施试图减缓、分散或储存的那股水流","example":"Rain gardens are designed to capture surface runoff before it reaches the drain.","exampleCN":"雨水花园的设计目的是在地表径流进入排水口前将其截住。","why":"Modern practice treats this flow as a resource to be detained rather than a waste to be piped away.","whyCN":"现代做法把这股水流当作应当滞留的资源，而不是应当用管道排走的废物。"},{"no":"08","title":"Abstract: what stays on the surface","titleCN":"比喻：停留在表面的那部分","definition":"a visible, easily moved portion of something that never enters the deeper system","definitionCN":"某事物中可见、易被带走、从未进入更深系统的那部分","example":"Most of the debate was surface runoff; the real change happened underground.","exampleCN":"这场争论大多是表层径流，真正的变化发生在地下。","why":"The image separates what is visible and fast from what is deep and slow, a distinction that fits many systems.","whyCN":"这个意象把可见而快速的部分与深层而缓慢的部分分开，这种区分适用于许多系统。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Surface runoff joins a Latin-derived word for the outer face to a native English verb phrase. The combination is a twentieth-century technical term. Dates are approximate.","cn":"surface runoff 把拉丁来源的「外表面」一词与英语本族动词短语组合起来。这个组合是二十世纪的技术术语。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN SUPERFICIES","en":"Superficies meant the outer face of a body, built from super, above, and facies, form or appearance; French surface and English surface descend from it.","cn":"superficies 指物体的外表面，由 super「在上方」与 facies「形状、外观」构成；法语 surface 与英语 surface 即由此而来。"},{"era":"LATIN FACIES","en":"Facies meant shape, face or appearance, not 'to make'; it is a different word from facere, and this is a common source of error.","cn":"facies 指形状、面容或外观，并非「制造」；它与 facere 是不同的词，此处常被误解。"},{"era":"NATIVE OFF","en":"The second half is the native verb phrase run off, whose off is an adverb of separation rather than a preposition.","cn":"后半部分是本族动词短语 run off，其中的 off 是表示分离的副词，而非介词。"},{"era":"TWENTIETH-CENTURY HYDROLOGY","en":"As catchments came to be modelled separately for surface and subsurface paths, the explicit two-word term became standard.","cn":"当流域开始把地表路径与地下路径分开建模时，这个明示的双词术语成为标准说法。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first attestation): no standard dictionary fixes the first use of the exact phrase surface runoff, so the dating here is an estimate.","cn":"来源不确定（首见年代）：没有通行辞书确定 surface runoff 这一确切短语的首次使用，此处年代只是估计。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group holds phrases that differ by one word; the second holds flow terms that are adjacent in the same system.","cn":"第一组是只差一个词的短语；第二组是同一系统中相邻的水流术语。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"subsurface runoff","ipa":"/ˌsʌbˈsɜː.fɪs ˈrʌn.ɒf/","tag":"the other path","definition":"Water that travels laterally below the surface; it is the counterpart, not a synonym.","definitionCN":"在地表以下横向移动的水；是对照项，不是同义词。"},{"word":"surface water","ipa":"/ˈsɜː.fɪs ˌwɔːtə/","tag":"the body, not the flow","definition":"Water standing or stored in rivers and lakes; runoff is the moving supply that reaches them.","definitionCN":"停留在河流湖泊中的水；径流是到达它们的流动补给。"},{"word":"overland flow","ipa":"/ˈəʊ.və.lænd fləʊ/","tag":"technical synonym","definition":"The same unchannelled flow, named from the land it crosses rather than the surface it uses.","definitionCN":"同一未成沟的水流，以其穿越的陆地命名，而非以其所在表面命名。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"runoff","ipa":"/ˈrʌn.ɒf/","tag":"the short form","definition":"The general term for water flowing off the land, of which the surface path is one branch.","definitionCN":"流离陆地的水的总称，地表路径是其中一支。"},{"word":"infiltration","ipa":"/ˌɪn.fɪlˈtreɪ.ʃən/","tag":"the competing fate","definition":"Water entering the soil; every drop goes to one path or the other.","definitionCN":"进入土壤的水；每一滴水都走向两者之一。"},{"word":"stormwater","ipa":"/ˈstɔːm.wɔː.tə/","tag":"managed rain","definition":"Rain and its runoff considered as a drainage problem in built areas.","definitionCN":"在建成区被当作排水问题处理的降雨及其径流。"},{"word":"base flow","ipa":"/beɪs fləʊ/","tag":"the slow part","definition":"The dry-weather flow fed by groundwater, the opposite timescale to surface runoff.","definitionCN":"由地下水补给的旱季流量，与地表径流的时间尺度相反。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: the two real words, the Latin facies behind surface, and the pairing with subsurface flow.","cn":"正常联想：两个真实词、surface 背后的拉丁语 facies，以及与地下流的成对关系。"},"normal":[{"en":"surface + runoff says where and what: the flow that stays on the outer face.","cn":"surface 加 runoff 同时说明位置与内容：停留在外表面的那股流。"},{"en":"surface comes from Latin superficies, super above plus facies face, so it is literally the 'upper face'.","cn":"surface 出自拉丁语 superficies，即 super「在上」加 facies「面」，字面就是「上面」。"},{"en":"facies means face or appearance, not 'make', so surface has nothing to do with factory.","cn":"facies 指面容或外观，不是「制造」，因此 surface 与 factory 无关。"},{"en":"The pair is surface runoff and subsurface flow: one over the ground, one through it.","cn":"成对的说法是地表径流与地下流：一个在地面之上，一个穿过地面。"},{"en":"Paving turns almost all rain into surface runoff, which is why cities flood faster than fields.","cn":"铺装把几乎所有雨水变成地表径流，所以城市比田野更容易内涝。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Abstractly, this term separates the visible fast layer from the hidden slow one.","cn":"抽象地看，这个术语把可见而快速的表层，与隐藏而缓慢的深层分开。"},{"en":"What stays on the surface is easy to see, easy to measure and easy to blame.","cn":"停留在表面的东西容易看见、容易测量，也容易被归咎。"},{"en":"Every system has a surface runoff: the part of its activity that never enters its depths.","cn":"每个系统都有它的「表层径流」：那部分从未进入深处的活动。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Surface runoff from the construction site silted up the stream for months.","cn":"工地产生的地表径流让这条溪流淤积了数月。"},{"en":"The model separates surface runoff from groundwater discharge in the annual budget.","cn":"该模型在年度收支中把地表径流与地下水排泄分开。"},{"en":"Wetlands slow surface runoff and let sediment settle before it reaches the lake.","cn":"湿地减缓地表径流，让泥沙在入湖前沉降。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「表面（surface）+ 跑掉（run off）」——只在地面表层跑掉的水 → 地表径流","word":"surface runoff"},"root":"拉丁语 superficies「外表面」（super「在上」+ facies「面」）经法语 surface 进入英语 + 本族动词短语 run off。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one visible flow: the surface branch, its storm pulse, its urban form, its load of farm pollution, its erosion work, its basin response, its place in rainwater design, and finally any visible surplus.","cn":"八个义项围绕同一股可见水流展开：地表分支、暴雨脉冲、城市形态、携带的农业污染、侵蚀作用、流域响应、在雨水设计中的位置，最后是任何可见的剩余。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a film of rain sliding across asphalt into a gutter and through a drain grate.","cn":"核心意象：一层雨水滑过沥青面，汇入边沟并穿过雨水篦子。"},"chain":["RAIN","HARD SURFACE","NO ENTRY","SHEET FLOW","GUTTER","DRAIN"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S2","en":"LOCATION AND SPEED: the branch is defined by staying on top, and intensity sets its pace.","cn":"位置与速度：这一支因停留在表面而得名，而强度决定它的快慢。"},{"senses":"S3","en":"THE PAVED CITY: hard surfaces leave almost no other route.","cn":"铺装的城市：硬质表面几乎不留别的去处。"},{"senses":"S4 · S5","en":"CARRIER AND CUTTER: the flow moves fertiliser and also removes soil.","cn":"搬运与切割：这股流既搬走肥料，也削去土壤。"},{"senses":"S6 · S7","en":"FAST RESPONSE AND DESIGN: it sets flood timing, and green infrastructure tries to detain it.","cn":"快速响应与设计：它决定洪水时序，而绿色基础设施试图滞留它。"},{"senses":"S8","en":"VISIBLE SURPLUS: what never enters the depths stays on the face and moves quickly.","cn":"可见的剩余：从未进入深处的东西留在表面，移动得很快。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"The phrase mixes a Latin-derived noun with a native verb phrase, so it shows both layers of English vocabulary in one term.","cn":"这个短语把拉丁来源的名词与本族动词短语混在一起，因此在一个术语里同时显示英语词汇的两个层次。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin element is superficies, from super above and facies face; facies is not related to facere, to make. The second element has no Latin root at all.","cn":"拉丁成分是 superficies，由 super「在上」与 facies「面」构成；facies 与 facere「制造」并无关联。第二个成分完全没有拉丁词根。"},"items":[{"word":"surface","structure":"surface (French, from Latin superficies, super + facies)","meaning":"the outer face of a body","meaningCN":"物体的外表面","example":"Water gathered on the surface.","exampleCN":"水聚在表面上。"},{"word":"superficies","structure":"super- (above) + facies (form, face)","meaning":"the outer face","meaningCN":"外表面","example":"The Latin word survives in legal usage.","exampleCN":"这个拉丁词仍见于法律用语。"},{"word":"superficial","structure":"superficies + -al (relating to)","meaning":"of the surface only; shallow","meaningCN":"仅涉及表面的；浅的","example":"The damage was superficial.","exampleCN":"损坏只在表面。"},{"word":"run","structure":"run (native verb, to flow)","meaning":"to flow","meaningCN":"流动","example":"Water runs down the slope.","exampleCN":"水沿坡流下。"},{"word":"off","structure":"off (native adverb, away)","meaning":"away from a place","meaningCN":"离开某处","example":"The water ran off the roof.","exampleCN":"水从屋顶流走。"},{"word":"runoff","structure":"run + off (noun)","meaning":"water flowing off the land","meaningCN":"从陆地流走的水","example":"Runoff enters the ditch.","exampleCN":"径流进入沟渠。"},{"word":"surface runoff","structure":"surface + runoff","meaning":"the flow that stays on the surface","meaningCN":"停留在表面的水流","example":"Surface runoff reached the drain in minutes.","exampleCN":"地表径流几分钟内就到了排水口。"},{"word":"subsurface","structure":"sub- (under) + surface","meaning":"below the surface","meaningCN":"表面以下的","example":"Subsurface flow feeds the stream slowly.","exampleCN":"地下流缓慢地补给溪流。"},{"word":"stormwater","structure":"storm + water (native compound)","meaning":"rain and runoff in built areas","meaningCN":"建成区的降雨与径流","example":"Stormwater ponds detain the flow.","exampleCN":"雨水塘滞留住这股水流。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"superficies","structure":"super- (above) + facies (form, face)","meaning":"the outer surface of a body","meaningCN":"物体的外表面"},{"word":"facies","structure":"facies (Latin noun, form or appearance)","meaning":"form, face, appearance","meaningCN":"形状；面容；外观"},{"word":"super","structure":"super (Latin preposition and prefix, above)","meaning":"above, over","meaningCN":"在上方；超过"}]}},{"word":"drainage basin","ipa_uk":"/ˈdreɪ.nɪdʒ ˌbeɪ.sn/","ipa_us":"/ˈdreɪ.nɪdʒ ˌbeɪ.sən/","definition_zh":"流域；由分水岭围成、降水汇入同一河系的集水区域","definition_en":"the area of land bounded by divides whose rain and snowmelt drain into one river system","core_image":"四周山脊围出一只巨大的碗，碗底的河道把四面来的水收进一条出口","scene":"山谷四周的山脊把雨水分开，落在东侧的水进东河，落在西侧的水进西河。Ridges on every side divide the rain, and each drop stays inside its own drainage basin.","sceneCN":"这里 drainage basin 指「由分水岭围成、降水汇入同一河系的陆地区域」（第 1 个义项：以地形边界划定的汇水单元）；句意为四周山脊把雨水分开，每一滴水都留在各自的流域内。可辨识物件：山脊、谷地、两支河道、分水线。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"流域；集水盆地（水文）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"drainage basin area","zh":"流域面积"},{"phrase":"large drainage basin","zh":"大流域"},{"phrase":"drainage basin management","zh":"流域管理"},{"phrase":"drainage basin divide","zh":"流域分水岭"},{"phrase":"upper drainage basin","zh":"流域上游"},{"phrase":"drainage basin model","zh":"流域模型"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"drainage basin"},{"label":"复数","form":"drainage basins"},{"label":"同义术语（英式常用）","form":"catchment"},{"label":"同义术语（美式常用）","form":"watershed"},{"label":"相关术语（河系）","form":"river basin"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"basin","pos":"n.","zh":"盆地；流域；（器物）盆"},{"word":"subbasin","pos":"n.","zh":"子流域"},{"word":"drainage","pos":"n.","zh":"排水；水系"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The area that drains to one river","titleCN":"汇入同一河系的区域","definition":"all the land whose surface water reaches a single river system and its outlet","definitionCN":"其地表水最终到达同一河系及其出口的全部陆地","example":"The Amazon drainage basin covers several countries.","exampleCN":"亚马孙流域覆盖数个国家。","why":"The term is defined by an exit: land belongs to the basin if its water ends up at the same outlet, however far it travels.","whyCN":"这个术语由出口来定义：只要水最终到达同一个出口，无论走多远，那块地就属于该流域。"},{"no":"02","title":"An area bounded by divides","titleCN":"由分水岭围成的区域","definition":"the region enclosed by ridges or high ground that separate it from neighbouring basins","definitionCN":"由山脊或高地围起、与相邻流域分开的区域","example":"A low divide separates this basin from the one to the north.","exampleCN":"一道低矮的分水岭把这个流域与北面的流域分开。","why":"Water cannot choose, so the boundary is drawn where the slope reverses: on one side it goes here, on the other side it goes there.","whyCN":"水无法选择，因此边界画在坡向反转之处：一侧流向这里，另一侧流向那里。"},{"no":"03","title":"A measured area","titleCN":"有面积与属性的单元","definition":"the basin treated as a mapped unit with area, relief, soils and land cover","definitionCN":"被当作具有面积、地形、土壤与地表覆被的制图单元","example":"The basin covers four thousand square kilometres of mixed forest.","exampleCN":"这个流域覆盖四千平方公里的混交林。","why":"Once its boundary is drawn, the basin becomes a unit that can be measured, compared and assigned a single water budget.","whyCN":"边界一旦画出，流域就成了可测量、可比较并能配一份水量收支的单元。"},{"no":"04","title":"Nested subbasins","titleCN":"嵌套的子流域","definition":"the hierarchy in which a large basin is made of smaller basins joined by tributaries","definitionCN":"大流域由支流连接的小流域组成的层级结构","example":"Each tributary has its own subbasin within the larger basin.","exampleCN":"每条支流在大流域内都有自己的子流域。","why":"Because a basin is defined by an outlet, cutting the outlet upstream produces another basin inside the first, and so on down the hierarchy.","whyCN":"因为流域由出口定义，把出口向上游移动就会在第一个流域内部产生另一个流域，如此层层嵌套。"},{"no":"05","title":"A unit of hydrological response","titleCN":"水文响应单元","definition":"the area whose rainfall, soils and slopes produce a characteristic stream response","definitionCN":"其降雨、土壤与坡度产生特定河流响应过程的区域","example":"Forecasters divide the basin into response units for flood modelling.","exampleCN":"预报人员把流域分成响应单元用于洪水模拟。","why":"Rain falls everywhere at once, but the outlet sees only the sum; the basin is the container that turns scattered rain into one hydrograph.","whyCN":"雨同时落在各处，而出口只看到总和；流域就是把分散的降雨变成一条过程线的容器。"},{"no":"06","title":"A management unit","titleCN":"管理单元","definition":"the administrative area used for water allocation, pollution control and planning","definitionCN":"用于水量分配、污染控制与规划的管理区域","example":"The new law makes the drainage basin the unit of water planning.","exampleCN":"新法律把流域作为水资源规划的单元。","why":"Water ignores political borders, so the basin offers the only boundary that matches the movement it is meant to govern.","whyCN":"水不理会政治边界，因此流域提供了唯一与其运动相符合的管理边界。"},{"no":"07","title":"A conveyor of material","titleCN":"物质输移的通道","definition":"the basin seen as a system that moves sediment, nutrients and pollutants downstream","definitionCN":"把泥沙、养分与污染物向下游输送的系统","example":"The basin delivers sediment to the delta every flood season.","exampleCN":"每个汛期流域都把泥沙送到三角洲。","why":"Every slope in the basin feeds the same channel network, so the basin also describes where material comes from and where it ends up.","whyCN":"流域内每一处坡面都汇入同一套河网，因此流域也描述了物质从哪里来、到哪里去。"},{"no":"08","title":"Abstract: an area of influence","titleCN":"比喻：影响的吸纳范围","definition":"any region or group whose activity flows toward one centre","definitionCN":"其活动都流向同一个中心的任何区域或群体","example":"The old port was the drainage basin of an entire hinterland.","exampleCN":"这座老港口是整个腹地资源的汇聚之处。","why":"The image generalises easily: whatever falls inside the divide ends up at one outlet, whether it is water, trade or attention.","whyCN":"这个意象很容易泛化：落在分水岭以内的一切最终都到一个出口，不论是水、贸易还是注意力。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Drainage basin joins a French-derived word for draining to a French-derived word for a bowl. Both routes are old, and parts of both are uncertain. Dates are approximate.","cn":"drainage basin 把法语来源的「排水」与法语来源的「盆」组合在一起。两条借入路径都很早，且各有不确定之处。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"OLD FRENCH DRAINER","en":"English drain comes from Old French drainer, to drain; the further origin is uncertain, with Germanic and native English explanations both proposed.","cn":"英语 drain 来自古法语 drainer「排水」；其更早来源不确定，日耳曼来源与本族英语来源两种解释都有人提出。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH BACIN","en":"Basin comes from Old French bacin, from Vulgar Latin *baccinum, a water vessel; the ultimate origin may be Gaulish and is not settled.","cn":"basin 来自古法语 bacin，再上溯到通俗拉丁语 *baccinum「水器」；其最终来源可能是高卢语，尚无定论。"},{"era":"DRAINAGE IN ENGLISH","en":"Drainage names the act or system of removing surplus water, a word of the eighteenth and nineteenth centuries in its modern technical sense.","cn":"drainage 指排除多余水的动作或系统，其现代技术义属十八、十九世纪。"},{"era":"THE COMPOUND TERM","en":"Drainage basin became the standard English term for a catchment in the nineteenth and twentieth centuries, alongside watershed in American use.","cn":"十九、二十世纪，drainage basin 成为集水区的标准英语术语，美式用法则并行使用 watershed。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (both etymologies and first date): the origin of drainer is disputed, the pre-Latin origin of baccinum is unsettled, and dictionaries give only approximate dates for the compound.","cn":"来源不确定（两条词源与首见年代）：drainer 的来源有争议，baccinum 的拉丁语之前来源无定论，辞书对该复合词也只给出约数。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group holds the three regional words for the same area; the second holds terms that name a part or a neighbour of the basin.","cn":"第一组是同一区域的三种地域性说法；第二组是流域的局部或邻近概念。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"catchment","ipa":"/ˈkætʃ.mənt/","tag":"British preference","definition":"The British term for the same area; in everyday use it can also mean the people a service serves.","definitionCN":"同一区域的英式说法；日常中也可指某项服务所覆盖的人群。"},{"word":"watershed","ipa":"/ˈwɔː.tə.ʃed/","tag":"American sense","definition":"In American English the whole basin; in British English the dividing ridge itself.","definitionCN":"美式指整个流域；英式则指分水岭本身。"},{"word":"river basin","ipa":"/ˈrɪ.və ˌbeɪ.sn/","tag":"same idea, named by the river","definition":"A near synonym that stresses the river system rather than the draining.","definitionCN":"几乎同义的表达，强调河系而非排水过程。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"divide","ipa":"/dɪˈvaɪd/","tag":"the boundary","definition":"The ridge that separates two basins; it is the edge, not the area.","definitionCN":"分开两个流域的山脊；是边缘，不是区域。"},{"word":"subbasin","ipa":"/ˈsʌb.beɪ.sn/","tag":"a part","definition":"A basin nested inside a larger one, drained by a tributary.","definitionCN":"嵌套在大流域内、由一条支流排水的小流域。"},{"word":"floodplain","ipa":"/ˈflʌd.pleɪn/","tag":"the low part","definition":"The land beside a river that floods; it lies inside the basin but is not the whole of it.","definitionCN":"河流旁会泛滥的陆地；它在流域之内，但不等于整个流域。"},{"word":"wetland","ipa":"/ˈwet.lænd/","tag":"a habitat","definition":"A saturated habitat within the basin, not a drainage unit.","definitionCN":"流域内的一类饱和生境，而不是排水单元。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: the bowl image, the three regional synonyms, and the outlet rule that defines the whole concept.","cn":"正常联想：碗的意象、三种地域同义词，以及定义整个概念的出口规则。"},"normal":[{"en":"A basin is a bowl, and a drainage basin is the bowl that collects rain for one river.","cn":"basin 是碗，drainage basin 就是为同一条河收集雨水的碗。"},{"en":"The rim of the bowl is the divide: stand on it, and rain goes one way or the other.","cn":"碗沿就是分水岭：站在上面，雨水不是往这边就是往那边。"},{"en":"Same area, three words: drainage basin, catchment, watershed.","cn":"同一片区域有三种说法：drainage basin、catchment、watershed。"},{"en":"The outlet defines the basin, so moving the outlet upstream creates a subbasin.","cn":"出口定义了流域，所以把出口上移就产生一个子流域。"},{"en":"Water crosses political borders, which is why basins, not provinces, are used for water planning.","cn":"水会越过政治边界，所以水资源规划用流域而非省份作单元。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Abstractly, a basin is any bounded region with one exit: everything inside must pass through the same gate.","cn":"抽象地看，流域是任何有单一出口的封闭区域：内部的一切都必须经过同一道门。"},{"en":"Its boundary is not a wall but a slope reversal, which makes it invisible on the ground yet decisive in the water.","cn":"它的边界不是墙，而是坡向的反转处，因此在地面上看不见，却决定了水的去向。"},{"en":"Any organisation with a single reporting point is organised like a basin, whether it knows it or not.","cn":"任何只有一个汇报出口的组织，无论自知与否，其结构都像一个流域。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The drainage basin of the river crosses three provinces.","cn":"这条河的流域跨越三个省。"},{"en":"Land clearing in the upper basin increased sediment at the outlet.","cn":"流域上游的清林增加了出口处的泥沙。"},{"en":"Every drainage basin has its own balance of rainfall, evaporation and discharge.","cn":"每个流域都有自己的降雨、蒸发与排泄平衡。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「排水（drainage）+ 盆（basin）」——把四周的雨水收进同一只盆里 → 流域","word":"drainage basin"},"root":"英语 drain「排水」（源自古法语 drainer）+ 古法语 bacin「盆」（上溯通俗拉丁语 *baccinum）。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one bowl: the area with a single outlet, its divide, its measured extent, its nested parts, its response to rain, its use in management, its role in moving material, and finally any region with one centre.","cn":"八个义项围绕同一只「碗」展开：只有一个出口的区域、它的分水岭、被测定的范围、嵌套的部分、对降雨的响应、管理中的用途、搬运物质的角色，最后是任何只有一个中心的区域。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a great bowl of ridges with one channel at the bottom, all rain inside flowing to that point.","cn":"核心意象：山脊围成的一只巨碗，碗底只有一条河道，碗内所有雨水都流向那一点。"},"chain":["RIDGE","SLOPE","CHANNEL","TRIBUTARY","OUTLET","DELTA"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S2","en":"AREA AND EDGE: one outlet defines the inside, and the slope reversal draws the edge.","cn":"区域与边缘：一个出口定义内部，坡向反转画出边缘。"},{"senses":"S3","en":"MEASURED UNIT: with a boundary, the basin gains area and a single budget.","cn":"测量单元：有了边界，流域就有了面积与单一收支。"},{"senses":"S4 · S5","en":"NESTING AND RESPONSE: subbasins nest by outlet, and each contributes to one hydrograph.","cn":"嵌套与响应：子流域按出口嵌套，各自汇入同一条过程线。"},{"senses":"S6","en":"GOVERNANCE: the basin is the boundary that matches water's movement.","cn":"治理：流域是与水的运动相符合的边界。"},{"senses":"S7 · S8","en":"CONVEYOR AND METAPHOR: material travels to one outlet, and any region with one centre borrows the image.","cn":"输送与比喻：物质流向一个出口，而任何只有一个中心的区域都借用这个意象。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Drainage basin is a two-word technical compound in which both members came into English through French, so the word shows a double borrowing.","cn":"drainage basin 是双词技术复合词，两个成分都经法语进入英语，因此显示出双重借入。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin element is obscured: baccinum is a reconstructed Vulgar Latin vessel word, possibly of Gaulish origin, and drainer has no Latin root at all.","cn":"这里的拉丁成分并不显眼：baccinum 是重构的通俗拉丁语「容器」词，可能源自高卢语，而 drainer 完全没有拉丁词根。"},"items":[{"word":"drain","structure":"drain (Old French drainer, to drain; deeper origin uncertain)","meaning":"to remove surplus water","meaningCN":"排除多余的水","example":"The field drains into the ditch.","exampleCN":"这块田的水排入沟里。"},{"word":"drainage","structure":"drain + -age (process or system)","meaning":"the system by which water is removed","meaningCN":"排除水的系统","example":"Drainage ditches criss-cross the plain.","exampleCN":"排水沟纵横交错于平原上。"},{"word":"basin","structure":"basin (Old French bacin, from Vulgar Latin *baccinum, vessel)","meaning":"a bowl; a low area collecting water","meaningCN":"盆；汇水的低地","example":"The basin filled with rain.","exampleCN":"盆里积满了雨。"},{"word":"drainage basin","structure":"drainage + basin","meaning":"the land drained by one river system","meaningCN":"由同一河系排水的陆地","example":"The drainage basin ends at the river mouth.","exampleCN":"流域在河口结束。"},{"word":"catchment","structure":"catch + -ment (that which is caught)","meaning":"the area catching rain for a river","meaningCN":"为一条河收集雨水的区域","example":"The catchment supplies the city.","exampleCN":"这个集水区供给这座城市。"},{"word":"watershed","structure":"water + shed (a divide)","meaning":"a dividing ridge; in American use, a basin","meaningCN":"分水岭；美式用法中也可指流域","example":"The watershed marks the border of two basins.","exampleCN":"这条分水岭标出两个流域的边界。"},{"word":"divide","structure":"divide (Latin dividere, to separate, through French)","meaning":"the high ground between basins","meaningCN":"流域之间的高地","example":"Rain on the divide goes both ways.","exampleCN":"分水岭上的雨会向两边流。"},{"word":"tributary","structure":"tribut- (Latin tribuere, to assign) + -ary","meaning":"a stream feeding a larger river","meaningCN":"汇入大河的溪流","example":"A tributary joins the main river here.","exampleCN":"一条支流在此汇入主河。"},{"word":"subbasin","structure":"sub- (under, secondary) + basin","meaning":"a basin nested inside a larger one","meaningCN":"嵌套在大流域内的小流域","example":"The subbasin has its own gauges.","exampleCN":"这个子流域有自己的测站。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"baccinum","structure":"baccinum (reconstructed Vulgar Latin, water vessel, possibly Gaulish)","meaning":"a water vessel or bowl","meaningCN":"水器；盆"}]}},{"word":"water reservoir","ipa_uk":"/ˈwɔːtə ˈrez.ə.vwɑː/","ipa_us":"/ˈwɔːtər ˈrez.ɚ.vwɑːr/","definition_zh":"水库；人工蓄水的水体或设施；也指储水容器","definition_en":"an artificial lake or storage facility built to hold water for supply, irrigation or power","core_image":"山口一道坝把河水拦住，水面在山谷里铺开，淹没线在两岸留下清晰的痕迹","scene":"山口的坝把河水拦住，库面在山谷里铺开，岸边露出旧道路的痕迹。A dam at the valley mouth turned the river into a large water reservoir.","sceneCN":"这里 water reservoir 指「为供水、灌溉或发电而建的人工蓄水体」（第 1 个义项：由坝拦蓄形成、可调节水量的水库）；句意为山口的大坝把河流变成一座大型水库。可辨识物件：大坝、库面、淹没线、旧路痕迹。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"水库；蓄水池（人工水体）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"储水容器；水箱"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"water reservoir capacity","zh":"水库库容"},{"phrase":"drinking water reservoir","zh":"饮用水水库"},{"phrase":"water reservoir management","zh":"水库调度管理"},{"phrase":"underground water reservoir","zh":"地下水库"},{"phrase":"water reservoir level","zh":"水库水位"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"water reservoir"},{"label":"复数","form":"water reservoirs"},{"label":"简称","form":"reservoir"},{"label":"同义说法（人工湖）","form":"artificial lake"},{"label":"相关设施（坝）","form":"dam"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"reservoir","pos":"n.","zh":"水库；储库；储备"},{"word":"water-reservoir","pos":"adj.","zh":"水库的（作定语，罕用连字符）"},{"word":"reservoir-based","pos":"adj.","zh":"以水库为依托的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The artificial lake","titleCN":"人工湖：由坝拦蓄形成","definition":"a body of water stored behind a dam or other structure in a valley","definitionCN":"在谷地中由坝或其他结构拦蓄形成的水体","example":"The water reservoir behind the dam supplies three towns.","exampleCN":"坝后的水库供给三个城镇。","why":"The word names a store, not a flow: a river is turned into a place where water waits until it is needed.","whyCN":"这个词命名的是储库，而不是流动：河流被变成水可以等待、直到需要时才放出的地方。"},{"no":"02","title":"Capacity and regulation","titleCN":"库容与调节","definition":"the storage volume and the operating rule that shift water from wet to dry periods","definitionCN":"把水从丰水期转移到枯水期的蓄水容积与调度规则","example":"The reservoir stores winter rain for the summer harvest.","exampleCN":"水库把冬季的雨储存起来供夏季收获使用。","why":"A reservoir is useful because inflow and demand are out of step; storage is time moved from one season to another.","whyCN":"水库之所以有用，是因为来水与需求不同步；蓄存就是把时间从一个季节搬到另一个季节。"},{"no":"03","title":"A drinking-water source","titleCN":"饮用水水源","definition":"a protected impoundment from which treated water is drawn for cities","definitionCN":"受保护、为城市取水并处理的人工蓄水体","example":"The city's drinking water comes from a mountain reservoir.","exampleCN":"这座城市的饮用水来自一座山区水库。","why":"Storing water also settles sediment and evens out quality, so a reservoir is a treatment step as much as a supply.","whyCN":"蓄水同时让泥沙沉降、使水质更稳定，因此水库既是供水设施，也是一道处理环节。"},{"no":"04","title":"Irrigation and hydropower","titleCN":"灌溉与发电的调节池","definition":"an impoundment that guarantees water or head for farms and turbines","definitionCN":"为农田或水轮机保证水量或水头的人工蓄水体","example":"The reservoir releases water for the rice fields in May.","exampleCN":"水库在五月放水给稻田。","why":"Both uses need a steady supply that nature does not provide, and a reservoir converts an irregular river into a scheduled one.","whyCN":"这两种用途都需要自然无法提供的稳定供给，水库把不规则的河流变成按时刻表运行的河流。"},{"no":"05","title":"Sediment and ecology","titleCN":"泥沙与生态影响","definition":"the reservoir as a trap for sediment and a changed habitat behind the dam","definitionCN":"作为泥沙陷阱、并改变坝后生境的水库","example":"The reservoir trapped silt that once reached the delta.","exampleCN":"水库拦住了原本到达三角洲的泥沙。","why":"Slow water drops its load, so every reservoir necessarily fills with sediment and starves the downstream channel.","whyCN":"流速变慢便卸下负载，因此每座水库都必然淤积，同时也让下游河道失去泥沙来源。"},{"no":"06","title":"The container sense","titleCN":"容器义：储水罐","definition":"a tank or vessel that holds water in a building or machine","definitionCN":"建筑物或机器中储存水的罐或容器","example":"A water reservoir on the roof feeds the upper floors.","exampleCN":"屋顶的储水罐为上几层供水。","why":"The same word covers the small version: anything that holds water for later use is a reservoir, whatever its size.","whyCN":"同一个词也涵盖小型版本：任何为日后使用而存水的器物都是 reservoir，无论大小。"},{"no":"07","title":"Abstract: a reserve of anything","titleCN":"比喻：任何事物的储备","definition":"a stock of people, skills or goodwill held back for future need","definitionCN":"为未来需要而保有的人才、技能或善意存量","example":"The scholarship fund is a reservoir of talent for the region.","exampleCN":"这项奖学金基金是该地区的人才储备。","why":"A reservoir is defined by holding something back, and that structure can be borrowed by any resource that is stored rather than spent.","whyCN":"水库的定义特征是「把东西留住」，这种结构可被任何储存而非消耗的资源借用。"},{"no":"08","title":"A body's water store","titleCN":"生物体内的储水结构","definition":"an organ or tissue in an organism that holds water or fluid","definitionCN":"生物体内储存水或液体的器官或组织","example":"The cactus uses its stem as a water reservoir.","exampleCN":"仙人掌把茎当作储水结构。","why":"Life solves the same problem as engineering: keep water where it will not evaporate, then draw on it slowly.","whyCN":"生命与工程解决同一个问题：把水存在不会蒸发的地方，然后慢慢取用。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Water reservoir is a hybrid: a native English noun plus a French noun that goes back to Latin reservare. Dates are approximate.","cn":"water reservoir 是混合词：本族英语名词加上可上溯到拉丁语 reservare 的法语名词。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"OLD ENGLISH WÆTER","en":"Wæter continues Proto-Germanic *watōr and belongs to the same Indo-European family as Greek hydōr.","cn":"wæter 延续原始日耳曼语 *watōr，与希腊语 hydōr 同属一个印欧词族。"},{"era":"FRENCH RÉSERVOIR","en":"French réservoir first meant a place where something is kept back, then a store of water; English borrowed it in the seventeenth century.","cn":"法语 réservoir 最初指把某物留住的地方，后指储水之处；英语在十七世纪借入。"},{"era":"LATIN RESERVARE","en":"Reservare meant to keep back or preserve, built from re-, back, and servare, to keep or guard.","cn":"reservare 意为留住、保存，由 re-「向后」与 servare「保存、守护」构成。"},{"era":"ENGINEERING SENSE","en":"The large artificial lake sense became standard in the nineteenth century with the growth of dam building for cities and industry.","cn":"随着为城市与工业建坝的增多，大型人工湖这一义项在十九世纪成为标准用法。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first date of the engineering sense): dictionaries give only approximate dates for the shift from 'store' to 'impounded lake'.","cn":"来源不确定（工程义首见年代）：辞书对从「储库」到「拦蓄湖泊」的转变只给出约数。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group holds look-alike phrases for storage facilities; the second holds water bodies that are close but not built stores.","cn":"第一组是形近的储水设施短语；第二组是相近但并非人工储库的水体。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"reservoir","ipa":"/ˈrez.ə.vwɑː/","tag":"the short form","definition":"The single word, which also covers oil reservoirs, reserves of talent and host populations.","definitionCN":"单词形式，也涵盖油藏、人才储备与宿主群体。"},{"word":"water tank","ipa":"/ˈwɔːtə tæŋk/","tag":"small container","definition":"An enclosed container of water, usually small and built rather than impounded.","definitionCN":"封闭的储水容器，通常较小且为制造物，而非拦蓄形成。"},{"word":"water tower","ipa":"/ˈwɔːtə ˌtaʊə/","tag":"elevated store","definition":"A raised tank whose height supplies pressure; the point is the head, not the volume.","definitionCN":"以高度提供压力的架高水罐；重点在水头，不在容积。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"lake","ipa":"/leɪk/","tag":"natural counterpart","definition":"A natural standing body of water; a reservoir is made, and its level is controlled.","definitionCN":"天然静水体；水库是人工的，且水位受控。"},{"word":"pond","ipa":"/pɒnd/","tag":"small still water","definition":"A small body of still water, usually shallow and not managed for supply.","definitionCN":"小型静水体，通常较浅，也不为供水而调度。"},{"word":"aquifer","ipa":"/ˈæk.wɪ.fə/","tag":"underground store","definition":"A rock layer that stores groundwater; the store is natural and invisible.","definitionCN":"储存地下水的岩层；储库是天然且看不见的。"},{"word":"cistern","ipa":"/ˈsɪs.tən/","tag":"rainwater container","definition":"A tank for catching and storing rainwater, usually at a building.","definitionCN":"收集并储存雨水的容器，通常位于建筑物处。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: the French word for keeping back, the dam image, and the real contrast with a natural lake.","cn":"正常联想：法语中「留住」的词、大坝意象，以及与天然湖泊的真实区别。"},"normal":[{"en":"reservoir comes from French réserver, to keep back: a reservoir is water kept back.","cn":"reservoir 出自法语 réserver「留住」：水库就是把水留住。"},{"en":"The dam is the door and the valley is the room: together they make the store.","cn":"坝是门，谷地是房间：两者合起来就是储库。"},{"en":"A lake is found; a reservoir is built and its level is managed.","cn":"湖泊是找到的，水库是建成的，而且水位受调度。"},{"en":"Slow water drops its sediment, so every reservoir silts up over time.","cn":"流速变慢便卸下泥沙，所以每座水库都会逐渐淤积。"},{"en":"The same word covers a rooftop tank, because both hold water for later.","cn":"同一个词也指屋顶水箱，因为两者都为日后存水。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Abstractly, a reservoir is time made spatial: water from one season is placed where another season can reach it.","cn":"抽象地看，水库是被空间化的时间：一个季节的水被放到另一个季节够得着的地方。"},{"en":"It is a deliberate delay, and every delay has a cost: silt, drowned land, displaced people.","cn":"它是有意的延迟，而每种延迟都有代价：淤积、被淹的土地、被迁移的人。"},{"en":"Any reserve — talent, trust, capital — works the same way and silts up in the same way if unused or misused.","cn":"任何储备——人才、信任、资本——都同样运作，若闲置或用错也会同样「淤积」。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The water reservoir was built to carry the city through two dry years.","cn":"这座水库是为让城市度过两个干旱年份而建的。"},{"en":"Sediment has reduced the water reservoir's capacity by a quarter.","cn":"泥沙已使这座水库的库容减少了四分之一。"},{"en":"A small water reservoir on the roof keeps pressure steady on the top floor.","cn":"屋顶的小储水罐让顶层的压力保持稳定。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「水（water）+ 留住（reservoir）」——把水留在大坝后面 → 水库","word":"water reservoir"},"root":"古英语 wæter「水」+ 法语 réservoir（上溯拉丁语 reservare「留住」，re- + servare「保存」）。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one store: the artificial lake, its capacity, its use for drinking water, its role in irrigation and power, its sediment and ecology, the small container, the abstract reserve, and the water store inside a living body.","cn":"八个义项围绕同一处储库展开：人工湖、库容、饮用水用途、灌溉与发电中的作用、泥沙与生态影响、小型容器、抽象储备，以及生物体内的储水结构。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a dam closing a valley, water spreading flat behind it, an old road disappearing under the surface.","cn":"核心意象：一道坝封住谷口，水在坝后摊平，一条旧路没入水面。"},"chain":["VALLEY","DAM","IMPOUNDED WATER","CAPACITY","RELEASE","DOWNSTREAM"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S2","en":"STORE AND SCHEDULE: the lake holds water, and the rule decides when it leaves.","cn":"储存与调度：湖把水存住，规则决定它何时离开。"},{"senses":"S3 · S4","en":"TWO DEMANDS: cities need clean water, farms and turbines need guaranteed flow.","cn":"两种需求：城市要干净的水，农田与水轮机要保证的流量。"},{"senses":"S5","en":"SIDE EFFECT: still water traps sediment and rewrites the habitat.","cn":"副作用：静水拦住泥沙，也改写了生境。"},{"senses":"S6","en":"SCALE DOWN: the same word serves a tank on a roof.","cn":"缩小尺度：同一个词也用于屋顶水箱。"},{"senses":"S7 · S8","en":"RESERVE AND BODY: anything held back is a reservoir, including water inside a plant.","cn":"储备与身体：任何被留住的东西都是储库，包括植物体内的水。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Water reservoir combines a native noun with a French borrowing, and the second member brings the whole Latin family of reservare.","cn":"water reservoir 把一个本族名词与一个法语借词组合起来，第二个成分带来了 reservare 的整个拉丁词族。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin base is reservare, from re- back and servare to keep or guard. Reserve, reservation, reserved and preserve all belong to this family.","cn":"拉丁语基础是 reservare，由 re-「向后」与 servare「保存、守护」构成。reserve、reservation、reserved 与 preserve 都属于这个词族。"},"items":[{"word":"reserve","structure":"re- (back) + servare (to keep) + -e (verb and noun)","meaning":"to keep back for later use","meaningCN":"留待日后使用","example":"They reserved two seats.","exampleCN":"他们留了两个座位。"},{"word":"reservation","structure":"reserve + -ation (action or result)","meaning":"an arrangement kept back for someone","meaningCN":"为某人预留的安排","example":"The reservation is for eight o'clock.","exampleCN":"预订是八点的。"},{"word":"reserved","structure":"reserve + -ed (having the quality)","meaning":"kept for a purpose; also holding back in manner","meaningCN":"预留给某用途的；也指态度含蓄的","example":"These seats are reserved.","exampleCN":"这些座位是预留的。"},{"word":"reservoir","structure":"French réservoir, from réserver (Latin reservare)","meaning":"a place or thing that stores something","meaningCN":"储存某物的地方或器物","example":"The reservoir supplies the valley.","exampleCN":"水库供给这个谷地。"},{"word":"preserve","structure":"pre- (before, in advance) + servare (to keep)","meaning":"to keep safe from harm or change","meaningCN":"保护以免受损或改变","example":"The trust preserves the old documents.","exampleCN":"这家信托机构保存旧文件。"},{"word":"conservation","structure":"con- (together) + servare + -ation","meaning":"careful keeping of a resource","meaningCN":"对资源的谨慎保存","example":"Water conservation begins with fixing leaks.","exampleCN":"节水从修好漏水开始。"},{"word":"observation","structure":"ob- (toward) + servare + -ation","meaning":"watching while keeping attention","meaningCN":"持续留意地观看","example":"The observation was recorded hourly.","exampleCN":"这次观测每小时记录一次。"},{"word":"dam","structure":"dam (Middle English, of uncertain origin)","meaning":"a barrier built to hold back water","meaningCN":"为拦住水而建的屏障","example":"The dam created the reservoir.","exampleCN":"大坝形成了这座水库。"},{"word":"impoundment","structure":"im- (in) + pound (to enclose) + -ment","meaning":"the water body created by damming","meaningCN":"由筑坝拦蓄形成的水体","example":"The impoundment flooded the old road.","exampleCN":"拦蓄的水淹没了旧路。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"reservare","structure":"re- (back) + servare (Latin verb, to keep)","meaning":"to keep back, to preserve","meaningCN":"留住；保存"},{"word":"servare","structure":"servare (Latin verb, to keep, guard, preserve)","meaning":"to keep, to guard","meaningCN":"保存；守护"},{"word":"reservatus","structure":"reservare + -tus (Latin past participle)","meaning":"kept back","meaningCN":"被留住的"}]}},{"word":"reservoir","ipa_uk":"/ˈrez.ə.vwɑː/","ipa_us":"/ˈrez.ɚ.vwɑːr/","definition_zh":"水库；储库；储液罐；油藏；储备；储存宿主；数据存储区","definition_en":"a store of water or another substance, natural or built, kept for later use","core_image":"大坝后面的静水面铺满谷地，取水塔与浮标立在水上，远处是一圈淹没线","scene":"山间大坝后面，水面铺满整个谷底，取水塔立在平静的水中。Behind the dam, a reservoir covers the whole valley floor.","sceneCN":"这里 reservoir 指「由坝拦蓄、为日后取用而储存大量水的人工水体」（第 1 个义项：可调节放水的水库）；句意为坝后的水库覆盖了整个谷底。可辨识物件：坝体、取水塔、浮标、淹没线、静水面。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"水库；蓄水池；储库"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"储液罐；（油）储层"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"储备；储存宿主；存储区"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"oil reservoir","zh":"油藏；储油层"},{"phrase":"reservoir of talent","zh":"人才储备"},{"phrase":"reservoir host","zh":"储存宿主"},{"phrase":"reservoir capacity","zh":"库容；储层容量"},{"phrase":"reservoir pressure","zh":"储层压力"},{"phrase":"reservoir of infection","zh":"感染储存源"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数","form":"reservoir"},{"label":"复数","form":"reservoirs"},{"label":"相关动词","form":"reserve"},{"label":"相关名词（预留）","form":"reservation"},{"label":"相关形容词","form":"reserved"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"reserve","pos":"v./n.","zh":"预留；储备；保护区"},{"word":"reservation","pos":"n.","zh":"预订；保留意见"},{"word":"reserved","pos":"adj.","zh":"预留的；含蓄的"},{"word":"reservoired","pos":"adj.","zh":"储集于储层的（石油地质用语）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The water store behind a dam","titleCN":"坝后的水库","definition":"an artificial lake formed by damming a valley to hold water","definitionCN":"在谷地筑坝拦水形成的人工湖","example":"The reservoir behind the dam supplies the whole plain.","exampleCN":"坝后的水库供给整个平原。","why":"The core sense is a place where water waits: an impoundment converts a flowing river into stored volume.","whyCN":"核心义是水等待的地方：拦蓄把流动的河变成储存的水量。"},{"no":"02","title":"A container of liquid","titleCN":"储液容器","definition":"a tank, chamber or vessel that holds a fluid for later use","definitionCN":"为日后使用而储存流体的罐、腔或容器","example":"The brake reservoir was almost empty.","exampleCN":"刹车油壶几乎空了。","why":"Scale does not change the structure: whether the store is a valley or a plastic bottle, the function is to hold and release.","whyCN":"尺度不改变结构：无论储库是谷地还是塑料瓶，功能都是存住并释放。"},{"no":"03","title":"An oil or gas reservoir","titleCN":"油藏；储层","definition":"a porous rock formation containing recoverable oil or gas","definitionCN":"含有可采石油或天然气的多孔岩层","example":"The field's reservoir lies in fractured limestone.","exampleCN":"这个油田的储层位于裂隙灰岩中。","why":"Petroleum geology reused the water term because the geometry is identical: fluid held in the pores of rock until a well releases it.","whyCN":"石油地质沿用这个水词，因为几何关系完全相同：流体存于岩石孔隙，直到井把它释放。"},{"no":"04","title":"A reserve of people or qualities","titleCN":"人才或品质的储备","definition":"a stock of skills, talent or goodwill available when needed","definitionCN":"需要时可取用的技能、人才或善意存量","example":"The university is a reservoir of expertise for the region.","exampleCN":"这所大学是该地区的专业人才储备。","why":"Anything held back rather than spent behaves like stored water, and the word transfers without effort.","whyCN":"任何留而不用的东西都像存住的水，这个词因此毫不费力地迁移过去。"},{"no":"05","title":"The reservoir host","titleCN":"储存宿主","definition":"an animal or environment in which a pathogen persists and from which it can spread","definitionCN":"病原体在其中持续存在、并可向外传播的动物或环境","example":"Bats are a natural reservoir for several viruses.","exampleCN":"蝙蝠是几种病毒的天然储存宿主。","why":"Epidemiology needs a word for the place where a disease waits between outbreaks, and that is exactly the reservoir image.","whyCN":"流行病学需要一个词来指疾病在两次暴发之间等待的地方，而这正是储库的意象。"},{"no":"06","title":"A computer storage area","titleCN":"数据存储区","definition":"a region of memory or storage set aside for a particular kind of data","definitionCN":"为某类数据专门留出的内存或存储区域","example":"The parser writes into a temporary reservoir of tokens.","exampleCN":"解析器把词元写入一个临时存储区。","why":"Computing borrows the word for capacity set aside and read later, which is the same hold-and-release pattern.","whyCN":"计算机领域借用这个词指预留、日后再读的容量，仍是同一套「存住再释放」的模式。"},{"no":"07","title":"An equalising basin","titleCN":"调节池：让流量变稳","definition":"a basin that absorbs surges so that downstream flow or supply stays steady","definitionCN":"吸收流量波动，使下游流量或供给保持稳定的水池","example":"The service reservoir smooths demand between morning and evening.","exampleCN":"调节水库把早晚之间的用水波动抹平。","why":"The purpose here is not total volume but timing: the store is a buffer against peaks.","whyCN":"这里的目的不是总水量，而是时序：储库是对峰值的缓冲。"},{"no":"08","title":"An ecological pool","titleCN":"生态储库：物质的驻留处","definition":"a component of an ecosystem in which a substance is stored longer than in others","definitionCN":"生态系统中某物质停留时间比在其他组分更长的部分","example":"Soil is the largest carbon reservoir on land.","exampleCN":"土壤是陆地上最大的碳储库。","why":"Biogeochemistry speaks of pools and fluxes, and the reservoir is simply the pool with a long residence time.","whyCN":"生物地球化学讲「库」与「通量」，而储库就是停留时间较长的那个库。"},{"no":"09","title":"Abstract: pent-up feeling","titleCN":"比喻：积存的情绪","definition":"a quantity of unexpressed feeling or tension that may be released at once","definitionCN":"未表达的情绪或张力积存起来，可能一次释放","example":"The reservoir of anger behind the calm voice was obvious.","exampleCN":"平静语气背后的那一片怒气很明显。","why":"The metaphor keeps the pressure: water held behind a barrier accumulates force, and so does feeling held too long.","whyCN":"这个比喻保留了压力：被屏障拦住的水会积聚力量，压抑过久的情绪也是如此。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Reservoir is a French noun built on réserver, from Latin reservare, to keep back. English took it in the seventeenth century and extended it to oil, data and hosts. Dates are approximate.","cn":"reservoir 是建立在法语 réserver 之上的名词，再上溯拉丁语 reservare「留住」。英语在十七世纪借入，后来扩展到油藏、数据与宿主。年代为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"FRENCH RÉSERVER","en":"Old French reserver meant to keep back or hold for a purpose, and French réservoir named the place where the kept thing stays.","cn":"古法语 reserver 意为留住或为某目的保留，法语 réservoir 指被留住之物所在的地方。"},{"era":"LATIN RESERVARE","en":"Reservare combined re-, back, with servare, to keep or guard; the participle reservatus gives English reserved.","cn":"reservare 由 re-「向后」与 servare「保存、守护」组合；分词 reservatus 给出英语 reserved。"},{"era":"SEVENTEENTH CENTURY ENGLISH","en":"English reservoir first named a place where water or another liquid is stored, including natural stores and containers.","cn":"英语 reservoir 最初指储存水或其他液体的地方，包括天然储库与容器。"},{"era":"THE ENGINEERING AND INDUSTRIAL SENSES","en":"Dam building in the nineteenth century gave the word its large artificial lake sense, and petroleum geology later reused it for rock formations holding oil.","cn":"十九世纪的筑坝工程赋予这个词大型人工湖义，石油地质后来又用它指储存石油的岩层。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (first dates of the extended senses): standard dictionaries give only approximate dates for the oil, data and ecological uses, and the exact sequence is not documented.","cn":"来源不确定（扩展义首见年代）：通行辞书对石油、数据与生态用法只给约数，确切先后未见记载。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group holds words that look close in form; the second holds stores and supplies that overlap in meaning.","cn":"第一组是词形相近的词；第二组是含义交叠的储库与供给概念。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"reserve","ipa":"/rɪˈzɜːv/","tag":"one letter shorter","definition":"The verb and noun meaning to keep back, or the stock itself; it lacks the -oir ending.","definitionCN":"表示留住的动词与名词，或指存量本身；没有 -oir 词尾。"},{"word":"reservation","ipa":"/ˌrez.əˈveɪ.ʃən/","tag":"the arrangement","definition":"A booking or a doubt held back; it is an abstract arrangement, not a place.","definitionCN":"预订或保留意见；是抽象安排，不是场所。"},{"word":"reservist","ipa":"/rɪˈzɜː.vɪst/","tag":"person, not place","definition":"A member of a military reserve force; the ending -ist marks a person.","definitionCN":"预备役军人；词尾 -ist 表示人。"},{"word":"reservoir","ipa":"/ˈrez.ə.vwɑː/","tag":"headword","definition":"The noun ending in -oir, borrowed whole from French with a characteristic silent final r.","definitionCN":"以 -oir 结尾的名词，整体借自法语，词尾的 r 常不发音。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"stock","ipa":"/stɒk/","tag":"general store","definition":"A supply kept for use; it can be of anything, while a reservoir usually holds something fluid or spatial.","definitionCN":"为使用而保有的供给；可指任何事物，而 reservoir 通常指流体或空间上的储库。"},{"word":"aquifer","ipa":"/ˈæk.wɪ.fə/","tag":"natural rock store","definition":"A permeable rock layer holding groundwater, a natural reservoir in rock.","definitionCN":"储存地下水的透水岩层，是岩石中的天然储库。"},{"word":"lake","ipa":"/leɪk/","tag":"natural water body","definition":"A natural standing body of water; a reservoir is made and regulated.","definitionCN":"天然静水体；水库是人工的、受调度的。"},{"word":"tank","ipa":"/tæŋk/","tag":"manufactured container","definition":"A container for liquid, usually small and made; a reservoir may be built into the ground.","definitionCN":"储液容器，通常较小且为制造物；reservoir 可以建在地下。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: the French -oir ending, the re- plus servare structure, and the fields that borrowed the word.","cn":"正常联想：法语 -oir 词尾、re- 加 servare 的结构，以及借用这个词的领域。"},"normal":[{"en":"reservoir is French for 'the place that keeps back', from réserver.","cn":"reservoir 在法语中就是「把东西留住的地方」，出自 réserver。"},{"en":"re- is back and servare is keep, so reservare is 'keep back' and reserve is its verb.","cn":"re- 是向后，servare 是保存，所以 reservare 就是「留住」，动词是 reserve。"},{"en":"The word spreads by shape: water behind a dam, oil in rock, data in memory.","cn":"这个词按结构扩散：坝后的水、岩层中的油、内存中的数据。"},{"en":"The -oir ending is French, like memoir and boudoir, and the final r is often silent.","cn":"-oir 是法语词尾，如 memoir 与 boudoir，词末的 r 常不发音。"},{"en":"A reservoir host is where a disease waits between outbreaks.","cn":"储存宿主就是疾病在两次暴发之间等待的地方。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Abstractly, a reservoir is stored time under pressure: what is held can be released later, and holding builds force.","cn":"抽象地看，储库是受压的储存时间：存住的东西可以稍后释放，而存住本身会积聚力量。"},{"en":"Every reservoir has a dam, and every dam has a cost: something is drowned so that something else stays dry.","cn":"每个储库都有一道坝，每道坝都有代价：淹掉一处，才让另一处保持干燥。"},{"en":"The same word for water, oil, data and anger shows that storage, not substance, is what it names.","cn":"同一个词用于水、油、数据与怒气，说明它命名的不是物质，而是「储存」。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The reservoir holds enough water for eighteen months of normal demand.","cn":"这座水库储存的水够十八个月正常需求。"},{"en":"Pressure in the reservoir drives the oil up the well.","cn":"储层中的压力把石油沿井筒顶上来。"},{"en":"Rodents can act as a reservoir for the bacteria that cause the fever.","cn":"啮齿动物可以成为引起这种发热的细菌的储存宿主。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"「瑞泽沃（reservoir）」——把水留在谷地里「瑞泽」一片 → 水库、储库","word":"reservoir"},"root":"法语 réservoir「留住东西的地方」，上溯拉丁语 reservare（re-「向后」+ servare「保存、守护」）。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses follow one act of keeping back: the lake behind a dam, the tank, the oil formation, the reserve of people, the host that harbours a pathogen, the data area, the equalising basin, the ecological pool, and finally pent-up feeling.","cn":"九个义项围绕同一个「留住」的动作展开：坝后的湖、储液罐、油藏、人才储备、藏病原的宿主、数据区、调节池、生态储库，最后是积压的情绪。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a still sheet of water filling a valley behind a dam, with a intake tower standing in it.","cn":"核心意象：坝后铺满谷底的静水，取水塔立在水面。"},"chain":["INFLOW","BARRIER","STORED VOLUME","PRESSURE","RELEASE","USE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S2","en":"WATER AT TWO SCALES: a valley impoundment and a tank are the same structure at different sizes.","cn":"两种尺度的水：谷地拦蓄与储液罐是同一结构的不同尺寸。"},{"senses":"S3","en":"ROCK AS CONTAINER: petroleum geology reuses the water geometry for oil in pores.","cn":"岩石即容器：石油地质把水的几何关系套用到孔隙中的油。"},{"senses":"S4 · S5","en":"HOLDING SOMETHING ALIVE: talent is stored, and so is a pathogen between outbreaks.","cn":"留住活的东西：人才被储存，病原体也在两次暴发之间被储存。"},{"senses":"S6 · S7","en":"CAPACITY SET ASIDE: memory and service basins both reserve room for later demand.","cn":"预留的容量：内存与调节池都为日后的需求留出空间。"},{"senses":"S8 · S9","en":"RESIDENCE AND PRESSURE: a pool holds a substance longer, and held feeling builds force.","cn":"停留与压力：库让物质停留更久，而被压住的情绪会积聚力量。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Reservoir sits inside a Latin family that English knows well through reserve, reservation and preserve, so its structure is easy to see.","cn":"reservoir 属于一个英语很熟悉的拉丁词族，通过 reserve、reservation 与 preserve 可以清楚看出它的结构。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin verb is reservare, re- back plus servare to keep. Servare also builds preserve, conserve and observe; the noun suffix -oir is French, not Latin.","cn":"拉丁动词是 reservare，即 re-「向后」加 servare「保存」。servare 也构成 preserve、conserve 与 observe；名词词尾 -oir 属法语，并非拉丁语。"},"items":[{"word":"reserve","structure":"re- (back) + servare (to keep)","meaning":"to keep back for later","meaningCN":"留待日后","example":"Reserve a seat for me.","exampleCN":"给我留个座位。"},{"word":"reservation","structure":"reserve + -ation (action)","meaning":"something kept back for a person","meaningCN":"为某人预留的东西","example":"We have a reservation for two.","exampleCN":"我们订了两人位。"},{"word":"reservoir","structure":"French réservoir, from réserver (Latin reservare)","meaning":"a place or thing that stores","meaningCN":"储存某物的地方或器物","example":"The reservoir stores the winter rain.","exampleCN":"水库储存冬季的雨。"},{"word":"reservoired","structure":"reservoir + -ed (having, technical)","meaning":"held within a rock reservoir","meaningCN":"储集在岩层储库中的","example":"The oil is reservoired in sandstone.","exampleCN":"石油储集在砂岩中。"},{"word":"preserve","structure":"pre- (in advance) + servare","meaning":"to keep safe","meaningCN":"保护保存","example":"Preserve the samples in cold storage.","exampleCN":"把样品冷藏保存。"},{"word":"conserve","structure":"con- (together) + servare","meaning":"to keep from loss","meaningCN":"保存以免损失","example":"Conserve water in dry months.","exampleCN":"旱月要节约用水。"},{"word":"observe","structure":"ob- (toward) + servare","meaning":"to watch with attention","meaningCN":"专注地观察","example":"Observe the gauge twice a day.","exampleCN":"每天观察水位两次。"},{"word":"conservation","structure":"con- + servare + -ation","meaning":"the keeping of a resource","meaningCN":"对资源的保存","example":"Conservation saved the wetland.","exampleCN":"保护工作保住了这片湿地。"},{"word":"storage","structure":"store + -age (place or process)","meaning":"the keeping of something for later","meaningCN":"为日后保留某物","example":"Storage capacity is limited.","exampleCN":"储存容量有限。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"reservare","structure":"re- + servare (Latin verb)","meaning":"to keep back, to preserve","meaningCN":"留住；保存"},{"word":"servare","structure":"servare (Latin verb, to keep or guard)","meaning":"to keep, guard","meaningCN":"保存；守护"},{"word":"reservatus","structure":"reservare + -tus (past participle)","meaning":"kept back","meaningCN":"被留住的"}]}}]);
